Q6VXNlcjc3NjkxOTg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77691984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/harshit-wadhwani","html_url":"https://github.com/harshit-wadhwani","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/harshit-wadhwani/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/harshit-wadhwani/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/harshit-wadhwani/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/harshit-wadhwani/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/harshit-wadhwani/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/harshit-wadhwani/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/harshit-wadhwani/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/harshit-wadhwani/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/harshit-wadhwani/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1b270c86fe24381c28d3ed35a31d754bd58bbf6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1b270c86fe24381c28d3ed35a31d754bd58bbf6e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1b270c86fe24381c28d3ed35a31d754bd58bbf6e"}]},{"sha":"1b270c86fe24381c28d3ed35a31d754bd58bbf6e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDFiMjcwYzg2ZmUyNDM4MWMyOGQzZWQzNWEzMWQ3NTRiZDU4YmJmNmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T20:17:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T20:17:47Z"},"message":"fix(code): use SDK pin as effective editable version (#4949)\n\nEditable `deepagents-code` installs in the monorepo can run the SDK\nworkspace at HEAD even though the SDK's source version marker still\nnames the latest stable release and dcode's live `pyproject.toml` pins a\nnewer SDK alpha. `/version`, `/doctor`, and trace metadata previously\ntreated that normal checkout as an incompatible old SDK.\n\nDiagnostics now represent this specific checkout as an editable form of\nthe pinned published baseline. The user-facing and trace version gains a\nPEP 440 local suffix, while the raw source marker remains visible:\n\n```text\ndeepagents-code version: 0.1.45\ndeepagents (SDK) version: 0.7.0a8+editable (workspace HEAD; source marker: 0.6.12)\ndcode_client_deepagents_version: 0.7.0a8+editable\n```\n\nThe published `0.7.0a8` baseline is still used for SDK release-age\nchecks. For editable dcode installs, the requirement comes from the\ncheckout's current `pyproject.toml` rather than potentially stale\ninstalled metadata.\n\nThis inference is deliberately narrow: both packages must be editable\nsibling package roots in the same monorepo, the SDK source marker must\nbe parseable, the dcode requirement must be one exact pin, and that pin\nmust be newer than both observed SDK markers. Unrelated or genuinely\nstale editable SDK checkouts, ranged requirements, older or equal pins,\nand missing or malformed source markers keep the observed version and\nsurface a mismatch; `/doctor` also marks an invalid source marker\nunhealthy. PEP 610 paths are normalized so the sibling check behaves\nconsistently for Windows drive-path forms.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `python -m pytest libs/code/tests/unit_tests/test_extras_info.py\nlibs/code/tests/unit_tests/test_version.py\nlibs/code/tests/unit_tests/test_doctor.py\nlibs/code/tests/unit_tests/tui/test_textual_adapter.py` (424 passed)\n- `make -C libs/code lint_diff`\n- `make -C libs/code type`\n- `deepagents-code` pre-commit hooks\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"a7f64b1141c92b118bebe9635ae888cfedf5eb75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a7f64b1141c92b118bebe9635ae888cfedf5eb75"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/1b270c86fe24381c28d3ed35a31d754bd58bbf6e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYSVrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAi7sQAGzgFTfpQIDUE1lDu38oSCvC\nyCQdayzf1c7a2Y6vHr5WGv99x/aSApBfnFqmOlh+OadPX0dV0emyhYBfWc9RPACU\nKlFcZ0GQYoFUi2+W2vYwrBvjMexGycfO2ShjeGOyLT4bUTzjkpEYmbgGPGK32MYq\nDceWtJwxDX1nRkhsdf8E9Qi8vjoNnMwy2P0+msuLckUb6S/Iz+9b1pquKu+WipkD\nXwxATYDYiS2Wg84mHBJuurVLxOdFraqO3j8CKTtVv/5xHyLdjs7R63rRtCnQTJ1i\nhHKlq6p9VROgAnNF1Gn2/Fg3WzsMLvp6eUD9Edi8x6q2I7f1FNsJZG0fQ3YgZwRq\ndr11UYgqB0eDTjzNGkQV1GBB0R6POdVzLBiwWKE3xkr2OdBMduk47utBW45+0W6b\n2gTTPvpIsbQaxyuBAbhKEuk3Pvuq50oMYnyth1D9M+5zYRoML2u71sjEZ6kI83E8\n9P47MZkBxkeygdpmM+uGXRuv7aQI6yAVjWBSlIj8N2HjUdUgvvFplH0Of+tHz232\nJsSiErkv0EP+gvF4MQygkHk5rnpfzYU7zdnhBOEZ8JZz576Twfloy9PbXRNP7xIs\ns+EKTZDcw2kNR5hWr/ZzPpZ/Qh7Pu8k1qvCbUXLcgFxsmjt4QnmDr5EZbPdhN8Ks\nMD8j9atutkL57zt+xK24\n=6CDm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a7f64b1141c92b118bebe9635ae888cfedf5eb75\nparent 8b4e508d4664ef02e220854d50f5d98e0913aed8\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784751467 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784751467 -0400\n\nfix(code): use SDK pin as effective editable version (#4949)\n\nEditable `deepagents-code` installs in the monorepo can run the SDK\nworkspace at HEAD even though the SDK's source version marker still\nnames the latest stable release and dcode's live `pyproject.toml` pins a\nnewer SDK alpha. `/version`, `/doctor`, and trace metadata previously\ntreated that normal checkout as an incompatible old SDK.\n\nDiagnostics now represent this specific checkout as an editable form of\nthe pinned published baseline. The user-facing and trace version gains a\nPEP 440 local suffix, while the raw source marker remains visible:\n\n```text\ndeepagents-code version: 0.1.45\ndeepagents (SDK) version: 0.7.0a8+editable (workspace HEAD; source marker: 0.6.12)\ndcode_client_deepagents_version: 0.7.0a8+editable\n```\n\nThe published `0.7.0a8` baseline is still used for SDK release-age\nchecks. For editable dcode installs, the requirement comes from the\ncheckout's current `pyproject.toml` rather than potentially stale\ninstalled metadata.\n\nThis inference is deliberately narrow: both packages must be editable\nsibling package roots in the same monorepo, the SDK source marker must\nbe parseable, the dcode requirement must be one exact pin, and that pin\nmust be newer than both observed SDK markers. Unrelated or genuinely\nstale editable SDK checkouts, ranged requirements, older or equal pins,\nand missing or malformed source markers keep the observed version and\nsurface a mismatch; `/doctor` also marks an invalid source marker\nunhealthy. PEP 610 paths are normalized so the sibling check behaves\nconsistently for Windows drive-path forms.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `python -m pytest libs/code/tests/unit_tests/test_extras_info.py\nlibs/code/tests/unit_tests/test_version.py\nlibs/code/tests/unit_tests/test_doctor.py\nlibs/code/tests/unit_tests/tui/test_textual_adapter.py` (424 passed)\n- `make -C libs/code lint_diff`\n- `make -C libs/code type`\n- `deepagents-code` pre-commit hooks\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-07-22T20:17:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1b270c86fe24381c28d3ed35a31d754bd58bbf6e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1b270c86fe24381c28d3ed35a31d754bd58bbf6e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1b270c86fe24381c28d3ed35a31d754bd58bbf6e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8b4e508d4664ef02e220854d50f5d98e0913aed8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8b4e508d4664ef02e220854d50f5d98e0913aed8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8b4e508d4664ef02e220854d50f5d98e0913aed8"}]},{"sha":"8b4e508d4664ef02e220854d50f5d98e0913aed8","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhiNGU1MDhkNDY2NGVmMDJlMjIwODU0ZDUwZjVkOThlMDkxM2FlZDg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T20:10:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T20:10:01Z"},"message":"feat(code): add Hooks v2 capability snapshots (#4916)\n\nRelated DCD-70\n\nHooks v2 now validates and freezes configuration into deterministic\nsession snapshots backed by one authoritative event capability registry.\n\n---\n\nThis is 1/3 in the DCD-70 stack.\n\n- Defines event ownership, matching, timeout, output, and aggregation\ncapabilities.\n- Loads project and user configuration in stable precedence order with\nsemantic-only legacy migration.\n- Computes canonical snapshot hashes and rejects unsupported matcher or\nhandler combinations before execution.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `uv run --group test pytest tests/unit_tests/hooks` — 81 passed at\nthis stack layer\n- `make lint`\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- branch-stack-start -->\n\n-------------------------\n- main\n  - **johannes117/code/dcd-70-hooks-capabilities** 👈\n-\n[johannes117/code/dcd-70-hooks-execution](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/4917)\n-\n[johannes117/code/dcd-70-hooks-transcripts](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/4918)\n\n<sup>[Stack](https://www.git-town.com/how-to/proposal-breadcrumb.html)\ngenerated by [Git Town](https://github.com/git-town/git-town)</sup>\n\n<!-- branch-stack-end -->","tree":{"sha":"40268cbac2b829eedc7de5fd637958657004ee4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/40268cbac2b829eedc7de5fd637958657004ee4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8b4e508d4664ef02e220854d50f5d98e0913aed8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYSOZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAs+8QADBsVyuKuf2IJib/vpdiIVa9\nL5E8dSLiC6Q1tyhP6IpdMnA51nu5jAaEMLWL+SdjwOcEvXOm3egfdej2gcE9T4Gx\nx97zrCj1dXFDbaidrc62KeIKogOfMII0CTyats6r2EQanciu1AmqotyU/373mcBU\nf9lgeaXfgiRXhUqA+kte9zXXnYkGVyte1q3dRDoQaarZyIfxRbS2Hq+0rqMNHNOl\nfkW4N1a/YwQS/KgYaCe2Lab4F8qs7qolrpQBvbfBLOaCbUtzzF4IR0dG5hTH3uas\nfi/O7J7muE06HQ1MFpN/3PPr0fQ2INzksX5uXP5fdTISMVMQfFHF0TqQ57RMK/ko\nIhsjq/PNjy9a6FLqUaVl/ttmV4fqX7GXxDf/lYFAv9ZpWRXmfKL6T466DtWgNXyq\n+lye8jFSR5E2vtdwvtipTM3Y+WOhUIb+dzxD/MlVOF4GFLoTVSaLtBq92PTrTtr7\niV/kcue9tGjqZrNQVZk2jCN4qKz25ppqkv7hSSyv4frgxxpun+cabqhTVQbSnbw4\nQi8K2b112CHdQuvpUYr0MkB3Z1+5OUKjCWlnwiF93sr0dG/28QtflD4uwwK2bq6n\ntyRhFRrdz8yoeSA5bvRWqmqhZSKptYYrzia9Mdv+3shRa9ZVT1oKixH0TnQFCb7F\n9SKBW/N6b4JlCbVu/wpY\n=dAJz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 40268cbac2b829eedc7de5fd637958657004ee4e\nparent e6ab9c05e8fcb9a332396a9425e2b302607be823\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1784751001 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784751001 +0000\n\nfeat(code): add Hooks v2 capability snapshots (#4916)\n\nRelated DCD-70\n\nHooks v2 now validates and freezes configuration into deterministic\nsession snapshots backed by one authoritative event capability registry.\n\n---\n\nThis is 1/3 in the DCD-70 stack.\n\n- Defines event ownership, matching, timeout, output, and aggregation\ncapabilities.\n- Loads project and user configuration in stable precedence order with\nsemantic-only legacy migration.\n- Computes canonical snapshot hashes and rejects unsupported matcher or\nhandler combinations before execution.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `uv run --group test pytest tests/unit_tests/hooks` — 81 passed at\nthis stack layer\n- `make lint`\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- branch-stack-start -->\n\n-------------------------\n- main\n  - **johannes117/code/dcd-70-hooks-capabilities** 👈\n-\n[johannes117/code/dcd-70-hooks-execution](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/4917)\n-\n[johannes117/code/dcd-70-hooks-transcripts](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/4918)\n\n<sup>[Stack](https://www.git-town.com/how-to/proposal-breadcrumb.html)\ngenerated by [Git Town](https://github.com/git-town/git-town)</sup>\n\n<!-- branch-stack-end -->","verified_at":"2026-07-22T20:10:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8b4e508d4664ef02e220854d50f5d98e0913aed8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8b4e508d4664ef02e220854d50f5d98e0913aed8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8b4e508d4664ef02e220854d50f5d98e0913aed8/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e6ab9c05e8fcb9a332396a9425e2b302607be823","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e6ab9c05e8fcb9a332396a9425e2b302607be823","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e6ab9c05e8fcb9a332396a9425e2b302607be823"}]},{"sha":"e6ab9c05e8fcb9a332396a9425e2b302607be823","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGU2YWI5YzA1ZThmY2I5YTMzMjM5NmE5NDI1ZTJiMzAyNjA3YmU4MjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T19:58:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T19:58:00Z"},"message":"fix(code): abort YOLO launch on `Ctrl+C`/`Ctrl+D` (#4953)\n\nPressing Ctrl+C or Ctrl+D at the `dcode --yolo` acknowledgement prompt\nnow quits without launching the TUI, instead of silently dropping into\nManual mode and starting the session. Ctrl+D also aborts from the\ninteractive project MCP action picker, matching Escape and the existing\ncheckbox-picker behavior.\n\n---\n\nThe inline YOLO acknowledgement selector previously treated `Ctrl+C` as\ndeclining the warning, while `Ctrl+D` surfaced as EOF and was caught by\nthe same Manual fallback. Either input could therefore turn an explicit\n`--yolo` launch into a Manual session that still started.\n\n`Ctrl+C` and `Ctrl+D` now raise `KeyboardInterrupt` from the YOLO\nselector. The exception reaches the existing top-level handler in\n`cli_main`, which prints `Interrupted` and exits before Textual starts.\n`Escape` still selects Manual, matching the on-screen hint.\n\nThe project MCP action picker previously let `Ctrl+D` fall through to\nits text fallback, where EOF was treated as **Deny** and startup\ncontinued. Interactive `Ctrl+D` now returns the existing cancellation\noutcome and aborts startup. Non-interactive EOF still fails closed to\n**Deny**, so closed or piped stdin cannot grant project MCP trust.\n\nRegression coverage exercises the real prompt-toolkit key bindings and\nverifies that an interrupted YOLO acknowledgement never calls the\nTextual launcher.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/25afa87b-70d9-c9ed-3f4a-89f9cbefa8b9)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ee301fec84fd04bebd9343dbc04763dc938a689e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ee301fec84fd04bebd9343dbc04763dc938a689e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/e6ab9c05e8fcb9a332396a9425e2b302607be823","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYSDICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgqwQAKvlUrGx0sQ1wu2YOhtAaI4d\nYMYMoFBiIJm78ey05cAV5MsNAD4aXAcpcsFsUpiRVqQY0rrtmYKWOYvj0BgLaWSq\njrvb7kVoFItEf3ZwiJoa+vJmW7wEc8ljJN7pdQd94upmKsv6jQU87p0XTYVbRS6t\nzVPNa++vlOti3D2pM92P5n/tJZd7su5rIHKAEl38WeZJsOyfMjLoBXyQh7dYEOGz\nD6fHMZKNQ88WO1RofyZz28wGFUP5m/pQOcOfq/m8ndo7ICcekauKKjWtqKujsiyY\ntCluThrWPCJoWUZehvhRfZdW451wldKgEXsKrWCRqm0Fts0i1LzW+MN2/Ni2bSb1\n0BZ0mVTqyouFXagJCTHu2jIx6S468UFtevFY0vIF7hFNwOF/hkEDjfliyax6KsLJ\nN6PnpGfS5FQHIB8eNyuuvWtp8ye31tZq2uUkNGT+QED+K8XjcUgNCYwDJAD87zER\ngmHUzFWwI0Aw9ThAPMR1A0rcxTNitG/wvu+Nm6LDR6OkJYg6cYVoAT81RviDfg8o\nBhNQLOOAgkNL/xD9eBOA/ZTNBOTppQgsYpLNLbCuVsUI6ZD+HlIo30Hmw2DVxoTm\n9fUL+iFfLT3d/8vuTmSgleSUsp5KZ5hGr9CD0Zaok4gblMJ4jKgI2j2earTF4Bgn\n4J0PCdpX8uPQlGpQ2lEi\n=NXaA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ee301fec84fd04bebd9343dbc04763dc938a689e\nparent d029585ab79432d00edfa5a70e77a31f2388ed5b\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784750280 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784750280 -0400\n\nfix(code): abort YOLO launch on `Ctrl+C`/`Ctrl+D` (#4953)\n\nPressing Ctrl+C or Ctrl+D at the `dcode --yolo` acknowledgement prompt\nnow quits without launching the TUI, instead of silently dropping into\nManual mode and starting the session. Ctrl+D also aborts from the\ninteractive project MCP action picker, matching Escape and the existing\ncheckbox-picker behavior.\n\n---\n\nThe inline YOLO acknowledgement selector previously treated `Ctrl+C` as\ndeclining the warning, while `Ctrl+D` surfaced as EOF and was caught by\nthe same Manual fallback. Either input could therefore turn an explicit\n`--yolo` launch into a Manual session that still started.\n\n`Ctrl+C` and `Ctrl+D` now raise `KeyboardInterrupt` from the YOLO\nselector. The exception reaches the existing top-level handler in\n`cli_main`, which prints `Interrupted` and exits before Textual starts.\n`Escape` still selects Manual, matching the on-screen hint.\n\nThe project MCP action picker previously let `Ctrl+D` fall through to\nits text fallback, where EOF was treated as **Deny** and startup\ncontinued. Interactive `Ctrl+D` now returns the existing cancellation\noutcome and aborts startup. Non-interactive EOF still fails closed to\n**Deny**, so closed or piped stdin cannot grant project MCP trust.\n\nRegression coverage exercises the real prompt-toolkit key bindings and\nverifies that an interrupted YOLO acknowledgement never calls the\nTextual launcher.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/25afa87b-70d9-c9ed-3f4a-89f9cbefa8b9)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-22T19:58:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e6ab9c05e8fcb9a332396a9425e2b302607be823","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e6ab9c05e8fcb9a332396a9425e2b302607be823","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e6ab9c05e8fcb9a332396a9425e2b302607be823/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d029585ab79432d00edfa5a70e77a31f2388ed5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d029585ab79432d00edfa5a70e77a31f2388ed5b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d029585ab79432d00edfa5a70e77a31f2388ed5b"}]},{"sha":"d029585ab79432d00edfa5a70e77a31f2388ed5b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQwMjk1ODVhYjc5NDMyZDAwZWRmYTVhNzBlNzdhMzFmMjM4OGVkNWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T19:57:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T19:57:41Z"},"message":"fix(code): disable LangSmith secret redaction by default (#4970)\n\nWhen LangSmith tracing is active, dcode now leaves traces unredacted by\ndefault. Users can still opt in to secret redaction with\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_REDACT=true` or `[tracing] langsmith_redact =\ntrue`.\n\n---\n\nThis changes only the default: anonymizer setup and its fail-closed\nbehavior remain intact when redaction is requested.","tree":{"sha":"bc5f89562b2c3b1fe9ebb5b632f90268b964c8e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/bc5f89562b2c3b1fe9ebb5b632f90268b964c8e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d029585ab79432d00edfa5a70e77a31f2388ed5b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYSC1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4nUQAB3El/pFbfVZo7e+C2+o5gB4\n+Q5M6qY5SlZFlw+wo2zZpZRoztFrLrRDgLIVk1oipPX3m4+IWqpcYbOylG04dHt+\nUVo+NBWjo5DmCrzUGpJsl4xZRm5DzD4GLqxAmo1YdjFORIHzVfgWoVOosuVBvZBw\na2O2KOwCfnVq/4w1C4lJm0sNZqk7lt7JYEBsgsv2hf6dolruD5XX+S1H03pYk8qg\n7gjcjJzJU65O4bJaeaB6QqB8KiYz7c8zY7zenLrHBAdXIqG+hDZ/lKIL+f+7pzWE\niQaK4DCpwM7EocMEGGSCiHn+0Kb5W36nUjeBAVbTr8QOgSU0Ff6YcX7Ym764NolN\nCvMPWcZpuhG7wh6hMWgA5KJQfgTsjPIlPtWSL4/iInkvp5VhFdqUB/fBNM21V8PV\n4IS6Zo/crzGTVL8w5Om3os+FYp+vcEl6RPtdiMEIN3YbAagAWzBZ/gwHoibIZTjA\nCZLGDx4vM9VbIoMifWiX9UnXDt/sEwZ5yCrSM3S+k9ot9tMdoCsqbd6YZBojTE+a\niwskC/iKq96loOsFpFVJKGgnpW4HO1ofxa0AIjXbMZhMIiWbGj0xizBkMdVa3K6T\nb7HguDzkUrbjmarzIt4E6hsRhEVu6lW0o/579Falg0cNltUg5wWc11ANnF6dp6qv\nQYq1ZWYigVkghAAwkSBy\n=/gVP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bc5f89562b2c3b1fe9ebb5b632f90268b964c8e0\nparent bca70aa1f30ee1472809894e2474a76e4ff2f8bd\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784750261 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784750261 -0400\n\nfix(code): disable LangSmith secret redaction by default (#4970)\n\nWhen LangSmith tracing is active, dcode now leaves traces unredacted by\ndefault. Users can still opt in to secret redaction with\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_REDACT=true` or `[tracing] langsmith_redact =\ntrue`.\n\n---\n\nThis changes only the default: anonymizer setup and its fail-closed\nbehavior remain intact when redaction is requested.","verified_at":"2026-07-22T19:57:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d029585ab79432d00edfa5a70e77a31f2388ed5b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d029585ab79432d00edfa5a70e77a31f2388ed5b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d029585ab79432d00edfa5a70e77a31f2388ed5b/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bca70aa1f30ee1472809894e2474a76e4ff2f8bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bca70aa1f30ee1472809894e2474a76e4ff2f8bd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bca70aa1f30ee1472809894e2474a76e4ff2f8bd"}]},{"sha":"bca70aa1f30ee1472809894e2474a76e4ff2f8bd","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGJjYTcwYWExZjMwZWUxNDcyODA5ODk0ZTI0NzRhNzZlNGZmMmY4YmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T19:42:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T19:42:54Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): include HTTP status in rubric grader errors (#4967)\n\nRubric grader failures now include a direct provider exception's integer\nHTTP status when available, while preserving the existing explanation\nfor exceptions without one.\n\n---\n\nThis makes overloaded and gateway failures distinguishable in\nacceptance-criteria grading without coupling `RubricMiddleware` to a\nprovider SDK. Non-integer values are ignored, and grader retry and\nclassification behavior is unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"f98ea81b599c452300d072637f13aba3a57582b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f98ea81b599c452300d072637f13aba3a57582b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/bca70aa1f30ee1472809894e2474a76e4ff2f8bd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYR0+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKkkQAIljqD8/eEHMCqEk4/7SIFjw\n6PYkelHGwprCS/zpEymU1A43YmfRbP0QxlEjTCAWIHsr/W/7gCLzo35v0nM3gbj/\nNCESz1N8Nxe4EFwgkpoutOQiaagcYepAxI180j1fM6X55avyqzFLe2Vs88CvfHGj\nNFzkKAr10EO07lo+o1DAPU77/+cnmLuOT0dxBe0i5bPXg3jfq13zPf8P5045yCd+\nkBZLxpkDmxYgRjJg/D10VCE76XmzNhmad7FQFfx/SL247DQlt+XPJWgMFFcA1AYR\n5Xqv4yNYzdFr9iT2rhi26sQ/VdXpb3d39x2ssFY6ZhzRnw/lZ/pXk5owwjNl06B7\nKfJ4WUnOaZwviYSaU80xfTAI5Hud3SaMWMYkyeRogByHqOL3svMzh5aQlnK6wN7A\nN66ye67WgDmge3fAmeJS7XZqnDVEjnLe95e0vBa4e9vzZdzH3O/nni4J2wVMMMr0\nYq2Vr0vsff2/DbIlnvBmjNG+8fF2lYCsmg5OUB6x6sm+Q+yVuCG/5ZZ5JTK5Rqca\nlmNWYd2vtA7j+ikluL78ynCTQeEFNSkpMI98mPPt3fQywn3PNf74Q/Hbo2aoc3Sc\nm+HQ8W7ZULns3qT3g9cJ3C90NXtebvc3VnIdZTm42jCKCQH7xay+Jc+n2ZiD39As\nliykEEDqNxH/tsU8EXB8\n=L5Oc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f98ea81b599c452300d072637f13aba3a57582b7\nparent 19e4805dc2c4514e733e263ab9e24a3cca4885dd\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784749374 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784749374 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): include HTTP status in rubric grader errors (#4967)\n\nRubric grader failures now include a direct provider exception's integer\nHTTP status when available, while preserving the existing explanation\nfor exceptions without one.\n\n---\n\nThis makes overloaded and gateway failures distinguishable in\nacceptance-criteria grading without coupling `RubricMiddleware` to a\nprovider SDK. Non-integer values are ignored, and grader retry and\nclassification behavior is unchanged.","verified_at":"2026-07-22T19:42:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bca70aa1f30ee1472809894e2474a76e4ff2f8bd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bca70aa1f30ee1472809894e2474a76e4ff2f8bd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bca70aa1f30ee1472809894e2474a76e4ff2f8bd/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"19e4805dc2c4514e733e263ab9e24a3cca4885dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/19e4805dc2c4514e733e263ab9e24a3cca4885dd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/19e4805dc2c4514e733e263ab9e24a3cca4885dd"}]},{"sha":"19e4805dc2c4514e733e263ab9e24a3cca4885dd","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDE5ZTQ4MDVkYzJjNDUxNGU3MzNlMjYzYWI5ZTI0YTNjY2E0ODg1ZGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T19:42:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T19:42:38Z"},"message":"docs(repo): clarify pre-release workflow (#4968)\n\nThe pre-release guide described a generic workflow with alpha-specific\nbranch names and commit text, leaving beta, release-candidate, and\ndevelopment releases open to interpretation.\n\nThis makes the workflow stage-neutral and defines each placeholder\nbefore it is used. It also distinguishes the exact PEP 440 version from\nits branch-safe slug, assigns stage-specific branch prefixes, clarifies\nthat the workflow input does not set the built package version, and\nrequires an explicit approval checkpoint before publication.","tree":{"sha":"6d7dfbb4e3d2da80dd5edfbff628ea807e6d8613","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6d7dfbb4e3d2da80dd5edfbff628ea807e6d8613"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/19e4805dc2c4514e733e263ab9e24a3cca4885dd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYR0uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASoUQABQPsOhN2vpHQxSCNGv4WVdG\nwgYse5sFy6Ytgls6y5kQ1TdoLbZDTHkfwuCX8ZmBr+47XbKSNOPY29PlsUBn1Z4y\no2lSMXzSMjBOVdp33cMwde46I080zZ8HibiBGs9a7L4z9Aj8nMj//dhEZtk3gu22\nBzysia6oubxPhp9VP0K50wF1rEnR5Jp/MavBSObj8KPXGflIQ1wRZ0yNUhB6a/aK\n59Sd2MQWbwVp8AfE9uc8Lw+62xVU8I4Tv92j4lr8PhBOO5ORmCl6qifMSGrFSqwf\nLOlb294nut4HNONV/K/9Dlv5N3rt1lGEZ+bt33iWSekCtMcQdBHf4hrcNRKaVcFw\nyPYVkHlYIrDlmcKcMcYyoqtKWBNbtntAi0ZKDYhPOTpcF6BHQBYPZZnHgZeKzExM\nhGh3bE4ha0exMNPv+rwELSRrazPXubJNNjpjXG9xiSIS4RDhs3g5mxZzIPr63EbT\nyZQsOh0cIQwweLNMrykSICQ7tr5TmfMToe0ROFlE3oZhw9gQUPM598Wk0vg7npGH\nq1t09rzlpvuwfMOz+mE+0nFYNjYXW2RrWWWlh9wJW7HRRRPTi7RdhVJzRhPb6Smo\n9uS9RdW8jotSVATlGfTTE7/+hMZL7PmKqsECCQ2Hq26R6dDcea7ldE1PL9uHED8e\njF6pKPW5C4SkC80Adq2p\n=oJqD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6d7dfbb4e3d2da80dd5edfbff628ea807e6d8613\nparent f5f962e14cbb847cc5ebc0dcebb1e3d740c1d643\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784749358 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784749358 -0400\n\ndocs(repo): clarify pre-release workflow (#4968)\n\nThe pre-release guide described a generic workflow with alpha-specific\nbranch names and commit text, leaving beta, release-candidate, and\ndevelopment releases open to interpretation.\n\nThis makes the workflow stage-neutral and defines each placeholder\nbefore it is used. It also distinguishes the exact PEP 440 version from\nits branch-safe slug, assigns stage-specific branch prefixes, clarifies\nthat the workflow input does not set the built package version, and\nrequires an explicit approval checkpoint before publication.","verified_at":"2026-07-22T19:42:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/19e4805dc2c4514e733e263ab9e24a3cca4885dd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/19e4805dc2c4514e733e263ab9e24a3cca4885dd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/19e4805dc2c4514e733e263ab9e24a3cca4885dd/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f5f962e14cbb847cc5ebc0dcebb1e3d740c1d643","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f5f962e14cbb847cc5ebc0dcebb1e3d740c1d643","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f5f962e14cbb847cc5ebc0dcebb1e3d740c1d643"}]},{"sha":"f5f962e14cbb847cc5ebc0dcebb1e3d740c1d643","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGY1Zjk2MmUxNGNiYjg0N2NjNWViYzBkY2ViYjFlM2Q3NDBjMWQ2NDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T19:31:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T19:31:58Z"},"message":"ci(infra): collect `dcode` coverage on Python 3.14 (#4964)\n\nDeep Agents Code currently collects coverage on Python 3.12, where\ncoverage.py uses its C tracing core. Python 3.14 lets coverage.py 7.15.2\nuse CPython's `sys.monitoring` core by default, reducing instrumentation\noverhead on the coverage-enabled test leg.\n\nThis moves only coverage collection to the existing Python 3.14 leg.\nTests continue to run on Python 3.11–3.14. A workflow contract keeps the\nsupported matrix and coverage leg aligned.","tree":{"sha":"667c51b81103cdd77e39ce84405f7b77a5b84848","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/667c51b81103cdd77e39ce84405f7b77a5b84848"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f5f962e14cbb847cc5ebc0dcebb1e3d740c1d643","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYRquCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVd4QACL8xoDaGEZSK2waq9KprazA\ndBiyuivrN/yL5D55PES7IvreVbhHDery2meX5fRL+wnqleNczEvMFiIDsiAbIKgq\n46xZZjBfapt26OAJlzc9BOTBd/49f+ZCEibGFHq/vtTOURnJWRLPqwhkkEu2Ncq/\nIVl++SY1YvOQP+iR6AKMxMil60damlfDk2DbKrJiubuHzcNENWLNJgfCmyVd3kjs\n7qvMKu3X40ITPuUBnwtP0AkzC5WuuGDvOvo5+MQnuhCXRg0GYXw4EHqJrqNXH49Q\nyPkAkPv1GqE0+IqrMsr2ckLSfFgWedbHuLBRTfPN+/5qXoIiK4lGalnmqs/j5+AY\nrSV0AdgPpmTjU4VMD0DBaB88Cpkl8BFX7YbPVApmveiPdiIu4l6KNXziIwQ8Ap8j\n3OhI/eTafNZEV8Ns56M3G5DeCdxqgXlvChtU14jQVNfa1ycWKti/Jf1DsJvd+zOD\nFkw8O9hOo3zGml/nXK/olnZucwYmsQwbWf6siF4Z/D06SWiPdANoTaBfSYq6sqHL\nPxwc21Cep3kX2ydGZRc3+HLhsr8O/la6t+TEO2XZLfjoE6P8N75DmM5NhJS8WWgY\n3u+VBEc3M4w2s/umeUXEt1oc78ByKojgBKqxrSsFLOLV/PaBAKBypokNooyJnBhd\n7A5lKXyWG9s0yUv4OYUB\n=7fhd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 667c51b81103cdd77e39ce84405f7b77a5b84848\nparent fe07f39ad78c5c09ea6959540a49196cd2f47f3e\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784748718 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784748718 -0400\n\nci(infra): collect `dcode` coverage on Python 3.14 (#4964)\n\nDeep Agents Code currently collects coverage on Python 3.12, where\ncoverage.py uses its C tracing core. Python 3.14 lets coverage.py 7.15.2\nuse CPython's `sys.monitoring` core by default, reducing instrumentation\noverhead on the coverage-enabled test leg.\n\nThis moves only coverage collection to the existing Python 3.14 leg.\nTests continue to run on Python 3.11–3.14. A workflow contract keeps the\nsupported matrix and coverage leg aligned.","verified_at":"2026-07-22T19:31:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f5f962e14cbb847cc5ebc0dcebb1e3d740c1d643","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f5f962e14cbb847cc5ebc0dcebb1e3d740c1d643","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f5f962e14cbb847cc5ebc0dcebb1e3d740c1d643/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fe07f39ad78c5c09ea6959540a49196cd2f47f3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fe07f39ad78c5c09ea6959540a49196cd2f47f3e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fe07f39ad78c5c09ea6959540a49196cd2f47f3e"}]},{"sha":"fe07f39ad78c5c09ea6959540a49196cd2f47f3e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGZlMDdmMzlhZDc4YzVjMDllYTY5NTk1NDBhNDkxOTZjZDJmNDdmM2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T19:17:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T19:17:00Z"},"message":"fix(code): make YOLO warning friendlier for new users (#4950)\n\nReword the `dcode --yolo` acknowledgement warning so a new user can\nunderstand it without prior context.\n\n---\n\nThe previous warning leaned on jargon (\"gated actions\", \"action decision\nboundary\") and referenced `Auto` mode without ever explaining it, which\nis confusing for someone seeing the prompt for the first time. The new\ncopy explains in plain English what YOLO does, contrasts it with the\ndefault `Manual` mode, describes the concrete risks (arbitrary commands,\nfile changes, outside tools, following instructions planted in content\nit reads, no sandbox), and points the user to the `Use Manual` fallback\nshown in the selector below the warning.\n\nThis is a pure user-facing string change in\n`_prompt_yolo_acknowledgement`; no logic or gating behavior changes.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e73579cf-d814-b365-c7e8-08f215245505)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"10d138996795cc5f9d3d0f5aa009b1e5f84fb48d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/10d138996795cc5f9d3d0f5aa009b1e5f84fb48d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/fe07f39ad78c5c09ea6959540a49196cd2f47f3e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYRcsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxa4QAAfC6g+wp6DB7dRAsqoqYCdS\n79ttDkpZ3w2k9wJ3pYEV1OnIvL6vXSZSggXmGnD/JFdnnFqnd7IAlUkGgt0Fbt5J\n/BzmAl4Q1gEe6O6T3w3Pm0yclIF3VeXzglQljh2s5BwkHKB1xYQkhGfH/vBBk7na\neShkVo2PulfByL32MCkqKoTDeL1I6GGcPiiSANyYcbzaCkAapYFOQti4jJCpUnjm\n9WiOw9oN+SRvZEOiMNGnL5qJIN7+9eKmM0NQB1wbrrk5oblMj3vzn5iJ243WfcxV\n1VC/3z1vR91H2yevDLURm0XeYNgP0N2A02EQgx0PcG0tOtz3WF7Aqk4W5UKz+OUv\nyJRczURCvahIziwqpCOlheHmwzCv6XhFz0XQKfvmby0b2YSMxjlMQQ5sJNtcyfFA\nS9NF/S3GSn8lPeTpB2/eDyeB1Sbqif1NsReMQfIWlZucOL/c1x4kz1v7K8W9cKij\nHOpbk5gXCw9Kllqtcun0VJegIiDRg4dq1fGEk/QJmouRj+1BQprSbwCKxm6DuOnc\nwjNRZh56A2XTu7KAnoNIyOE11rtOo9wZHDCti4QEoKleETnIw5+iz/38iQAAhZRa\nEV1Q/T9ibAXs+L1evhbrCcS1OWNKTvPNQb+CFz5yEp8JvgimdEfaDEDLpBbIPvuZ\nvYHcYi3QM9e+b5xhxRCl\n=t8RH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 10d138996795cc5f9d3d0f5aa009b1e5f84fb48d\nparent 28d138a39587529738c416b272aa0e9044447648\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784747820 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784747820 -0400\n\nfix(code): make YOLO warning friendlier for new users (#4950)\n\nReword the `dcode --yolo` acknowledgement warning so a new user can\nunderstand it without prior context.\n\n---\n\nThe previous warning leaned on jargon (\"gated actions\", \"action decision\nboundary\") and referenced `Auto` mode without ever explaining it, which\nis confusing for someone seeing the prompt for the first time. The new\ncopy explains in plain English what YOLO does, contrasts it with the\ndefault `Manual` mode, describes the concrete risks (arbitrary commands,\nfile changes, outside tools, following instructions planted in content\nit reads, no sandbox), and points the user to the `Use Manual` fallback\nshown in the selector below the warning.\n\nThis is a pure user-facing string change in\n`_prompt_yolo_acknowledgement`; no logic or gating behavior changes.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e73579cf-d814-b365-c7e8-08f215245505)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-22T19:17:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fe07f39ad78c5c09ea6959540a49196cd2f47f3e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fe07f39ad78c5c09ea6959540a49196cd2f47f3e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fe07f39ad78c5c09ea6959540a49196cd2f47f3e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"28d138a39587529738c416b272aa0e9044447648","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/28d138a39587529738c416b272aa0e9044447648","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/28d138a39587529738c416b272aa0e9044447648"}]},{"sha":"28d138a39587529738c416b272aa0e9044447648","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDI4ZDEzOGEzOTU4NzUyOTczOGM0MTZiMjcyYWEwZTkwNDQ0NDc2NDg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T19:01:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T19:01:32Z"},"message":"style(code): hide terminal cursor in pre-TUI selectors (#4951)\n\nThe `dcode --yolo` acknowledgement selector and the project MCP trust\nprompts (shown before the Textual app starts) no longer leave the\nterminal cursor blinking on the first character while the selector is\nopen.\n\n---\n\nThese pre-TUI selectors render a `FormattedTextControl` inside a\nprompt_toolkit `Window`. Its `UIContent` defaults `cursor_position` to\n`Point(0, 0)` with `show_cursor=True`, so the focused window kept the\nterminal cursor visible on the first character. Passing\n`show_cursor=False` lets prompt_toolkit emit the hide-cursor sequence\nfor the lifetime of each selector, which is the idiomatic fix rather\nthan manually writing escape codes.\n\nApplies to the YOLO acknowledgement selector, the project MCP trust\naction picker, and the server checkbox picker. Added unit tests\nasserting each control is built with `show_cursor=False`.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/03529f7d-97be-ece6-a6cc-bf661700873e)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"591c0ad764214dfce13b02032c0869f11718bdd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/591c0ad764214dfce13b02032c0869f11718bdd5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/28d138a39587529738c416b272aa0e9044447648","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYROMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAttIQAGKiCkfYnlwXoyNt8EZeQeNV\n2XC5cFJ1VUbjazSqjH1sm18anMF+KwzVEWcxlyCBN0ghoz/X32vMdpHnosuwBtEh\nzFlNHn6gD6oet7aoEhryaO8yPXwL+ICdCbFXy4HMgu6dtDk36KBrajR0B37TFGOS\nTD9gdajS+Zax2nY4FSGYpBdB3dADSgHKID7D/H80OPiozvkSPWgmrl3RE61i3X9t\nVeWjI+Tc6Apalad1u7Qd+7MNJw10GROkaPWRkMnSaTVeMcke2rk5omhIDzYegWN8\nXyJ6U5sxwbscT8URj2XLdSXTC5lNFi73piWP2zirV5QGcz4GD7tqwDZ7HQ0uPUPN\n+5ExnRy6Uas7pqRSuZECE5eksZxSwQ+Z8FWw5keSOuQzSdiHXNKaFMpZL3NKGBmW\nLcqnvZtT/NNgkYhV/THptFa2xsgVmVy1ycw1FioFAR50GGWr3yux7D5Ap47uVkQL\nyPqCohmufscsNPgbnLaD/9FlqSwbvcFbgz2myA39/EkAhgqWjmEPHjJwGeLa9vow\nYS7cQr4s9cIkKeuF9c6Rj0uYygcbWdhMEGsv+idJwHwQOnv/7/BA/j58JJrjt5Fw\nNwRW/3+2nkETubVYSBZ/Wz517Q8dVC+Uao7ud8tHAVwN9SgX3xJfjqw4W143E0ZR\nJmUmL/q8ZkwWrdLCRCSC\n=jU3v\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 591c0ad764214dfce13b02032c0869f11718bdd5\nparent a8d1b32aa4136d0498ba7b48367c8001ac462bd0\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784746892 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784746892 -0400\n\nstyle(code): hide terminal cursor in pre-TUI selectors (#4951)\n\nThe `dcode --yolo` acknowledgement selector and the project MCP trust\nprompts (shown before the Textual app starts) no longer leave the\nterminal cursor blinking on the first character while the selector is\nopen.\n\n---\n\nThese pre-TUI selectors render a `FormattedTextControl` inside a\nprompt_toolkit `Window`. Its `UIContent` defaults `cursor_position` to\n`Point(0, 0)` with `show_cursor=True`, so the focused window kept the\nterminal cursor visible on the first character. Passing\n`show_cursor=False` lets prompt_toolkit emit the hide-cursor sequence\nfor the lifetime of each selector, which is the idiomatic fix rather\nthan manually writing escape codes.\n\nApplies to the YOLO acknowledgement selector, the project MCP trust\naction picker, and the server checkbox picker. Added unit tests\nasserting each control is built with `show_cursor=False`.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/03529f7d-97be-ece6-a6cc-bf661700873e)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-22T19:01:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/28d138a39587529738c416b272aa0e9044447648","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/28d138a39587529738c416b272aa0e9044447648","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/28d138a39587529738c416b272aa0e9044447648/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a8d1b32aa4136d0498ba7b48367c8001ac462bd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a8d1b32aa4136d0498ba7b48367c8001ac462bd0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a8d1b32aa4136d0498ba7b48367c8001ac462bd0"}]},{"sha":"a8d1b32aa4136d0498ba7b48367c8001ac462bd0","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGE4ZDFiMzJhYTQxMzZkMDQ5OGJhN2I0ODM2N2M4MDAxYWM0NjJiZDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T18:08:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T18:08:23Z"},"message":"feat(sdk,code,quickjs): lean system prompt by default, restorable (#4859)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe SDK shipped a full authored base prompt plus built-in middleware\ntool-usage prose that largely duplicates the tools' own schemas. The\nSystem Prompt Experiments found no arm statistically distinguishable, so\nparsimony argues for the leanest agent.\n\n## Change\n\n- `BASE_AGENT_PROMPT = \"\"`; the authored prose is preserved as an\nexported `DEFAULT_AGENT_PROMPT` (restore via `system_prompt={\"base\":\nDEFAULT_AGENT_PROMPT}`).\n- The built-in tool-usage guidance prose that duplicates the tool\nschemas (todo / filesystem / subagent) is trimmed unconditionally. This\napplies everywhere, including the Code CLI (its own `system_prompt.md`\nalready covers tool usage).\n- Skills/memory content and the filesystem host-path routing section are\nnever trimmed: they carry information the schemas don't.\n\n## Testing\n\ndeepagents + quickjs unit suites, `ruff`, and `ty` all green.\n\nDeferred (non-blocking): profile tuning-suffix hooks unchanged,\n`libs/acp` on the trimmed default, persona-to-user-memory not seeded.","tree":{"sha":"001f449fddfb5875bada5315f38b7aac1ff1ad8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/001f449fddfb5875bada5315f38b7aac1ff1ad8a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a8d1b32aa4136d0498ba7b48367c8001ac462bd0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYQcXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0H0QAEtibJ4p9m9S20lbw6FVo1ol\nVpnrZvMYYH97JDPzheZ9rY6/Q+DzZhWKATb5QOiX067zSTbJODGl4OEB+9UhyDi2\n9pjtkaUcY06ky1x+k3fDBvWB4tvC+98BCpBn2usN0txSINpqXIuWNtX2TfmiuYEm\n7aUo3yKuqGI2fNXyWyVJJ9v9kB558Yq3pJrDlmjvO4TfnbcffBpqkpGUqGWChMuD\nbHP2PG9gZG16zGU4LjJhFQTFWD4b8552GK4/e+TMQslwd/O7vRyH5qZ+r2kBMhJL\nRQXGgoHnmk9Rd4+UlL5uFLPy9XTpfJsP/Oa48ct/Vej+KYB/4hdYOjI3XJY+A5Ag\nwFKyKwBu4La09UXV8xLanf7KGrpHOkReT/nnPFjp2lCpitAwPPobZwATx1zkKIbC\nTr2TBQfVIet0ZW6mUdBiRHV/nyrSJ+3eIDgncgISRnMxb/OqN+75uGhOgJh3rfQ4\n0RQkDxTmPqeqibp98GcqctS6o2TTGIW1BMTeSAzPoRohyFLhToWDBI8FhkTCFdWA\nfW0kyCGC+W8KXn+xpvRnbYMuQ9SpShIT2eY7eR9wLdFiJIY2pYR11ypNfVT7OAxg\nHiKjO25aS3334eiTIZgalWCjBTIdjUWVXXWYiu/amlprgse0HACwJHz1L6iHsmfH\n7OSQqrkLtIkyK0gpaTwE\n=10u5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 001f449fddfb5875bada5315f38b7aac1ff1ad8a\nparent 803a27f366191016bcba37724f59d5cc71175316\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1784743703 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784743703 -0400\n\nfeat(sdk,code,quickjs): lean system prompt by default, restorable (#4859)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe SDK shipped a full authored base prompt plus built-in middleware\ntool-usage prose that largely duplicates the tools' own schemas. The\nSystem Prompt Experiments found no arm statistically distinguishable, so\nparsimony argues for the leanest agent.\n\n## Change\n\n- `BASE_AGENT_PROMPT = \"\"`; the authored prose is preserved as an\nexported `DEFAULT_AGENT_PROMPT` (restore via `system_prompt={\"base\":\nDEFAULT_AGENT_PROMPT}`).\n- The built-in tool-usage guidance prose that duplicates the tool\nschemas (todo / filesystem / subagent) is trimmed unconditionally. This\napplies everywhere, including the Code CLI (its own `system_prompt.md`\nalready covers tool usage).\n- Skills/memory content and the filesystem host-path routing section are\nnever trimmed: they carry information the schemas don't.\n\n## Testing\n\ndeepagents + quickjs unit suites, `ruff`, and `ty` all green.\n\nDeferred (non-blocking): profile tuning-suffix hooks unchanged,\n`libs/acp` on the trimmed default, persona-to-user-memory not seeded.","verified_at":"2026-07-22T18:08:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a8d1b32aa4136d0498ba7b48367c8001ac462bd0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a8d1b32aa4136d0498ba7b48367c8001ac462bd0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a8d1b32aa4136d0498ba7b48367c8001ac462bd0/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"803a27f366191016bcba37724f59d5cc71175316","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/803a27f366191016bcba37724f59d5cc71175316","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/803a27f366191016bcba37724f59d5cc71175316"}]},{"sha":"803a27f366191016bcba37724f59d5cc71175316","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDgwM2EyN2YzNjYxOTEwMTZiY2JhMzc3MjRmNTlkNWNjNzExNzUzMTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T16:15:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T16:15:12Z"},"message":"refactor(code): use concrete middleware backends (#4963)\n\nRelated #4541\n\nDeep Agents Code now uses concrete middleware backend instances\ndirectly, keeping plugin skill loading and forced conversation\ncompaction compatible with the SDK after backend factory support was\nremoved.\n\n---\n\nThe SDK cleanup in #4541 removed `SkillsMiddleware._get_backend`,\n`SummarizationToolMiddleware._resolve_backend`, and `BACKEND_TYPES`.\nDeep Agents Code still depended on those compatibility paths, so plugin\nskill discovery raised `AttributeError` and forced `/offload` compaction\nfailed.\n\nRead each adapter's configured backend directly. The compaction adapter\nstill wraps that backend in `_ArchiveReadGuard` to preserve fail-closed\nhistory writes. The SDK contract guard now tracks only the private\nparent helpers that remain inherited.","tree":{"sha":"2eaf9adc57f8489baac76a6dde3b0384abb45cb3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2eaf9adc57f8489baac76a6dde3b0384abb45cb3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/803a27f366191016bcba37724f59d5cc71175316","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYOyQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2QkQADnBkc1ncgD7XnvxoyPFd1fW\nAovsprhSPwppMUEaYDwuH4kC7Z4NPIbZVHN0sxyE4c7S9Byle3/mt9LtiE5r+nRM\nolNMM5B60dYt+arnikt1xk6rJpwrCT7bVU+PPJRM5Oton1J/06TR4RgsT+4zXMSC\nwXUJ2RQaiwSK7b5KxBMzfV4MKj6gSXMv8+pIS/lK5lnMXHSyQ7SiUUV908QH+vdj\n71R/9nHqp78crwBNjkiLgQzheH7HBA/gbVbTilRcHHbE4PQJyga53+Gq6+cYxQU4\nqmXaOtSvlaGjkPhg7Ik2hiPkYC05jWtHnGqnl2vQoBPL1KfLnN2SfiNHPladzzXt\nEv701kL1JymFsfSsctQSTZQZ9BimytrTOsO2R5UC2lT3PBIapot7e1sfO1YrfMIK\nsPRMslAu3YcJWeyq4DvBIiDTzJ65CzaagGjwld3mCqR6RK/vk1HD+JlBOm9ARcAc\n8y0oLAoVQzFJGO7EALwBeTnIam/oG9vuTbDnBMkcjQ+QyWYFNSx9ZJTGf9qvyRih\nNhIC9elCZDnhAa1MikgaJX5IcumgR6tk9GE685sIKGODQm6AfevU5qPszTIQ0k0S\nzBQYzmnVGLLYivVDfZ98k4X4N3G2Ky39Kb53hsiaEUv5QJsZFYc8TrdNbi/8anjw\naycbKgS/mLO4NsfRwTtn\n=OADS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2eaf9adc57f8489baac76a6dde3b0384abb45cb3\nparent df570109b5051107bee38a90fd5e083b4fe4f1a5\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784736912 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784736912 -0400\n\nrefactor(code): use concrete middleware backends (#4963)\n\nRelated #4541\n\nDeep Agents Code now uses concrete middleware backend instances\ndirectly, keeping plugin skill loading and forced conversation\ncompaction compatible with the SDK after backend factory support was\nremoved.\n\n---\n\nThe SDK cleanup in #4541 removed `SkillsMiddleware._get_backend`,\n`SummarizationToolMiddleware._resolve_backend`, and `BACKEND_TYPES`.\nDeep Agents Code still depended on those compatibility paths, so plugin\nskill discovery raised `AttributeError` and forced `/offload` compaction\nfailed.\n\nRead each adapter's configured backend directly. The compaction adapter\nstill wraps that backend in `_ArchiveReadGuard` to preserve fail-closed\nhistory writes. The SDK contract guard now tracks only the private\nparent helpers that remain inherited.","verified_at":"2026-07-22T16:15:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/803a27f366191016bcba37724f59d5cc71175316","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/803a27f366191016bcba37724f59d5cc71175316","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/803a27f366191016bcba37724f59d5cc71175316/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"df570109b5051107bee38a90fd5e083b4fe4f1a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/df570109b5051107bee38a90fd5e083b4fe4f1a5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/df570109b5051107bee38a90fd5e083b4fe4f1a5"}]},{"sha":"df570109b5051107bee38a90fd5e083b4fe4f1a5","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGRmNTcwMTA5YjUwNTExMDdiZWUzOGE5MGZkNWUwODNiNGZlNGYxYTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T16:01:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T16:01:54Z"},"message":"fix(evals): update memory eval for current backend API (#4960)\n\nRelated #4541\n\nKeeps the memory composite-backend eval compatible with the current\n`StoreBackend` and `FileData` contracts after deprecated SDK\ncompatibility paths were removed.\n\n---\n\nThe eval no longer relies on an implicit namespace or legacy list-backed\ncontent, so it continues to cover durable memory routing through\n`CompositeBackend`. Generated catalog links are refreshed to match the\nupdated source locations.","tree":{"sha":"0899a07617ae16cee008ec907c1ac94630468229","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/0899a07617ae16cee008ec907c1ac94630468229"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/df570109b5051107bee38a90fd5e083b4fe4f1a5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYOlyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZj4QAFKO37VQ1KlPiJWmMhjPM7kW\nS16xwun317jtZy4eQ7jSyw4VFovaT2D3UQS3paxiNLndKmcKzjC5gths+TJ+2qzL\n4vLuVtoCL+DiMau4rowK7byD6kaimBggFar/iPmDYxLgKjTtdYswDQgGLy7W0rmN\n42nfU1Qz2oaxQqogIeygkBp2GqlCiAs2Ro1AdOOVVR7IPOZOImvuc0KEKdq2cxjQ\nhS8NO567sXH0LcoeWaRZiyDOcWNmMBwubMZh3Prxu5Zd8jj6ironiqQu3WOw68in\nREOs45IbLbvTbq8Fo++XVHTCVjVcnVxhiXrhFEuNFTcV6c0lrZcS2y5wNVvp+RKT\nlQ1+9ajMmAHuMcq8JOEmsbA3rcoj5pAJnmBPlvLq5Q7z6rDmfm1NhULQ9A5Py6c3\ni4LkPkxU/T5gycOhX8jTxALH2wR5sPw09Ggmk4kDp2eInaZZsSnOG5yDdozCBZn6\nL5ZTDu3WQXjiIFDYb0v2IdiOMdLyINclLKSpIG3osTlxHaT25LMXPzQtPgYAXb2c\nSh6+0eepB6QLYQvsvZFSS39hEEsTQlpPIY2Q00kIYDNA1I9vcH6Z8j82BE2ABaMR\n+6Lb53uE4toLcNxcj8F4BpniQhkKtAg51zzLcurD8J5ULsLKuffb1frlTHU1wy9T\n6B5AfI7ebFEH5yqKTBbO\n=uCNn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0899a07617ae16cee008ec907c1ac94630468229\nparent 540a0fa7eb9a88d82413cf10a5cb5c807d491385\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784736114 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784736114 -0400\n\nfix(evals): update memory eval for current backend API (#4960)\n\nRelated #4541\n\nKeeps the memory composite-backend eval compatible with the current\n`StoreBackend` and `FileData` contracts after deprecated SDK\ncompatibility paths were removed.\n\n---\n\nThe eval no longer relies on an implicit namespace or legacy list-backed\ncontent, so it continues to cover durable memory routing through\n`CompositeBackend`. Generated catalog links are refreshed to match the\nupdated source locations.","verified_at":"2026-07-22T16:01:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/df570109b5051107bee38a90fd5e083b4fe4f1a5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/df570109b5051107bee38a90fd5e083b4fe4f1a5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/df570109b5051107bee38a90fd5e083b4fe4f1a5/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"540a0fa7eb9a88d82413cf10a5cb5c807d491385","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/540a0fa7eb9a88d82413cf10a5cb5c807d491385","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/540a0fa7eb9a88d82413cf10a5cb5c807d491385"}]},{"sha":"540a0fa7eb9a88d82413cf10a5cb5c807d491385","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDU0MGEwZmE3ZWI5YTg4ZDgyNDEzY2YxMGE1Y2I1YzgwN2Q0OTEzODU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T15:48:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T15:48:20Z"},"message":"refactor(sdk)!: remove deprecated backend compatibility shims (#4541)\n\nDeprecated backend APIs and compatibility symbols are now removed. Users\nshould pass backend instances instead of callable factories, configure\n`StoreBackend` with an explicit namespace, and use the current `ls` /\n`glob` / `grep` / `ReadResult` APIs. New files use string\n`FileData.content`; files persisted by older releases with `list[str]`\ncontent remain readable and are converted to the current format when\noverwritten or edited. The deprecated `runtime` parameters on\n`StateBackend` and `StoreBackend` are removed, along with the\ncompatibility symbols `BackendFactory`, `BACKEND_TYPES`, `FileFormat`,\nand `Unset`.\n\n---\n\nRemoves expired SDK compatibility paths and related legacy storage\ncontrols, so backend APIs now use the current storage and middleware\ncontracts directly without making persisted legacy files unreadable.\nThis tightens the public surface around `BackendProtocol` instances,\nexplicit `StoreBackend` namespaces, modern file data storage, and\nvirtual filesystem defaults.\n\n## Changes\n- **Backend construction:** removes callable `backend` factories across\n`create_deep_agent` and SDK middleware; callers now pass concrete\n`BackendProtocol` instances. The `BackendFactory` and `BACKEND_TYPES`\naliases are also removed.\n- **Backend constructors:** removes the deprecated `runtime` parameters\nfrom `StateBackend` and `StoreBackend`.\n- **Backend protocol cleanup:** drops deprecated `files_update` fields\nand their `Unset` sentinel, legacy `ls_info` / `glob_info` / `grep_raw`\nshims, and plain-string `read()` compatibility.\n- **File storage format:** removes the `FileFormat` alias and\n`file_format` controls, so new writes always store string content.\nExisting `list[str]` content remains readable without modifying stored\ndata and is converted to the string format when overwritten or edited.\n- **Persistent store behavior:** requires explicit\n`StoreBackend(namespace=...)`, removes `BackendContext`, and removes\nlegacy assistant-id namespace fallback.\n- **Filesystem defaults:** makes `FilesystemBackend` and\n`LocalShellBackend` default to `virtual_mode=True` without the old\nmigration warning.\n- **Summarization history:** removes deprecated `history_path_prefix`\nand uses the configured backend instance directly for\nconversation-history offloading.","tree":{"sha":"02bddc91ab2046edebd03bbbe2fc8cd1efb88d6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/02bddc91ab2046edebd03bbbe2fc8cd1efb88d6c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/540a0fa7eb9a88d82413cf10a5cb5c807d491385","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYOZECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEz4QAEuTLWH/mrYz95gxQSjHxfWa\nYbYwl4SRiioKnn5Ptr4lBSVpj26snJSkl+85RJZ9xox34h6Y12/hdlWn74Ke3sty\nT1QGCv5WkJQImgDml1/LYHKBkIzil3hdlsmpcO4zaXCyUG1sk7+seYypjyZtGJ5b\nMZuB4xQTKGRYNGtm4HE2KaINUGotggsnI2vd0rfFiGac0ydjiXvrb4FCSDVZawLD\nNhAxO02qH7CJMXNy34eYWpEI0UHq9gNG7AbkTKVSRCu7vfWKlqtXCW/x5w5OGGKp\nqAA0xhDSWJliercvif2QG8sEN7uh5A3+pDGC3zGA1XGURnbcacKum/gL5BogDyW+\njX3wYbDGEP1e8eLUXOsiokW9W4W9EdxsBhfyrC9imb/u0tx/2DLNG5IwbOSvEC2p\nE2/iyu06Owu7o5sfKpH8I0YbvenBhZSWre1CQlKssgCa+28hLNVgWsAUsXaO0HWG\nd9M0svA+xBjXKqXGskO7eyZkIjniiHRvx3roqYMNCH1tfSEUmsL/XlwWfXdmfWmu\n+zClq0gmd3UlUgWWkVi0kte7EmGlQh+fu3Brkmt8N8XnN9zhNyYqnatf1VuFHjnY\njuKAJXZoCwfacrg0TUS/KrvctxXdKiFZuU4q7WUUWj3tHzLJNUMcTjCiYGzfkurc\nqPs0AJBJsV6q/J2kmVM2\n=ReeD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 02bddc91ab2046edebd03bbbe2fc8cd1efb88d6c\nparent 7794b61a6e76230e8c7a49bdce808b3728305914\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784735300 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784735300 -0400\n\nrefactor(sdk)!: remove deprecated backend compatibility shims (#4541)\n\nDeprecated backend APIs and compatibility symbols are now removed. Users\nshould pass backend instances instead of callable factories, configure\n`StoreBackend` with an explicit namespace, and use the current `ls` /\n`glob` / `grep` / `ReadResult` APIs. New files use string\n`FileData.content`; files persisted by older releases with `list[str]`\ncontent remain readable and are converted to the current format when\noverwritten or edited. The deprecated `runtime` parameters on\n`StateBackend` and `StoreBackend` are removed, along with the\ncompatibility symbols `BackendFactory`, `BACKEND_TYPES`, `FileFormat`,\nand `Unset`.\n\n---\n\nRemoves expired SDK compatibility paths and related legacy storage\ncontrols, so backend APIs now use the current storage and middleware\ncontracts directly without making persisted legacy files unreadable.\nThis tightens the public surface around `BackendProtocol` instances,\nexplicit `StoreBackend` namespaces, modern file data storage, and\nvirtual filesystem defaults.\n\n## Changes\n- **Backend construction:** removes callable `backend` factories across\n`create_deep_agent` and SDK middleware; callers now pass concrete\n`BackendProtocol` instances. The `BackendFactory` and `BACKEND_TYPES`\naliases are also removed.\n- **Backend constructors:** removes the deprecated `runtime` parameters\nfrom `StateBackend` and `StoreBackend`.\n- **Backend protocol cleanup:** drops deprecated `files_update` fields\nand their `Unset` sentinel, legacy `ls_info` / `glob_info` / `grep_raw`\nshims, and plain-string `read()` compatibility.\n- **File storage format:** removes the `FileFormat` alias and\n`file_format` controls, so new writes always store string content.\nExisting `list[str]` content remains readable without modifying stored\ndata and is converted to the string format when overwritten or edited.\n- **Persistent store behavior:** requires explicit\n`StoreBackend(namespace=...)`, removes `BackendContext`, and removes\nlegacy assistant-id namespace fallback.\n- **Filesystem defaults:** makes `FilesystemBackend` and\n`LocalShellBackend` default to `virtual_mode=True` without the old\nmigration warning.\n- **Summarization history:** removes deprecated `history_path_prefix`\nand uses the configured backend instance directly for\nconversation-history offloading.","verified_at":"2026-07-22T15:48:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/540a0fa7eb9a88d82413cf10a5cb5c807d491385","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/540a0fa7eb9a88d82413cf10a5cb5c807d491385","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/540a0fa7eb9a88d82413cf10a5cb5c807d491385/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7794b61a6e76230e8c7a49bdce808b3728305914","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7794b61a6e76230e8c7a49bdce808b3728305914","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7794b61a6e76230e8c7a49bdce808b3728305914"}]},{"sha":"7794b61a6e76230e8c7a49bdce808b3728305914","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDc3OTRiNjFhNmU3NjIzMGU4YzdhNDliZGNlODA4YjM3MjgzMDU5MTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-22T05:13:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T05:13:34Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.45 (#4867)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. The published GitHub release body is extracted from the\nmerged `CHANGELOG.md` by `release.yml`, not from this PR description._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.45](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.44...deepagents-code==0.1.45)\n(2026-07-22)\n\n### Features\n\n- Added the Hooks v2 execution engine and typed hooks data models\n([#4880](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4880),\n[#4870](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4870))\n- Added a filesystem tool allowlist for `dcode` with `--allow-fs-tools`\n([#4635](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4635))\n- Added a GLM-5.2 harness profile\n([#4710](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4710))\n- Added a built-in thread inspector skill\n([#4769](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4769))\n- Replaced Gemini 3.5 Flash with Gemini 3.6 Flash in the model switcher\n([#4890](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4890))\n- Show experimental mode in the splash screen and debug console\n([#4863](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4863))\n- Gate debug console click-to-copy behind a checkbox\n([#4810](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4810))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Improved scratch-file handling by allowing cleanup of agent-created\nscratch files and safe OS-temp scratch artifacts\n([#4860](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4860),\n[#4869](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4869))\n- Skip grading during `/goal` proposals\n([#4941](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4941))\n- Improved MCP approval handling: Esc now aborts project MCP approval,\ndisabled MCP servers are honored for plugins, remembered approvals are\npreserved with the env allowlist, and approvals are shared across Git\nworktrees\n([#4888](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4888),\n[#4848](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4848),\n[#4889](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4889),\n[#4939](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4939))\n- Hardened installer downloads and paths\n([#4871](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4871))\n- Fixed forced `dcode update` checks to bust the CDN cache\n([#4862](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4862))\n- Prevented failed exit setup from stranding the app\n([#4913](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4913))\n- Fixed routing so `ctrl+x` goes to the focused `ask_user` input\n([#4926](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4926))\n- Show `-m` prompts as queued immediately on startup\n([#4861](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4861))\n- Kept harness-profile diagnostics out of terminal output\n([#4943](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4943))\n- Avoid tracking inline restart callers\n([#4894](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4894))\n- Fixed debug console thread ID copying on click\n([#4945](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4945))\n\n### Performance Improvements\n\n- Reduced exit latency by coordinating async shutdown teardown\n([#4831](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4831))\n- Sped up local context detection\n([#4922](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4922))\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a91c25dd9a89250414f3abb6e9cdb01d1263ab9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a91c25dd9a89250414f3abb6e9cdb01d1263ab9c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7794b61a6e76230e8c7a49bdce808b3728305914","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYFF+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACAQQAGLywasQlFiW5tQXONURETYM\nALGZAiujj1YwLo3sFWo0pKWGQxo7a4ni04IcxZy4ASat9whsx0lTghY/vRhl559n\nFw0lkzOXq50eeRhWbGecdsj2HvT9kwrBbovaTbupCjEENX6zu/EcIJ77AwPSpeng\nR8QAEZBMLBW7zZdRvs1QIqewjbKJrB32N0C8Xb2pt/UP27c5/Cp1hwtn0kdOveRI\nZn11084HskYxPpl+irCD8K5lANT4+W2zVFEzKGJ/US5O4LHU83cG9qMOlHpJFPVU\nZe0dCnySgDmusyXIRJJ71WPO2QId6RjggPRqe8VLfXE6mZVVGi1SVQQGKQlmFUI2\nKN9UuA5i67NVnJNsqNzwzG1Ehr03/UAK1qF4JIpm4OJ757As9Cbin4jetiNowY3d\nCBwfA3px8/asMDUiSNtgWVx6wPrPKPuShGE4gn3iqFwJfSmq1yfa0riL936uBJLD\ntYKNEJNLkozyUKVFmZvaLOh8z0INITTHkNoeULstdA835fHvmvetI8PHmtc4VJ17\n2zmNdU5TD6PUNZ0BTvteEf3k9nMuZBxxSCCTkHh1qzIw7RQbUQd8xAcAnkFRGL75\nJ21fi3a+ZPnCBEWN8GCMdn3dkyxltOOYBfwrINLhkMvM2SE+pKmMVAa33Klu5zSH\nxpZ1ABtQJ8vHFmkj7QYf\n=FUjF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a91c25dd9a89250414f3abb6e9cdb01d1263ab9c\nparent 467f9dd0400087c2918bcf19f270bd934cec623a\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784697214 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784697214 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.45 (#4867)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. The published GitHub release body is extracted from the\nmerged `CHANGELOG.md` by `release.yml`, not from this PR description._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.45](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.44...deepagents-code==0.1.45)\n(2026-07-22)\n\n### Features\n\n- Added the Hooks v2 execution engine and typed hooks data models\n([#4880](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4880),\n[#4870](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4870))\n- Added a filesystem tool allowlist for `dcode` with `--allow-fs-tools`\n([#4635](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4635))\n- Added a GLM-5.2 harness profile\n([#4710](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4710))\n- Added a built-in thread inspector skill\n([#4769](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4769))\n- Replaced Gemini 3.5 Flash with Gemini 3.6 Flash in the model switcher\n([#4890](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4890))\n- Show experimental mode in the splash screen and debug console\n([#4863](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4863))\n- Gate debug console click-to-copy behind a checkbox\n([#4810](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4810))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Improved scratch-file handling by allowing cleanup of agent-created\nscratch files and safe OS-temp scratch artifacts\n([#4860](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4860),\n[#4869](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4869))\n- Skip grading during `/goal` proposals\n([#4941](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4941))\n- Improved MCP approval handling: Esc now aborts project MCP approval,\ndisabled MCP servers are honored for plugins, remembered approvals are\npreserved with the env allowlist, and approvals are shared across Git\nworktrees\n([#4888](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4888),\n[#4848](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4848),\n[#4889](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4889),\n[#4939](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4939))\n- Hardened installer downloads and paths\n([#4871](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4871))\n- Fixed forced `dcode update` checks to bust the CDN cache\n([#4862](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4862))\n- Prevented failed exit setup from stranding the app\n([#4913](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4913))\n- Fixed routing so `ctrl+x` goes to the focused `ask_user` input\n([#4926](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4926))\n- Show `-m` prompts as queued immediately on startup\n([#4861](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4861))\n- Kept harness-profile diagnostics out of terminal output\n([#4943](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4943))\n- Avoid tracking inline restart callers\n([#4894](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4894))\n- Fixed debug console thread ID copying on click\n([#4945](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4945))\n\n### Performance Improvements\n\n- Reduced exit latency by coordinating async shutdown teardown\n([#4831](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4831))\n- Sped up local context detection\n([#4922](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4922))\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-22T05:13:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7794b61a6e76230e8c7a49bdce808b3728305914","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7794b61a6e76230e8c7a49bdce808b3728305914","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7794b61a6e76230e8c7a49bdce808b3728305914/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"467f9dd0400087c2918bcf19f270bd934cec623a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/467f9dd0400087c2918bcf19f270bd934cec623a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/467f9dd0400087c2918bcf19f270bd934cec623a"}]},{"sha":"467f9dd0400087c2918bcf19f270bd934cec623a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQ2N2Y5ZGQwNDAwMDg3YzI5MThiY2YxOWYyNzBiZDkzNGNlYzYyM2E","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T04:55:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T04:55:00Z"},"message":"fix(code): share MCP approvals across Git worktrees (#4939)\n\nUsers previously had to approve the same unchanged project MCP server\nonce per Git worktree, producing repeated approval entries when tools\ncreated temporary worktrees.\n\nApprovals are now **transport-aware** when Git's shared metadata can be\nvalidated:\n\n- **Remote servers with fixed URLs** (`http`/`sse`/`streamable_http`, no\n`${}` interpolation, no `command` field) are shared across linked\nworktrees via the validated Git common directory. These resolve\nidentically from any checkout, so sharing is safe.\n- **Local stdio servers** (any definition containing `command`) use the\nexact worktree root, because the same command can execute different\nfiles in another checkout.\n- **Remote servers with interpolated URLs** (containing `${`) use the\nexact worktree root, because project `.env` files can resolve the same\ntemplate to different endpoints.\n\nThe `git_common_dir` marker now participates in approval equality, so a\ntransport change under the same name (e.g. stdio → http) requires\nre-approval. Independent clones still require their own approval,\nnon-Git projects remain scoped to their exact resolved root, and any\nchanged command, URL, headers, or other server configuration still\nrequires re-approval.\n\nLegacy persisted approvals without a `git_common_dir` marker remain\nexact-worktree scoped and are never broadened to a Git identity, so\nexisting entries do not silently widen.\n\n---\n\nLinked worktrees are recognized only when their Git administration\ndirectory belongs to the repository's common metadata, points back to\nthat exact worktree, and carries its own valid `HEAD` and\nself-referential `gitdir` backlink. Malformed, missing, forged, or\nlinked metadata falls back to exact-root scoping instead of widening\ntrust. This closes a self-consistent forgery where an attacker's admin\ndirectory passes every acceptance check except its location under\n`worktrees/`.\n\nDisabled-server precedence and\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DANGEROUSLY_ENABLE_PROJECT_MCP_SERVERS` retain their\nexisting behavior.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Focused Git, model configuration, MCP loading, disabled-server,\nconfig-manifest, and startup trust-prompt tests: 1005 passed.\n- Ruff formatting and lint checks passed for all changed Python files.\n- `ty` passed for `deepagents-code`.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"249f5abaf2618e883d3e7937ce972b36e630075c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/249f5abaf2618e883d3e7937ce972b36e630075c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/467f9dd0400087c2918bcf19f270bd934cec623a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYE0kCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgRkQAKFowMZbeuwQTACR6Q7nnIF+\nDKTgyqbbDlMC7mVBJfxW079RRqe2pZkuHzcOqaJWFCgZ0+10+f8JwKptaslraReB\nXkUq5Lc5F+565WOirsWlNfi/pzmD+VpiGpt4P/6tN4ZnkvJChdHdh6aNGeCEtmo7\nCp7q900mwwPPrxs756SEzEr/+Nh4tBNpGJNP4pSt20NV4kgw1UYJiVLZd9XKj//P\nrXHgvUceEtLM7FcRhIsO+GlLuf2sT2erXP4Q3E0BREzl3JVrCr0bgNVTmXRSEUXB\n/sQkpE2XZORH9I3lVhQz7gwrdq32Dgcdq+353DwoFGxnenw1Z65dJUtJb0luuFW5\nDqP0hS5Xx5aIqySXFi+7uF8CTBxca7KJvVbNpiN7s3yL+oUhlZo6k3iOh0hrxod1\noQdgzL5jbC30vEu0CYQWyb2ag5vq1wpPSYUcNfNqXa6BnnWg18WlKe3N1OTD6HSg\nO6xV2OjhcR6+bZCGsSudc4tfM8aYtAY/cerI+8u8zAV0f/UpGBRKCxG5L2cfYuoN\nvDtEdiinXnidQ3s5HFpYykmk1JZ3tfe5yo0m34Jvdu24cBs0SuseCu+3G9LYRHwd\n0vBoVspIROVYziKmu0qYuM/ZQEpLus5xq6P/lKx5x3v4H3Anp5nRVdDU+sMCnGHq\nYKGWrUUyIuUCxhQ7eA9z\n=4UmJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 249f5abaf2618e883d3e7937ce972b36e630075c\nparent b4cb3937bf8883e616f47621547a775ce9b29995\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784696100 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784696100 -0400\n\nfix(code): share MCP approvals across Git worktrees (#4939)\n\nUsers previously had to approve the same unchanged project MCP server\nonce per Git worktree, producing repeated approval entries when tools\ncreated temporary worktrees.\n\nApprovals are now **transport-aware** when Git's shared metadata can be\nvalidated:\n\n- **Remote servers with fixed URLs** (`http`/`sse`/`streamable_http`, no\n`${}` interpolation, no `command` field) are shared across linked\nworktrees via the validated Git common directory. These resolve\nidentically from any checkout, so sharing is safe.\n- **Local stdio servers** (any definition containing `command`) use the\nexact worktree root, because the same command can execute different\nfiles in another checkout.\n- **Remote servers with interpolated URLs** (containing `${`) use the\nexact worktree root, because project `.env` files can resolve the same\ntemplate to different endpoints.\n\nThe `git_common_dir` marker now participates in approval equality, so a\ntransport change under the same name (e.g. stdio → http) requires\nre-approval. Independent clones still require their own approval,\nnon-Git projects remain scoped to their exact resolved root, and any\nchanged command, URL, headers, or other server configuration still\nrequires re-approval.\n\nLegacy persisted approvals without a `git_common_dir` marker remain\nexact-worktree scoped and are never broadened to a Git identity, so\nexisting entries do not silently widen.\n\n---\n\nLinked worktrees are recognized only when their Git administration\ndirectory belongs to the repository's common metadata, points back to\nthat exact worktree, and carries its own valid `HEAD` and\nself-referential `gitdir` backlink. Malformed, missing, forged, or\nlinked metadata falls back to exact-root scoping instead of widening\ntrust. This closes a self-consistent forgery where an attacker's admin\ndirectory passes every acceptance check except its location under\n`worktrees/`.\n\nDisabled-server precedence and\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DANGEROUSLY_ENABLE_PROJECT_MCP_SERVERS` retain their\nexisting behavior.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Focused Git, model configuration, MCP loading, disabled-server,\nconfig-manifest, and startup trust-prompt tests: 1005 passed.\n- Ruff formatting and lint checks passed for all changed Python files.\n- `ty` passed for `deepagents-code`.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-07-22T04:55:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/467f9dd0400087c2918bcf19f270bd934cec623a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/467f9dd0400087c2918bcf19f270bd934cec623a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/467f9dd0400087c2918bcf19f270bd934cec623a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b4cb3937bf8883e616f47621547a775ce9b29995","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b4cb3937bf8883e616f47621547a775ce9b29995","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b4cb3937bf8883e616f47621547a775ce9b29995"}]},{"sha":"b4cb3937bf8883e616f47621547a775ce9b29995","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGI0Y2IzOTM3YmY4ODgzZTYxNmY0NzYyMTU0N2E3NzVjZTliMjk5OTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T04:53:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T04:53:39Z"},"message":"fix(code): thread id always copies on click in Debug Console (#4945)\n\nClicking the thread id in the Debug Console now always copies it, and\nthe \"Click to copy\" checkbox governs only the log lines.\n\n---\n\nPreviously the checkbox gated both the log lines and the snapshot's\ncopyable spans, so the thread id would not copy on click unless the\ncheckbox was on. The checkbox now controls the log lines only; copyable\nsnapshot spans (currently the thread id) always copy on click. LangSmith\nlinks still take priority and open first.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4911c553-8a39-fcf7-1b15-de9f2eacca79)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"2b78f3eb8be1de394efdfedb5a1d351ca7a3a50d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2b78f3eb8be1de394efdfedb5a1d351ca7a3a50d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b4cb3937bf8883e616f47621547a775ce9b29995","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYEzTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwkQQABrviYmC08CEyqDHGN6MXpf+\n6AR30fI1PQOVWPT4MbIT2l4HjmgYznBjslzDiawFuWOONNFfVTF9eRvhs/1OBrG+\npza8skFRXmRY0HkNwsx6+sl+L0dGYvpz6w50D9KnumSfM1V9OLIg/kNOQ1VrtlaY\n74XGYhLJbN9T+nOzAbq9O2M+Y9bledfCD/ephICNYT1AtUihHc6346hVDw8MEnmV\nXYOBOtlrZCOlyPp65SOWmum+Dua/rfDm/vB8RqZf6Bj2BvKernRpmvDRrTCkj0/9\nhCp8QC5dFK9yl0OBQUObIxZRXXzJ7dqGuj+e8VqucRBgOvIECOk6mTbZYRq+xb5q\nJjHdg1kyhsl9HF0d6lXJW0paSC3LtOyVEmy4Uj4LvTcdIBl1CrUA+/rRCOPfCVVa\no7Z5R1+OnTugknpcWeAHmdtsYnJsP5m/Um8C1WwbNEVEK4fXK34mA+utPz+jp+xw\nX6rcZ3qjevcNJpSGYvfD4XPwZZ+6n1jEZcbHP5FCvl7brx0lWSDL2EALRlkGUs8J\nsOUwOCeDCWnd1+fBxTuSX5HDNuIB+fDfQyG+ruNwzKR3ApEWouJdol4KMuh0He5H\nB46zv3rkU3vTQ5rhXrzusccEEBYv/3xlg6Xvz95oFjwpnjH96qwlVIa8MhYBvD7y\nLKRnNfLO7ZRhYVXckk7Y\n=kDQo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2b78f3eb8be1de394efdfedb5a1d351ca7a3a50d\nparent 812bae4afad6749add097f9d58e489df9ec703a2\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784696019 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784696019 -0400\n\nfix(code): thread id always copies on click in Debug Console (#4945)\n\nClicking the thread id in the Debug Console now always copies it, and\nthe \"Click to copy\" checkbox governs only the log lines.\n\n---\n\nPreviously the checkbox gated both the log lines and the snapshot's\ncopyable spans, so the thread id would not copy on click unless the\ncheckbox was on. The checkbox now controls the log lines only; copyable\nsnapshot spans (currently the thread id) always copy on click. LangSmith\nlinks still take priority and open first.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4911c553-8a39-fcf7-1b15-de9f2eacca79)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-22T04:53:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b4cb3937bf8883e616f47621547a775ce9b29995","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b4cb3937bf8883e616f47621547a775ce9b29995","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b4cb3937bf8883e616f47621547a775ce9b29995/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"812bae4afad6749add097f9d58e489df9ec703a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/812bae4afad6749add097f9d58e489df9ec703a2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/812bae4afad6749add097f9d58e489df9ec703a2"}]},{"sha":"812bae4afad6749add097f9d58e489df9ec703a2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDgxMmJhZTRhZmFkNjc0OWFkZDA5N2Y5ZDU4ZTQ4OWRmOWVjNzAzYTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T04:19:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T04:19:16Z"},"message":"fix(code): keep harness-profile diagnostics out of terminal output (#4943)\n\nDeep Agents Code no longer prints internal harness-profile lookup\nwarnings while listing tools or starting with an unrelated pre-built\nmodel. These diagnostics remain available in the debug log when\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG` is enabled.\n\n---\n\n`dcode tools list` compiles an offline `_CatalogModel` to inspect the\ntools that the agent actually binds. Registering the built-in GLM-5.2\nprofile makes the SDK treat that model's expected profile miss as a\nwarning, and Python's last-resort logging handler writes it directly to\nstderr—once for the main agent and again for the inherited\n`general-purpose` subagent.\n\nRoute the harness-profile resolver alongside the noisy LangChain and\nLangSmith loggers that Deep Agents Code already handles: to the dcode\ndebug file when debug logging is enabled, otherwise to a `NullHandler`.\nOther `deepagents` loggers remain untouched, so actionable runtime\nwarnings keep their normal routing.","tree":{"sha":"d9c955d78172f6d4bb14c88e5079434a251121de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d9c955d78172f6d4bb14c88e5079434a251121de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/812bae4afad6749add097f9d58e489df9ec703a2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYETECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASUMQAKns+jKIX2eyewLZ0Q+/fyLo\nvJ9i1xwuMxtHMvVr7toL4OUjBG1jA6sSrz3rk5DwjB7gYpUuPm18eHy4FyyvMl4Y\nZrLpm8HhlCu6LQMVhooh0FhLu7YSUhoRky7BtIp5cbCmNSygLjqJZgBxN0SHBJMg\n3Iw+ZyPV+2Nr1FKVzIFdSrT5FYXUQ1NaWybhusBZCqxkNTQYT64O9ZjQY/9m9fmv\nL0ahvUzqG3LZGUk7VBUn8tw8PMwDmisr7vhdx/jOSVuf1vnO8DmmCGbtUn+KyTC9\nHewMPoMPFMF74HpC2NHzI/VKJH1s0TV5wT1qLFfFbwTElUdgXfRp6APpPhUi+ftf\n43UPOvRney6abBRInV9VvLSS+JDWDrPCdQU7y2Y/njjOj2n7cKnmkfNIYTXwfybp\nr91w8a0yKjs2OvF0De4+Ih9yFoaxsY7UNuTf9XLjQw7662zj+krK44GgeZdof/Nr\nAVgPAsEAEbnYRYYLu+KWJqO00i/lPO8dF/GnreSs9tgYERhQPOqrO9wHOlMzfrCn\nDwc4U9Qpy+koLNr4lTajX4uV7uvz9GgV6oyda1bA90qnSWa+2LB9+PjG7Gkk0W1Y\n53yWfryinYVqa44EbMWLpwEPdoClx//Lz+28UhvxRHQgOB5cqd7gVm8J4SstFPso\ntaBN4qJlgnkQjWRyNxxp\n=yf+I\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d9c955d78172f6d4bb14c88e5079434a251121de\nparent edeffe8e88ae70f52def0b29e3fa6e44cbae5f13\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784693956 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784693956 -0400\n\nfix(code): keep harness-profile diagnostics out of terminal output (#4943)\n\nDeep Agents Code no longer prints internal harness-profile lookup\nwarnings while listing tools or starting with an unrelated pre-built\nmodel. These diagnostics remain available in the debug log when\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG` is enabled.\n\n---\n\n`dcode tools list` compiles an offline `_CatalogModel` to inspect the\ntools that the agent actually binds. Registering the built-in GLM-5.2\nprofile makes the SDK treat that model's expected profile miss as a\nwarning, and Python's last-resort logging handler writes it directly to\nstderr—once for the main agent and again for the inherited\n`general-purpose` subagent.\n\nRoute the harness-profile resolver alongside the noisy LangChain and\nLangSmith loggers that Deep Agents Code already handles: to the dcode\ndebug file when debug logging is enabled, otherwise to a `NullHandler`.\nOther `deepagents` loggers remain untouched, so actionable runtime\nwarnings keep their normal routing.","verified_at":"2026-07-22T04:19:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/812bae4afad6749add097f9d58e489df9ec703a2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/812bae4afad6749add097f9d58e489df9ec703a2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/812bae4afad6749add097f9d58e489df9ec703a2/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"edeffe8e88ae70f52def0b29e3fa6e44cbae5f13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/edeffe8e88ae70f52def0b29e3fa6e44cbae5f13","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/edeffe8e88ae70f52def0b29e3fa6e44cbae5f13"}]},{"sha":"edeffe8e88ae70f52def0b29e3fa6e44cbae5f13","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGVkZWZmZThlODhhZTcwZjUyZGVmMGIyOWUzZmE2ZTQ0Y2JhZTVmMTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nishitha M","email":"32355027+imnishitha@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-22T04:11:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T04:11:56Z"},"message":"refactor(code): use `reasoning_effort` from `langchain` (#4795)\n\n`reasoning_effort.py `used to carry its own hardcoded per-provider\ntables (which models support which levels) and per-provider translation\nlogic (building each provider's exact request shape). [Upstreaming it to\nLangChain](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/pull/38887), so\nthis deletes the duplicated logic and reads from it instead.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"5e5bab3f0a25330c5ad4351b2f1d5d8168da752b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5e5bab3f0a25330c5ad4351b2f1d5d8168da752b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/edeffe8e88ae70f52def0b29e3fa6e44cbae5f13","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYEMMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA3oQAFoLgxm3X0IluoE/b+k/l8dh\n3u4ZQuBLujOBoiGRG1Meta61SZNwDUm8a85LNPsIdB9eX9uPXjLWknQCRoSFhDZU\nT/VHBksjJ4lcTWMzP2yGpdSloVT7yMLAqE0AHMe7dNBvunWAXYHuKBX6frDlTF17\n0HCTjjhd7Qta7y4VEMNkIb3E6r3PJ3eP3mP13li0V528bNJQ3JPQ3rJLtMMm0BDs\nIOdiBHzhW0lacgiBZEH2JaMQ9I/BQ4JcFsvfY328Jghs4CVgVz8NQmNYK5/4gY95\nvKatyATTF/3zNSIyVDrZkEbrGfJwvY7eIFq4H3UFSwTb6LMHiV1gAacg2dQ8lP1K\ndh8VarOfeeCRS8+HLEqIqyTjTraVQmiPf0r9NGmcHZY0l0EG1+YTO9sXENNI0nDA\n/mn0tgeYj21yG4P2a5GXwmXsgdbSNQYKqXLZHOO1xeNVSJYuhpmkDPkXStCtgJgm\nPZrnghfgYd3J0R1qB1bqcCweLeex8qG2lKQ3FQrIQQiFrj5MU2aVK0b5AGZI0pNy\nfKNClYXy+4mI39wIpagv3Luh8j78U3qHn18+VUF5iZFXoa0Y/TLbvMLhH0O+VJct\naGVsxHNoM1MkXT6dwlFY6yzN+rlf1NVba3NnQT2Ks20Vwo60HRqQ87W3FxwQ7Pne\nZhMmeTuXRVG9F5v0GCdc\n=oNA9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5e5bab3f0a25330c5ad4351b2f1d5d8168da752b\nparent d1ce66ea03e3726e6077c6700fc480209a849a7e\nauthor Nishitha M <32355027+imnishitha@users.noreply.github.com> 1784693516 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784693516 -0400\n\nrefactor(code): use `reasoning_effort` from `langchain` (#4795)\n\n`reasoning_effort.py `used to carry its own hardcoded per-provider\ntables (which models support which levels) and per-provider translation\nlogic (building each provider's exact request shape). [Upstreaming it to\nLangChain](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/pull/38887), so\nthis deletes the duplicated logic and reads from it instead.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-07-22T04:11:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/edeffe8e88ae70f52def0b29e3fa6e44cbae5f13","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/edeffe8e88ae70f52def0b29e3fa6e44cbae5f13","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/edeffe8e88ae70f52def0b29e3fa6e44cbae5f13/comments","author":{"login":"imnishitha","id":32355027,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzU1MDI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32355027?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha","html_url":"https://github.com/imnishitha","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d1ce66ea03e3726e6077c6700fc480209a849a7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d1ce66ea03e3726e6077c6700fc480209a849a7e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d1ce66ea03e3726e6077c6700fc480209a849a7e"}]},{"sha":"d1ce66ea03e3726e6077c6700fc480209a849a7e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQxY2U2NmVhMDNlMzcyNmU2MDc3YzY3MDBmYzQ4MDIwOWE4NDlhN2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T04:06:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T04:06:29Z"},"message":"fix(code): skip grading during `/goal` proposals (#4941)\n\nGoal creation and amendments no longer trigger an acceptance-criteria\ncheck while dcode is drafting their proposed criteria. This removes the\nmisleading “Checking acceptance criteria…” step after `/goal amend`,\nincluding when the previous work was interrupted.\n\n---\n\nGoal criteria requests bypass the normal task-agent loop, but previously\nretained the thread's active rubric when they jumped to the end of the\ngraph. That allowed the rubric middleware to grade a proposal-generation\nrun against the old criteria.\n\nClear only the per-invocation rubric when a proposal is produced. The\naccepted goal and sticky criteria remain in their dedicated state\nchannels, so normal work continues to be graded after review.\n\nIncludes regression coverage for create and amend proposals across\nsynchronous and asynchronous graph execution.","tree":{"sha":"f8286b37771ae4342314771ca62163ad0524f879","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f8286b37771ae4342314771ca62163ad0524f879"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d1ce66ea03e3726e6077c6700fc480209a849a7e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYEHFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqxMQAF4d+G7K8SJQZQ16Ixj13XN2\nERb+sS/oBvbK6RNyeQchnmc29qydG584YDriEkp0IOevCJN5TJeZhpaArA+hlvll\n7tNL27T/7Zy7Tgb/sKRavqizQaqePX/rSPgjmchdJFY2i6dJF/H+FOa3cl8ZUFgw\nfqVC4ly353yM2OHVx0fxVS8i0jE+MTDa9SnxZSKVBMI8MEqjvVT4nuVwJJp+/nCu\nnmSy/63ng4rgcKk1O8h0BPhbRwGiGCxK/zMjrlqabiAMzZ+0GVYfxmaOJ1f0nVpo\nwbHt+Uw4z8vBCKmyuzeHmPcKNTPfZXGTl7+jkg199awxLRzGWObaK1m3Km5BXz/1\njG1vzshyydNkIg+cZsGhCDbBNqVRGwJV60xR/HCXqMLPFgOruzAEDZ5PXY1c2vVo\njjFA+aHKEPjaeSMVL37c6sv0JyR64yxatoym6//s1za7QYMXmXl3vVoRxZumQwMe\nSirUwR4Z22XTJeOi5tMGGc2ennE3X9nvi0m4Xh3U79mhayvyp7sVB/IX1Cw526sm\nkPBOIyyc1qc75shcjqunod+HC4Sds8F1unN8K46EOggACajhz/zuuKUIDnSteIhW\n+8cSauJETLXV+nWm0n5MRovj8Jocg4fLyFCInE4jJipSXFKaty8jqDnQMah3dOs/\n8yQHQhDitX3CYg+m7YW3\n=oMV/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f8286b37771ae4342314771ca62163ad0524f879\nparent fe08582a386b86f78f7a8047db067ea45e7e2650\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784693189 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784693189 -0400\n\nfix(code): skip grading during `/goal` proposals (#4941)\n\nGoal creation and amendments no longer trigger an acceptance-criteria\ncheck while dcode is drafting their proposed criteria. This removes the\nmisleading “Checking acceptance criteria…” step after `/goal amend`,\nincluding when the previous work was interrupted.\n\n---\n\nGoal criteria requests bypass the normal task-agent loop, but previously\nretained the thread's active rubric when they jumped to the end of the\ngraph. That allowed the rubric middleware to grade a proposal-generation\nrun against the old criteria.\n\nClear only the per-invocation rubric when a proposal is produced. The\naccepted goal and sticky criteria remain in their dedicated state\nchannels, so normal work continues to be graded after review.\n\nIncludes regression coverage for create and amend proposals across\nsynchronous and asynchronous graph execution.","verified_at":"2026-07-22T04:06:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d1ce66ea03e3726e6077c6700fc480209a849a7e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d1ce66ea03e3726e6077c6700fc480209a849a7e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d1ce66ea03e3726e6077c6700fc480209a849a7e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fe08582a386b86f78f7a8047db067ea45e7e2650","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fe08582a386b86f78f7a8047db067ea45e7e2650","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fe08582a386b86f78f7a8047db067ea45e7e2650"}]},{"sha":"fe08582a386b86f78f7a8047db067ea45e7e2650","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGZlMDg1ODJhMzg2Yjg2Zjc4ZjdhODA0N2RiMDY3ZWE0NWU3ZTI2NTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T03:44:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T03:44:03Z"},"message":"fix(code): allow cleanup of agent-created scratch files (#4860)\n\nAuto mode no longer asks for separate permission to delete a\nrepository-local scratch file that `dcode` created and consumed solely\nwhile completing the current request.\n\n---\n\nThe action classifier previously treated any deletion absent from\nliteral user text as an inferred destructive target. That was too broad\nfor one-off intermediates such as a temporary file used with `gh pr edit\n--body-file`: the user did not request the file's creation, and leaving\nit behind is not part of the requested outcome.\n\nThe classifier prompt now distinguishes authorization from provenance.\nCurrent-turn tool history may establish that the exact in-worktree\ntarget is agent-created disposable scratch, while still requiring\nexplicit authorization for pre-existing or user-supplied files, intended\ndeliverables, project content, sensitive targets, broad or recursive\ndeletion, outside-worktree paths, and uncertain cases. A\ntemporary-looking filename alone is not enough.\n\nA regression test reconstructs the PR-description workflow and verifies\nthat both the scratch lifecycle and the narrow cleanup policy reach the\nclassifier.","tree":{"sha":"c9085583da978082fb10d499b2fa0cf55296a2f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c9085583da978082fb10d499b2fa0cf55296a2f3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/fe08582a386b86f78f7a8047db067ea45e7e2650","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYDyDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAK9EQAIVpmzV+jkB7pDpOWWCO0uGc\nW4aG1MXXoR1vGCfqT6RgKqMEBm63GOAev+k1DVibCh6O6leiXjgkenNiSUq3hFOC\nNOQHN7qPobZCIfEvUS683Cf+REsiHI4QAh7fAE7ShT4njKVJmZH51mI+Nb+IqXh3\nmK85cPqA9stoPjK73HusU6HZaI7MmdQL6lmlsc/FB+Gra0VajeD3/jtFzxHt9s2R\np/J/2V0w3jzi51RjsF9GYHSFtIpqIo1u3j/Fk+h6Uq2bmDLoP3u+Tzjp2F6faxH6\nsOYHCUbXZ6uiVdGAWl1ELg2AamFf4Wu8c7vnAoTMgcP0VwmM25E38XvPLPxfp5Ws\nc/J4POF7eBwYpBEKHL6NrH4YQxKZ3ChG68LigvTx9/BGSCJqf5uygZiz/di+gT+g\nullX++wMhsJFCjxDY3mXM23kdYBoKDZtRqo3YyjRb+rFU4D35tcx57Pb1k+3l4sv\n/vwsobmjaucsFMzFgirUVDOEGTnSX4fGqGmxSBs8pMvfBq33FEvBO5hLE6jxkp5p\nxoM1T7k5YVeCs6jXR+/vtIFPlvJ5+okThDf7s1fJgu6MJZjhlIr4i+ImoNqn1/pr\ncarE2WdrdKke/FHmYmfizQKDzjn3dPOLqQB9/TXJHXLcMqDdi9ijvtG+zJsFVQgx\nPMWeOlt4FF0mMEKYr75L\n=qp+f\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c9085583da978082fb10d499b2fa0cf55296a2f3\nparent b6613a8a88b7e914c3a2f1ebbca40a4313d7af45\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784691843 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784691843 -0400\n\nfix(code): allow cleanup of agent-created scratch files (#4860)\n\nAuto mode no longer asks for separate permission to delete a\nrepository-local scratch file that `dcode` created and consumed solely\nwhile completing the current request.\n\n---\n\nThe action classifier previously treated any deletion absent from\nliteral user text as an inferred destructive target. That was too broad\nfor one-off intermediates such as a temporary file used with `gh pr edit\n--body-file`: the user did not request the file's creation, and leaving\nit behind is not part of the requested outcome.\n\nThe classifier prompt now distinguishes authorization from provenance.\nCurrent-turn tool history may establish that the exact in-worktree\ntarget is agent-created disposable scratch, while still requiring\nexplicit authorization for pre-existing or user-supplied files, intended\ndeliverables, project content, sensitive targets, broad or recursive\ndeletion, outside-worktree paths, and uncertain cases. A\ntemporary-looking filename alone is not enough.\n\nA regression test reconstructs the PR-description workflow and verifies\nthat both the scratch lifecycle and the narrow cleanup policy reach the\nclassifier.","verified_at":"2026-07-22T03:44:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fe08582a386b86f78f7a8047db067ea45e7e2650","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fe08582a386b86f78f7a8047db067ea45e7e2650","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fe08582a386b86f78f7a8047db067ea45e7e2650/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b6613a8a88b7e914c3a2f1ebbca40a4313d7af45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b6613a8a88b7e914c3a2f1ebbca40a4313d7af45","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b6613a8a88b7e914c3a2f1ebbca40a4313d7af45"}]},{"sha":"b6613a8a88b7e914c3a2f1ebbca40a4313d7af45","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGI2NjEzYThhODhiN2U5MTRjM2EyZjFlYmJjYTQwYTQzMTNkN2FmNDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T03:32:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T03:32:13Z"},"message":"feat(evals): faithful Context-Bench grader + recalibrated context frontier (#4874)\n\nContext was graded by an exact-match reimplementation that zeroed\nverbose-but-correct answers; now grades with upstream Letta's\n`model_judge` (`rubric.txt`). Context dataset + lite set recalibrated to\nthe difficulty frontier (calibrated on terra + luna).","tree":{"sha":"fce9990f938b4258f699d1b91ac070a6d66151ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/fce9990f938b4258f699d1b91ac070a6d66151ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b6613a8a88b7e914c3a2f1ebbca40a4313d7af45","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYDm9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhVIQAHym8hLyL9Oj0hn5io+Vnc4a\nheGYTjGSYT6A7xLqQlP2aYlxVi2w3gVzoj/QmYJVpr+btu1phgQrMACu8cFONcfF\nqmbzYXg/38ITQL34k+o4yFAIdgo8aUIe0G9MHga1lS+IJTfV/LmFW0N8wls08jqX\nPl7kFXJa4B0d8AYPAdnQIc7wXb0TeKYtz1AQnW52s9ixZTYzMd93WMuNNGMNBliA\njZnWYIEphKlFGMynVYeqtvGvr1F3LAp1wl5q4iSqU3gJC3Gr1p7lGYowNTSbiyJu\n7DNkaoStDGjbnafz9/4D9d+GfWyreqf9ZPYjn+8+oJPCVWmQE5fkyA6f+nQVwQK8\nYIo6REs5Rr5ogBjSL20Y+T2fi2H81663Vu1GylMCjECw1tIcux4L2aVPvkmDk2P/\nZZPGpqzJkR7iA6MryAd5mIwm3W7osoWRwyhohperYfi5I5qHEHXvN6HawPk2CVm9\n9Im28ZarCHGnezfu0AI7JnLSB8oZQjfnlAXHqsKUPBA7L/fk+URPIyuWUF+1tkkw\n93WEB6C3/0nxoIw3x4wCItlgcS8LJz3OcTMHLdTsKAI5nL/+cQIS62nGJ2FpIYAa\nv3Loe0vTT6m7fVz++KmX2vlGuflt1UTfpN/ksyZCkhTB5Y2ht4rR4CEvr+LD6Cks\nqiH1nbuW6+FWQbEHYSFA\n=kbE5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fce9990f938b4258f699d1b91ac070a6d66151ae\nparent 3fbb85e3565f270f3a567f771ebd28323f10245d\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1784691133 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784691133 -0400\n\nfeat(evals): faithful Context-Bench grader + recalibrated context frontier (#4874)\n\nContext was graded by an exact-match reimplementation that zeroed\nverbose-but-correct answers; now grades with upstream Letta's\n`model_judge` (`rubric.txt`). Context dataset + lite set recalibrated to\nthe difficulty frontier (calibrated on terra + luna).","verified_at":"2026-07-22T03:32:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b6613a8a88b7e914c3a2f1ebbca40a4313d7af45","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b6613a8a88b7e914c3a2f1ebbca40a4313d7af45","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b6613a8a88b7e914c3a2f1ebbca40a4313d7af45/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3fbb85e3565f270f3a567f771ebd28323f10245d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3fbb85e3565f270f3a567f771ebd28323f10245d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3fbb85e3565f270f3a567f771ebd28323f10245d"}]},{"sha":"3fbb85e3565f270f3a567f771ebd28323f10245d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDNmYmI4NWUzNTY1ZjI3MGYzYTU2N2Y3NzFlYmQyODMyM2YxMDI0NWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nishitha M","email":"32355027+imnishitha@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-22T03:28:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T03:28:44Z"},"message":"feat(code):  add `--allow-fs-tools` filesystem tool allowlist to dcode (#4635)\n\nRelated to #3952\n\nDeep Agents Code users can now start a session with only the filesystem\ntools a task needs. This supports read-only audits, CI analysis, and\nplan-first workflows without requiring a custom agent configuration.\n\n---\n\nPreviously, dcode exposed all eight filesystem tools to the main agent\nand its synchronous subagents. The new `--allow-fs-tools` flag limits\nthat filesystem tool surface:\n\n```bash\n# Keep the existing unrestricted behavior (same as omission)\ndcode --allow-fs-tools all\n\n# Allow file listing and reading only\ndcode --allow-fs-tools ls,read_file\n\n# Allow read-only file discovery and search\ndcode -n \"audit this repository\" --allow-fs-tools ls,read_file,glob,grep\n```\n\nThe flag accepts `all` or a comma-separated subset of `ls`, `read_file`,\n`write_file`, `edit_file`, `delete`, `glob`, `grep`, and `execute`.\nExplicit lists must include `read_file`, which the filesystem middleware\nrequires. Omitting the flag, or passing `all`, preserves the existing\nunrestricted filesystem tool set. Empty lists, unknown names, and lists\nthat combine `all` with named tools fail before the agent starts.\n\nThe allowlist applies in the TUI, non-interactive mode, ACP mode, and\nthe local server subprocess. It is installed on the main agent and every\nsynchronous subagent, so delegation through `task` cannot restore a\nremoved filesystem tool. Async subagents are unaffected because they use\ntheir own remote backend. Non-filesystem tools are also unaffected.\n\n`/tools` and `dcode tools list` reflect the configured allowlist, so the\ndisplayed filesystem tool surface matches what the model can use.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"4eda954105ddfc802d067e6fe529097870b396d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4eda954105ddfc802d067e6fe529097870b396d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/3fbb85e3565f270f3a567f771ebd28323f10245d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYDjsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlbIQAE0fj4L+mbvG8OrIuQy0ztjW\ng5RqWfjnG6tyTZdnQbnx5z2wJMTNKnf99pTTeMtai3AqfY6lyy0ENnPxTyi7OnVM\nwOfo14wt9sNziDKYF0JsPtP1Aj4aZiqm+gg27Tz4HAqV9QHBjhnpu54aOOO7AWw5\nnyvAHWabe+ua455JMWTMNwH353oP22frv4jWxPN7YT4phoQxKdmv0XAvJf9ZzU/u\nLxvTfoR74pe7b3f4kYQLcO4YKF6P2a5nXcNAMEeAJrSNoPdg1bDVIl2CMi9WgP9q\nztrW19pQ/ker8OZuFeHVnwCEepr+zH1d7D57khz84h+E3kf8L/WhDLjHHYHjLzES\nX0Mpr/DDFXDGnPAaWVtKIqBTzc9LQNqMf84iSiKBJzYjK1AY4rDcrP23nSuRCmfk\nwUGJPWvwgnz2A7ss3DMC5D4qMX93xecI0Uks77sfxC5TvRlhQy4I2jsjuKQKX/y1\nDI5iFvTT+sz6qfd6ND7D7aS6pIqmyAQTHXY8Kw7kdGEdQW4wO7HV0Xa1inrY6zLc\nWcrWx6kCPXD0dHXExcOK4/pTgBX3DfYQ7ZGSk7qtEAnZ5x1nzjP+49+ufHZ3hSA8\n6A+qvE7NQScvTBCI7FnZBZ7cZC0pH5H34BEB0eYELS9fMwaDTPpBBLWlvTfBaJuS\nKcIE/ftCWUwzddDsWVhl\n=gSbO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4eda954105ddfc802d067e6fe529097870b396d1\nparent 982611d7f9e0669917dad8b47badf17b22240fdb\nauthor Nishitha M <32355027+imnishitha@users.noreply.github.com> 1784690924 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784690924 -0400\n\nfeat(code):  add `--allow-fs-tools` filesystem tool allowlist to dcode (#4635)\n\nRelated to #3952\n\nDeep Agents Code users can now start a session with only the filesystem\ntools a task needs. This supports read-only audits, CI analysis, and\nplan-first workflows without requiring a custom agent configuration.\n\n---\n\nPreviously, dcode exposed all eight filesystem tools to the main agent\nand its synchronous subagents. The new `--allow-fs-tools` flag limits\nthat filesystem tool surface:\n\n```bash\n# Keep the existing unrestricted behavior (same as omission)\ndcode --allow-fs-tools all\n\n# Allow file listing and reading only\ndcode --allow-fs-tools ls,read_file\n\n# Allow read-only file discovery and search\ndcode -n \"audit this repository\" --allow-fs-tools ls,read_file,glob,grep\n```\n\nThe flag accepts `all` or a comma-separated subset of `ls`, `read_file`,\n`write_file`, `edit_file`, `delete`, `glob`, `grep`, and `execute`.\nExplicit lists must include `read_file`, which the filesystem middleware\nrequires. Omitting the flag, or passing `all`, preserves the existing\nunrestricted filesystem tool set. Empty lists, unknown names, and lists\nthat combine `all` with named tools fail before the agent starts.\n\nThe allowlist applies in the TUI, non-interactive mode, ACP mode, and\nthe local server subprocess. It is installed on the main agent and every\nsynchronous subagent, so delegation through `task` cannot restore a\nremoved filesystem tool. Async subagents are unaffected because they use\ntheir own remote backend. Non-filesystem tools are also unaffected.\n\n`/tools` and `dcode tools list` reflect the configured allowlist, so the\ndisplayed filesystem tool surface matches what the model can use.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-22T03:28:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3fbb85e3565f270f3a567f771ebd28323f10245d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3fbb85e3565f270f3a567f771ebd28323f10245d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3fbb85e3565f270f3a567f771ebd28323f10245d/comments","author":{"login":"imnishitha","id":32355027,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzU1MDI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32355027?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha","html_url":"https://github.com/imnishitha","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"982611d7f9e0669917dad8b47badf17b22240fdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/982611d7f9e0669917dad8b47badf17b22240fdb","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/982611d7f9e0669917dad8b47badf17b22240fdb"}]},{"sha":"982611d7f9e0669917dad8b47badf17b22240fdb","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDk4MjYxMWQ3ZjllMDY2OTkxN2RhZDhiNDdiYWRmMTdiMjIyNDBmZGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T03:14:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T03:14:42Z"},"message":"chore(code): remove redundant goal command footer (#4937)\n\n`/goal` and `/goal show` no longer repeat the full command list below\nthe current goal state because the chat input hint already displays\nthose commands.\n\n---\n\nThe duplicate footer added noise to goal status messages. Goal output\nnow stays focused on the objective, criteria, status, and relevant\nguidance while command discovery remains available in the chat input.","tree":{"sha":"c8ef5423c5f9dcad4ac47db04e981295f4486db3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c8ef5423c5f9dcad4ac47db04e981295f4486db3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/982611d7f9e0669917dad8b47badf17b22240fdb","comment_count":0,"verification":