4d47dee19ccf10bb7a5ef","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDA0NWVjODExYmIzNDVjN2E4Y2Q0ZDQ3ZGVlMTljY2YxMGJiN2E1ZWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Alexander Olsen","email":"aolsenjazz@gmail.com","date":"2026-07-22T01:40:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T01:40:44Z"},"message":"style(code): add installed plugin action divider (#4840)\n\nCloses DCD-63\nSupersedes #4841\n\nAdds a horizontal divider above “Back to plugin list” in installed\nplugin details so navigation is visually separated from plugin actions.\n\n---\n\nThe divider uses terminal-safe glyphs and refits to the available\noption-list width.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/96f140c4-eb58-9c8c-7fba-09a45da51cfc)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Alexander Olsen <13665641+aolsenjazz@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"537dc1d54d726542e57562bcbb36883d8e4efe7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/537dc1d54d726542e57562bcbb36883d8e4efe7a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/045ec811bb345c7a8cd4d47dee19ccf10bb7a5ef","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYB+cCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEQUQAGrkj4WauvMIY5xWhWhcPa0n\nfoOqidWQ6Vw+3DAGRw8gsEpcDHebVq60yX8yNvaiypHzIKp49p7VBgIiwbfU8CR7\nTp5kL65RYbgrYEi55h98yt60ieXzLUiqQbCgssJeRt675J/ZWzvQ90Raekv/jYUY\nZ5Gi/l9ByG1whynex1XfOYLZ4XiMZAKY9Qa6FSh720fZ8o7OaDStMxrGxHIC4U6/\nScqQM2JRwcp6e+3cVoJzmrU6OqtKHTzL1zdWmQhHmF1qGFAVKklJbnRXOnU5vCK7\nJZVgRC1l1dxL9SPPE8A1KKEKJajxUH3p2QGxt2H+LI9OCn3p2K/2VKtMEOWpYe5K\nPB9OXooNjFV0Dr38t6/AHYVzyun75iwQ8g4vbOE6qFG+bgTjvPFcfTFQKO0+bkKc\n8QJ9wFlhjXcJTvmeHUKKf68aXBWO0V/dZMXQruhQxe87b14k9tAr4tOBZ1Vr3lr8\nY5CC9/p48vxnFxBLerVEWtEyNj2A/X0HGTZa5ZgXesvDFmhL5EWcLg/EMA+9RULi\nBr90uQdVTWosupQ2IIT9lLQNq7GjipPf0pu7ju9nAyLudJtb1qo37PWhNgjrrTSk\nxLKLBN7W4w9c4zGKS+nMK6zdJne+hFAzZe7aZiGcp2aIjF60nV3yjWxzM/fP0ltA\nsyauhxx82Jg3CWGZl4nB\n=Mzyg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 537dc1d54d726542e57562bcbb36883d8e4efe7a\nparent 47cfc33cf9145347b57eb2daf6ef82cdaa342ca4\nauthor Alexander Olsen <aolsenjazz@gmail.com> 1784684444 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784684444 -0400\n\nstyle(code): add installed plugin action divider (#4840)\n\nCloses DCD-63\nSupersedes #4841\n\nAdds a horizontal divider above “Back to plugin list” in installed\nplugin details so navigation is visually separated from plugin actions.\n\n---\n\nThe divider uses terminal-safe glyphs and refits to the available\noption-list width.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/96f140c4-eb58-9c8c-7fba-09a45da51cfc)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Alexander Olsen <13665641+aolsenjazz@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-22T01:40:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/045ec811bb345c7a8cd4d47dee19ccf10bb7a5ef","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/045ec811bb345c7a8cd4d47dee19ccf10bb7a5ef","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/045ec811bb345c7a8cd4d47dee19ccf10bb7a5ef/comments","author":{"login":"aolsenjazz","id":13665641,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjY1NjQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13665641?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz","html_url":"https://github.com/aolsenjazz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"47cfc33cf9145347b57eb2daf6ef82cdaa342ca4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/47cfc33cf9145347b57eb2daf6ef82cdaa342ca4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/47cfc33cf9145347b57eb2daf6ef82cdaa342ca4"}]},{"sha":"47cfc33cf9145347b57eb2daf6ef82cdaa342ca4","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQ3Y2ZjMzNjZjkxNDUzNDdiNTdlYjJkYWY2ZWY4MmNkYWEzNDJjYTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T01:07:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T01:07:41Z"},"message":"feat(code,evals): GLM-5.2 harness profile (#4710)\n\nDeep Agents Code now applies focused execution guidance when an agent is\nbuilt with GLM-5.2 on Fireworks, OpenRouter, or Baseten. The guidance\nencourages earlier artifact creation, exact source preservation, and\nresult-based verification. Headless Fireworks runs also get one bounded\nrecovery attempt when GLM-5.2 reaches its output limit without calling a\ntool.\n\n---\n\nTerminal-Bench exposed a recurring GLM-5.2 failure mode: the model could\nspend an entire response planning or explaining, reach its output limit\nwithout calling a tool, and leave no deliverable. The same runs showed\nweaker discipline around exact-output tasks, including changing source\nmaterial beyond the requested transformation, treating a successful\ncommand as proof of correctness, and delaying artifact creation until\ntoo late in the run.\n\nThis PR addresses those model-specific behaviors without changing the\ndefault prompt or runtime behavior for other models.\n\n## GLM-5.2 execution profile\n\nDcode registers a prompt suffix for the exact GLM-5.2 model specs\nexposed through Fireworks, OpenRouter, and Baseten. Registration is\nscoped to dcode rather than added as a global SDK default. If a\nuser-provided or future built-in profile already owns the prompt suffix\nfor one of those specs, dcode leaves it unchanged.\n\nThe suffix asks GLM-5.2 to:\n\n- identify every required output path and translate exact, ordered,\nranged, and prohibited requirements into a short checklist;\n- create a valid artifact early, keep it valid while refining it, and\nreserve the end of the run for verification;\n- use the exact requested source, version, tokenizer, date, or revision\nrather than relying on memory or a nearby substitute;\n- preserve source-of-truth input except for transformations the task\nexplicitly requests;\n- verify the actual result, including boundary, negative, and cleanup\nbehavior, rather than treating exit code 0 as sufficient;\n- preserve correctness and input bytes before optimizing, then compare\nrepeated measurements with enough margin for noise;\n- keep unsupported media out of this text-only model's context by\nextracting needed text, metadata, or frames with a shell utility or\nscript instead of calling `read_file` on images, PDFs, audio, or video;\n- retry an unavailable command once after correcting it, then change\napproaches instead of repeating the same failure; and\n- stop when the requested artifacts and assertions are complete instead\nof adding speculative work.\n\nThe suffix is selected when the agent graph is assembled. It contains\nguidance only; it does not filter `read_file` tool results at runtime.\n\n## Headless terminal-stall recovery\n\nNon-interactive dcode stacks install a recovery middleware that checks\nthe effective model on each call. For the exact Fireworks GLM-5.2\nendpoint, a response that ends with `finish_reason=\"length\"` and no tool\ncall is retried once with reasoning disabled, a forced tool choice, and\na short instruction to create the smallest valid artifact and run one\ndiscriminating check.\n\nRecovery is deliberately limited to one retry and to the measured\nFireworks endpoint. It does not activate for interactive sessions,\nOpenRouter, Baseten, structured responses, or responses that already\ncontain a tool call. Dcode installs it on the main agent and the\ndeclarative subagents it builds for headless execution.\n\n## Benchmark harness fidelity\n\nThe Harbor graph now constructs the production headless dcode prompt\ninstead of replacing it with a benchmark-only prompt. It populates the\nprompt's model identity, context limit, and unsupported-modality fields\nfrom the selected model, disables `ask_user` because Harbor has no\nresume loop, and defaults the exact GLM-5.2 specs to high reasoning\neffort unless the caller supplies a provider-native override.\n\nHarbor session IDs are normalized to dcode's filesystem-safe\n64-character assistant ID limit. A hash of the original ID preserves\ndisambiguation when two trial IDs normalize to the same text or share a\nlong prefix.\n\nThe reusable Harbor workflow also accepts multiple newline-separated\npackage overrides and installs them in one `uv` resolution. This allows\nan evaluation to pin Harbor core and `harbor-langsmith` to the same\nbranch so the plugin resolves against that checkout instead of the PyPI\nrelease.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"3cfa1a3cc755437062e57aa83ec5931158dc8201","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3cfa1a3cc755437062e57aa83ec5931158dc8201"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/47cfc33cf9145347b57eb2daf6ef82cdaa342ca4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYBfdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXzcQACmDjd62bXsGrcLCDDVIVfVF\n/R0dPHvRrGezxj0V7EXDWYi56Q3CiSxp0wlTFUcb31p6A/czxEf754zHFK2GjunK\nlyhHiecpKzqQfn8cVBVawbco5JN21DS/bedYnYCEmvAXu59WP8/1WZYDFZXMrbBH\nwIlfVnbuRkC0bFBtICoxSUSxoCR5tEVcc5efBrJ5j6PRYS2qtgu6iY4cqYSCoLbF\nQj1q6xKtFhUBjukvX1UEr+MYjkKXTgxvOvzCXphoi3VHThuHEu9Skt4jdbYdECXC\neeVQBCEEOOEh42WaMcNV9DpBq7vQj7Mq4Rt63tHsXJ1jQTVb16oEsr1KqjbN2/AS\nvLFornqSFh1S0O6HnFxDw73UX3O+ZPlrK1hCv8HmF1gmkq5oPzfSV0GGKb+VffNy\nZPO2zHcHf9ht2gz7ja7P/CllJwrI+KllEDeCCZF0nhKzXxu2qm4SZ37FYrDPeXQA\nHCgtbd1+RKbhLkzoqZ8WYEs6c/gzZTB5sgyyzd24DR5TIYgX1zfvaGynXEBFxX5q\ngOBXhe9asd45M+Aj3cUCpXaF7o9HvRlynDutT3ugGQM/oOksd23OQ2MzDKj4G82Q\nIRosdPFumtyeryJ3IpqSY3yjUkdLTJc6pFgOgh/Rl7QWaJfSa5v8sjukVMpk6n/O\nX6SQyWo4bD+Pk+0qvstZ\n=MZGj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3cfa1a3cc755437062e57aa83ec5931158dc8201\nparent 1c2224cfb7ee85f108e730f67b90e76b7ce43b72\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1784682461 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784682461 -0400\n\nfeat(code,evals): GLM-5.2 harness profile (#4710)\n\nDeep Agents Code now applies focused execution guidance when an agent is\nbuilt with GLM-5.2 on Fireworks, OpenRouter, or Baseten. The guidance\nencourages earlier artifact creation, exact source preservation, and\nresult-based verification. Headless Fireworks runs also get one bounded\nrecovery attempt when GLM-5.2 reaches its output limit without calling a\ntool.\n\n---\n\nTerminal-Bench exposed a recurring GLM-5.2 failure mode: the model could\nspend an entire response planning or explaining, reach its output limit\nwithout calling a tool, and leave no deliverable. The same runs showed\nweaker discipline around exact-output tasks, including changing source\nmaterial beyond the requested transformation, treating a successful\ncommand as proof of correctness, and delaying artifact creation until\ntoo late in the run.\n\nThis PR addresses those model-specific behaviors without changing the\ndefault prompt or runtime behavior for other models.\n\n## GLM-5.2 execution profile\n\nDcode registers a prompt suffix for the exact GLM-5.2 model specs\nexposed through Fireworks, OpenRouter, and Baseten. Registration is\nscoped to dcode rather than added as a global SDK default. If a\nuser-provided or future built-in profile already owns the prompt suffix\nfor one of those specs, dcode leaves it unchanged.\n\nThe suffix asks GLM-5.2 to:\n\n- identify every required output path and translate exact, ordered,\nranged, and prohibited requirements into a short checklist;\n- create a valid artifact early, keep it valid while refining it, and\nreserve the end of the run for verification;\n- use the exact requested source, version, tokenizer, date, or revision\nrather than relying on memory or a nearby substitute;\n- preserve source-of-truth input except for transformations the task\nexplicitly requests;\n- verify the actual result, including boundary, negative, and cleanup\nbehavior, rather than treating exit code 0 as sufficient;\n- preserve correctness and input bytes before optimizing, then compare\nrepeated measurements with enough margin for noise;\n- keep unsupported media out of this text-only model's context by\nextracting needed text, metadata, or frames with a shell utility or\nscript instead of calling `read_file` on images, PDFs, audio, or video;\n- retry an unavailable command once after correcting it, then change\napproaches instead of repeating the same failure; and\n- stop when the requested artifacts and assertions are complete instead\nof adding speculative work.\n\nThe suffix is selected when the agent graph is assembled. It contains\nguidance only; it does not filter `read_file` tool results at runtime.\n\n## Headless terminal-stall recovery\n\nNon-interactive dcode stacks install a recovery middleware that checks\nthe effective model on each call. For the exact Fireworks GLM-5.2\nendpoint, a response that ends with `finish_reason=\"length\"` and no tool\ncall is retried once with reasoning disabled, a forced tool choice, and\na short instruction to create the smallest valid artifact and run one\ndiscriminating check.\n\nRecovery is deliberately limited to one retry and to the measured\nFireworks endpoint. It does not activate for interactive sessions,\nOpenRouter, Baseten, structured responses, or responses that already\ncontain a tool call. Dcode installs it on the main agent and the\ndeclarative subagents it builds for headless execution.\n\n## Benchmark harness fidelity\n\nThe Harbor graph now constructs the production headless dcode prompt\ninstead of replacing it with a benchmark-only prompt. It populates the\nprompt's model identity, context limit, and unsupported-modality fields\nfrom the selected model, disables `ask_user` because Harbor has no\nresume loop, and defaults the exact GLM-5.2 specs to high reasoning\neffort unless the caller supplies a provider-native override.\n\nHarbor session IDs are normalized to dcode's filesystem-safe\n64-character assistant ID limit. A hash of the original ID preserves\ndisambiguation when two trial IDs normalize to the same text or share a\nlong prefix.\n\nThe reusable Harbor workflow also accepts multiple newline-separated\npackage overrides and installs them in one `uv` resolution. This allows\nan evaluation to pin Harbor core and `harbor-langsmith` to the same\nbranch so the plugin resolves against that checkout instead of the PyPI\nrelease.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-07-22T01:07:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/47cfc33cf9145347b57eb2daf6ef82cdaa342ca4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/47cfc33cf9145347b57eb2daf6ef82cdaa342ca4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/47cfc33cf9145347b57eb2daf6ef82cdaa342ca4/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1c2224cfb7ee85f108e730f67b90e76b7ce43b72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1c2224cfb7ee85f108e730f67b90e76b7ce43b72","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1c2224cfb7ee85f108e730f67b90e76b7ce43b72"}]},{"sha":"1c2224cfb7ee85f108e730f67b90e76b7ce43b72","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDFjMjIyNGNmYjdlZTg1ZjEwOGU3MzBmNjdiOTBlNzZiN2NlNDNiNzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T00:58:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T00:58:16Z"},"message":"style(code): dismiss debug console dropdown and highlight on outside click (#4923)\n\nWhen the debug console is open, clicking anywhere outside the expanded\n\"Level\" dropdown now closes it, and clicking outside a selected log line\nnow clears the \"click to copy\" selection highlight.\n\n---\n\nClicking a focusable control already blurs (and so closes) the open\nlevel dropdown, but clicking a non-focusable area — the snapshot, the\n\"Level\" label, the help footer, or empty modal space — left focus on the\noverlay, so the dropdown stayed open. The same gap left the log line's\nclick-to-copy highlight stuck after clicking elsewhere.\n\n`DebugConsoleScreen` now handles mouse-down at the screen level: if the\nlevel `Select` is expanded and the click lands outside both the select\nbox and its overlay, it collapses the dropdown (re-focusing the select\nonly when focus is still trapped on the now-hidden overlay); and if the\nclick lands outside the log view, it clears the selection highlight. A\nclick on empty space within the log also clears the highlight.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/147046a3-6229-6255-5638-51f725f2250c)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"c01e7ba639909aae75158d38429f5e596d2e7b5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c01e7ba639909aae75158d38429f5e596d2e7b5b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/1c2224cfb7ee85f108e730f67b90e76b7ce43b72","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYBWoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEssQADImTtGdEJw57/tP/ul1CXfr\nB/28McQmEaNIZpCiMxu88/UkReuscz1c8T9SX6kzHAGbXAS5pd9gDXHk51Uv19U9\npVuFjhJyilbP5g3PGTSPFxVxbow4cr7fwVTGZ9j2sQTMMsuub/mNILXe+GowmLZt\nk392e9oXcmUbaif02I9xm4rjOevUUAu/Z2+otZimBwv/yS0VFWLpVqDpfbFugZou\nWqzI8zQLXkf52tGPFHe2/wKsIxX2cbUMztGnmPf7F0JnVxzs7yKwuX+Zx0v8xKYo\nNhXCM5A3zyjauXlcmTXQVNkupe2d3z63rUtlYWxXYk0J/SJ/AyI5jYy4vbNfI0oi\nCydlftdMqnRjgCcPf67pgg2Y5tgn2vYaYWPJ8TXXNEz+RAPMueZpf8A2UdpPgBvo\n+uWN+r7tGQwdQ3iao3zQb5Xj81uwRgkx+LkJaX5InJKU76+LnSQFXuo4+D3S93Hj\nZI9h+pjsgmP4dZifuSFjmt4difA7iej0BmikzVhtLyyeoIWNWqBtdS0ay38/dZgh\nT0UMso35GthGLuN1vUUXFCEKoQpmRhoUEjvIQdvKMx/kUKGs4TC+1i2P0Kp5ErmC\nYvLpEDuladXcr/BIsk+j5sDN27Xvji+O2RI6RSOiHXScQPNTNPMaJnmU3MhXbXQy\na2r7TBXUvgZV/4XG/kUn\n=CAHI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c01e7ba639909aae75158d38429f5e596d2e7b5b\nparent 4c3b1667035e3be6ae88cf8c431e0d6f143d2ff4\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784681896 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784681896 -0400\n\nstyle(code): dismiss debug console dropdown and highlight on outside click (#4923)\n\nWhen the debug console is open, clicking anywhere outside the expanded\n\"Level\" dropdown now closes it, and clicking outside a selected log line\nnow clears the \"click to copy\" selection highlight.\n\n---\n\nClicking a focusable control already blurs (and so closes) the open\nlevel dropdown, but clicking a non-focusable area — the snapshot, the\n\"Level\" label, the help footer, or empty modal space — left focus on the\noverlay, so the dropdown stayed open. The same gap left the log line's\nclick-to-copy highlight stuck after clicking elsewhere.\n\n`DebugConsoleScreen` now handles mouse-down at the screen level: if the\nlevel `Select` is expanded and the click lands outside both the select\nbox and its overlay, it collapses the dropdown (re-focusing the select\nonly when focus is still trapped on the now-hidden overlay); and if the\nclick lands outside the log view, it clears the selection highlight. A\nclick on empty space within the log also clears the highlight.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/147046a3-6229-6255-5638-51f725f2250c)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-22T00:58:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1c2224cfb7ee85f108e730f67b90e76b7ce43b72","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1c2224cfb7ee85f108e730f67b90e76b7ce43b72","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1c2224cfb7ee85f108e730f67b90e76b7ce43b72/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4c3b1667035e3be6ae88cf8c431e0d6f143d2ff4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4c3b1667035e3be6ae88cf8c431e0d6f143d2ff4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4c3b1667035e3be6ae88cf8c431e0d6f143d2ff4"}]},{"sha":"4c3b1667035e3be6ae88cf8c431e0d6f143d2ff4","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRjM2IxNjY3MDM1ZTNiZTZhZTg4Y2Y4YzQzMWUwZDZmMTQzZDJmZjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T00:45:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T00:45:21Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): propagate root listing errors from `CompositeBackend` (#4925)\n\nCloses #4846\n\n`CompositeBackend.ls(\"/\")` and `als(\"/\")` now report failures from the\ndefault backend instead of returning a successful route-only listing.\nThis prevents agents from interpreting an unavailable root filesystem as\nhealthy and nearly empty.\n\nCredit to @Kushal9889 for reporting the issue and providing the\nreproduction.\n\n---\n\nRoot listings combine the default backend's files with virtual route\ndirectories. Previously, that merge ignored an error from the default\nbackend and constructed a successful result from routes alone. This\nchange gives backend failures precedence over partial listings, matching\nrouted listings and the existing grep and glob merge behavior.","tree":{"sha":"e02e0250d2a6a78e1b0679a45d496e038c05b405","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e02e0250d2a6a78e1b0679a45d496e038c05b405"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4c3b1667035e3be6ae88cf8c431e0d6f143d2ff4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYBKhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArCwQAHuYbf5f3TRXlVwuc2yl785k\nqYxSracCCqERJXuomsCNs4SxqQ3825oe67hxzgCzWUsGga1JZTs6j40adeyXhczp\nlX+hfntSEofanEKqZAI4+V1ZFdSnyjo2Xn3U7wp3m7CHueS7nuSDU30FsieKU6nC\nEAIjSbN1QcYYpcc1I5CPbsWVADqJlqR5PSAU1ZKmBzQFhGMQ25wF0VaresseiKPk\nG1B+C4ECJjpGnjQPibBPG6tT4TZKVSA5Cm43hXd0lb/QFJLnAmbJnzOjypzXfRJv\nOiyhSzRoAui8VgxnFG1oWrY7YfBT/NhY/IuVaLijZPnKQeLO/WRQXrsaefIzQWhu\nRmWnRuG76nS5PHq8xJx1wR2nfk5OzH386BQvRMiEKsac4KKDGf+5G4Qyi5bvanYK\nG2R5FXwmNx5GsIPV5IoHeDMLLIzDCA6+travxp6KOomd9a/IPz9x6MwICQYPm9qA\nOUzAQxA0mRapmSuqcjW/1MWuoQl2xtPnYox8UPzxVNeO868X+ym52uyH4twPiQEJ\n+RG3ZIeXhpI5vFwGEvGzumGjv9Skv5IY4hFVGNYnE0QLckgPVHuNEtDSO8SCQXOr\nYtqgdQhEjRYvj3QskFFMQ/BrXrFl1tQSydwFIxhn0in5whcyjk7/HygDRx5Dee+Q\n386xGsbmEipmfrx3Nfk5\n=Spx3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e02e0250d2a6a78e1b0679a45d496e038c05b405\nparent 94134d4fef18450e1dc242d512a0cf0b644596de\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784681121 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784681121 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): propagate root listing errors from `CompositeBackend` (#4925)\n\nCloses #4846\n\n`CompositeBackend.ls(\"/\")` and `als(\"/\")` now report failures from the\ndefault backend instead of returning a successful route-only listing.\nThis prevents agents from interpreting an unavailable root filesystem as\nhealthy and nearly empty.\n\nCredit to @Kushal9889 for reporting the issue and providing the\nreproduction.\n\n---\n\nRoot listings combine the default backend's files with virtual route\ndirectories. Previously, that merge ignored an error from the default\nbackend and constructed a successful result from routes alone. This\nchange gives backend failures precedence over partial listings, matching\nrouted listings and the existing grep and glob merge behavior.","verified_at":"2026-07-22T00:45:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4c3b1667035e3be6ae88cf8c431e0d6f143d2ff4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4c3b1667035e3be6ae88cf8c431e0d6f143d2ff4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4c3b1667035e3be6ae88cf8c431e0d6f143d2ff4/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"94134d4fef18450e1dc242d512a0cf0b644596de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/94134d4fef18450e1dc242d512a0cf0b644596de","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/94134d4fef18450e1dc242d512a0cf0b644596de"}]},{"sha":"94134d4fef18450e1dc242d512a0cf0b644596de","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDk0MTM0ZDRmZWYxODQ1MGUxZGMyNDJkNTEyYTBjZjBiNjQ0NTk2ZGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T00:44:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T00:44:59Z"},"message":"fix(evals): restore clean-checkout checks (#4924)\n\nCloses #4886\n\n---\n\nThe tau3 Harbor unit test was added with a local standard-library import\nand intentionally unused stub parameters that violate the evals Ruff\nconfiguration. Move the import to module scope and mark the stub\nparameters as unused so `make format` succeeds on a clean checkout.\n\nDeep Agents Code subsequently raised dependency minimums that overlap\nwith evals' narrower direct ranges. Align those ranges and regenerate\nthe evals lockfile so the repository's lock validation can resolve the\npackage again.\n\nThanks to @kenwoodjw for reporting the formatting failure and\nidentifying its fix.\n\nCo-authored-by: kenwoodjw <10386710+kenwoodjw@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"91b081d7b88b260de3075aeee0a5f917070cef76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/91b081d7b88b260de3075aeee0a5f917070cef76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/94134d4fef18450e1dc242d512a0cf0b644596de","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYBKLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgk4QAFPrswD2+ImNl4jbhbWyhQzp\nov0NOFS/PMsNk69jSp597DzFlZU62eKSCuFCC6cFOiW/jML9/OrT/Rg6qD8H/DHc\nK+TFw1iwNOdq55l7XG2TpLLj7J9wPsGOxH3fCd4Z/WC8tbGzpLljNk+iJqgfoMs2\n2qnLy1ZX028UxhUFEJbv/x0pt9FGdHYi/5hz6P2Jzrajptv0DOHEp3Z28u9r/cQc\netVBuYP2qpMXOKBA9L8+TXttjKKsCigRHg0U+l0O7g6GZd8xzpKHMhpajNXK+piv\nLR2TUPsMqIimZa6eTkFwTp3+sTiO+wH9LESao4uaiPk9/6Fj8/6DMeOskBafPkQe\nh5yEWD78LHXWKJg25RutPiAQpCSsO3cBOixc3BhtOWYwgMZSJWWakIMoRLXxHljZ\niYJG/npdMCB0sLbe7Qy/efxfwHwt7pBvorTUF8TesksU5PuOIZVUZ4RI3fHSW9WD\n8mR/Lo2PIAnhvHnwadoeCHepUOG0SQ534sNIdh3GN/u8zAwdp/GbjRjp5vKxB0xF\ngzF4m69Ug6atP6fGt/lz6GtQCNAvm0WkZrc9QxyblkGkN7CPhxWSM4S+48iYENfS\nCGo0z/1HUtJ+cNj7KuwxOOns8aj085rNeH3dwdHLXujgHTTQvyR5RtWVVV9FiC0b\n617QHW1B3qbtdbZ3wYZt\n=6dWz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 91b081d7b88b260de3075aeee0a5f917070cef76\nparent d3650c7b1f5ca968abd72345a511719d4ba65907\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784681099 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784681099 -0400\n\nfix(evals): restore clean-checkout checks (#4924)\n\nCloses #4886\n\n---\n\nThe tau3 Harbor unit test was added with a local standard-library import\nand intentionally unused stub parameters that violate the evals Ruff\nconfiguration. Move the import to module scope and mark the stub\nparameters as unused so `make format` succeeds on a clean checkout.\n\nDeep Agents Code subsequently raised dependency minimums that overlap\nwith evals' narrower direct ranges. Align those ranges and regenerate\nthe evals lockfile so the repository's lock validation can resolve the\npackage again.\n\nThanks to @kenwoodjw for reporting the formatting failure and\nidentifying its fix.\n\nCo-authored-by: kenwoodjw <10386710+kenwoodjw@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-22T00:45:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/94134d4fef18450e1dc242d512a0cf0b644596de","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/94134d4fef18450e1dc242d512a0cf0b644596de","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/94134d4fef18450e1dc242d512a0cf0b644596de/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d3650c7b1f5ca968abd72345a511719d4ba65907","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d3650c7b1f5ca968abd72345a511719d4ba65907","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d3650c7b1f5ca968abd72345a511719d4ba65907"}]},{"sha":"d3650c7b1f5ca968abd72345a511719d4ba65907","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQzNjUwYzdiMWY1Y2E5NjhhYmQ3MjM0NWE1MTE3MTlkNGJhNjU5MDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T00:01:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T00:01:54Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): condition large-result guidance on visible tools (#4920)\n\nDepends on #4921\nCloses #4914\n\nThis is the second of two related fixes. #4921 comes first: it removes\n`execute` instructions that forbid shell search or point to hidden\ndedicated tools. With that prerequisite in place, this PR makes the\n`Large Tool Results` prompt recommend search paths that the model\nactually can use: the dedicated `grep` tool when available, `execute` as\na shell-search fallback when it is the only option, or no search\nguidance when neither is available.\n\n---\n\nThe choice is made after both the `tools=` allowlist and backend\ncapability filtering. A restricted `read_file`-only smoke snapshot\nguards the final model prompt, while the default all-tools snapshots\nremain unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"ee156df54aa834ddaaf7346680eba34c664eccde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ee156df54aa834ddaaf7346680eba34c664eccde"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d3650c7b1f5ca968abd72345a511719d4ba65907","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYAhyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYasQAFW2GzofUmT6WhaSGuFH56Zq\nIREjUN64R5L9VBWxHrOa/MuuTFmqyh7uKZjsRiS3O/rP6Rye+m3LIAT06w135HRb\n6BUO2c1JWxQBkcMIFcxdNjlPXtE69vCnwhkbVRXkCT/CyZm/xjBs7LkaLUnCe0Pq\nNipDhC1FDIDtxILqSebT8NJnhlUaQruNylGMEECmeWciQ5f+cQFvAl693OpYDsoc\n4L1P/IOm6CbaRq3FtwdEzKZJs1nfisEM3X0hTBjxkyNnrAUy1cWwxCPWYJLHVyKt\ndZTnItv+oCCCxW4EJlf0StFaHbNsciIvPWO6j2wGtgvUB8a3qQxjyQm0O/SoDlVP\noYQSXVlhcNdN+6l/kf6HhZ4zDep6PpOGkemuH85R8TNp9MjOjowtD6FTc32NFxta\nJ9aZc41B0VJ0Zr16+4HUJd1kY7KAq4iDlPlKFb1vZi2to2XwjxA5LIhTEoCfEOI9\ngrhXj1tawgB8pvESspyLcC+/aDx5BJSrLogj9i6q7YI98dciRPl7btC65tKEZZpd\nzaqey54+YVLCDLw3S5pirDQcX4TfmURX85aV+Fs8o1dTiy8UmxLZq7tPuHHBXepJ\nGRvNq76axWar8E0PD8fB/FSSqYyGAXTnwpsUbFHzdpMoT6C35rcb26TSoKetx00h\nEG0n4D6Y75d//df+0Dln\n=8sQB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ee156df54aa834ddaaf7346680eba34c664eccde\nparent b65cc0076caab2e35c07598055b8b338a47e5e1a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784678514 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784678514 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): condition large-result guidance on visible tools (#4920)\n\nDepends on #4921\nCloses #4914\n\nThis is the second of two related fixes. #4921 comes first: it removes\n`execute` instructions that forbid shell search or point to hidden\ndedicated tools. With that prerequisite in place, this PR makes the\n`Large Tool Results` prompt recommend search paths that the model\nactually can use: the dedicated `grep` tool when available, `execute` as\na shell-search fallback when it is the only option, or no search\nguidance when neither is available.\n\n---\n\nThe choice is made after both the `tools=` allowlist and backend\ncapability filtering. A restricted `read_file`-only smoke snapshot\nguards the final model prompt, while the default all-tools snapshots\nremain unchanged.","verified_at":"2026-07-22T00:01:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d3650c7b1f5ca968abd72345a511719d4ba65907","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d3650c7b1f5ca968abd72345a511719d4ba65907","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d3650c7b1f5ca968abd72345a511719d4ba65907/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b65cc0076caab2e35c07598055b8b338a47e5e1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b65cc0076caab2e35c07598055b8b338a47e5e1a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b65cc0076caab2e35c07598055b8b338a47e5e1a"}]},{"sha":"b65cc0076caab2e35c07598055b8b338a47e5e1a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGI2NWNjMDA3NmNhYWIyZTM1YzA3NTk4MDU1YjhiMzM4YTQ3ZTVlMWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-21T23:52:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T23:52:45Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): condition `execute` search guidance on visible tools (#4921)\n\nRelated #4914\n\nThis is the first of two related fixes and should merge before #4920.\n\nAdjusts `execute`'s tool description so that search tools\n(`glob`/`grep`) are not still recommended if removed, and equivalent\nshell commands are not forbidden.\n\n#4920 can then safely describe `execute` as the fallback for large\noffloaded results when `grep` is not visible.\n\n---\n\n`FilesystemMiddleware` derives the description from the search tools\nthat remain visible after allowlist and backend capability filtering.\nCustom `execute` descriptions remain authoritative, and the default\nall-tools description is unchanged.\n\n## Before and after\n\nWith `tools=[\"read_file\", \"execute\"]`, neither dedicated search tool is\nregistered.\n\n- Before, `execute` said:\n\n> You MUST avoid using search commands like find and grep. Instead use\nthe grep, glob tools to search.\n\n  It also labeled shell `find` and `grep -r` commands as bad examples.\n- After, `execute` keeps the guidance to use `read_file` instead of\n`cat`, `head`, or `tail`, but no longer discourages shell `find` or\n`grep`.\n\nWith `tools=[\"read_file\", \"glob\", \"execute\"]`, only file discovery has a\ndedicated search tool.\n\n- Before, `execute` recommended both `grep` and `glob` and discouraged\nboth equivalent shell commands.\n- After, `execute` says:\n\n> You MUST avoid using shell find for searches. Instead use the glob\ntool to find files.\n\nIt keeps the shell `find` bad example but removes the shell `grep -r`\nbad example.","tree":{"sha":"c98c0726a313f2311f5a90b68bfe88240c3bcac2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c98c0726a313f2311f5a90b68bfe88240c3bcac2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b65cc0076caab2e35c07598055b8b338a47e5e1a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYAZNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7CYQACRRZNeA8guAoQTrK5NB+HS5\nGBZGmusJ6EF9pVV0eRshuBaFdjT50nxo6qgY64tQ9lg4FAq2CAQ0DyBD5lnoAbw6\nDUmNm9hZtLRjYBETSHPXsiAk/UWswbJe9Y0NsvhResqYotoEiz7Rb59h88Q/Jneg\nq+5W93am9LMpON6jKG2ZQozJzB7CJ998xStf5CebP+1V2q+B5RBqTAOg2fOokcY9\nVwbP7ZmbJyVNkCBotacvDdz1LIkJRgOO/SsRR6W/HG4nBm2cS8qS9YlcGmNZMeQW\nqPg14mrlIqWENmFoZYQXr+oYi5DuIQ0A/eqBjpTlno81el262EZUqkasDkHJR8Ar\nB25stkphptNOZKmPE6J7ZLpVGZ/PY0yGXw+cnOqAK7JfN5VMM/L+QPim6ubQbL2f\nBISVzUTzV9dZ490GjgIWGrN+hfqNrPDjLIds+r7BGgvMuK8ktnaaAXcui2/Lwwbz\ntM4h5GELBBU3Wg8c/GCih1An8Y+siUBYgKJ6afzy+l4cYaIa6Ebd/u/6GWolB3ui\nL4laS1nwiebmgAGXpwtQ/XZC+LOMwKkh3+7sYrhVrhFyjYhy+Tq2vzQC4jxyQuD5\nyVralLVmb0L4ji6yR+XhDXyU2aYgO72MM6cfb8dvGrXQD3Shei/vLPBEQBNVO0qB\nLD+ZywHB/8MShxCMbMS6\n=KM1t\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c98c0726a313f2311f5a90b68bfe88240c3bcac2\nparent 0b512d4b79b1a03c7e452f1e76350cf726b1ec38\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784677965 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784677965 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): condition `execute` search guidance on visible tools (#4921)\n\nRelated #4914\n\nThis is the first of two related fixes and should merge before #4920.\n\nAdjusts `execute`'s tool description so that search tools\n(`glob`/`grep`) are not still recommended if removed, and equivalent\nshell commands are not forbidden.\n\n#4920 can then safely describe `execute` as the fallback for large\noffloaded results when `grep` is not visible.\n\n---\n\n`FilesystemMiddleware` derives the description from the search tools\nthat remain visible after allowlist and backend capability filtering.\nCustom `execute` descriptions remain authoritative, and the default\nall-tools description is unchanged.\n\n## Before and after\n\nWith `tools=[\"read_file\", \"execute\"]`, neither dedicated search tool is\nregistered.\n\n- Before, `execute` said:\n\n> You MUST avoid using search commands like find and grep. Instead use\nthe grep, glob tools to search.\n\n  It also labeled shell `find` and `grep -r` commands as bad examples.\n- After, `execute` keeps the guidance to use `read_file` instead of\n`cat`, `head`, or `tail`, but no longer discourages shell `find` or\n`grep`.\n\nWith `tools=[\"read_file\", \"glob\", \"execute\"]`, only file discovery has a\ndedicated search tool.\n\n- Before, `execute` recommended both `grep` and `glob` and discouraged\nboth equivalent shell commands.\n- After, `execute` says:\n\n> You MUST avoid using shell find for searches. Instead use the glob\ntool to find files.\n\nIt keeps the shell `find` bad example but removes the shell `grep -r`\nbad example.","verified_at":"2026-07-21T23:52:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b65cc0076caab2e35c07598055b8b338a47e5e1a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b65cc0076caab2e35c07598055b8b338a47e5e1a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b65cc0076caab2e35c07598055b8b338a47e5e1a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0b512d4b79b1a03c7e452f1e76350cf726b1ec38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0b512d4b79b1a03c7e452f1e76350cf726b1ec38","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0b512d4b79b1a03c7e452f1e76350cf726b1ec38"}]},{"sha":"0b512d4b79b1a03c7e452f1e76350cf726b1ec38","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDBiNTEyZDRiNzliMWEwM2M3ZTQ1MmYxZTc2MzUwY2Y3MjZiMWVjMzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-21T23:51:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T23:51:02Z"},"message":"perf(code): speed up local context detection (#4922)\n\nSpeeds up Deep Agents Code's local-context collection, reducing the\ndelay before the first interaction and after conversation summarization\nwithout changing the context shown to the agent.\n\n---\n\nLocal-context collection previously ran several independent shell probes\nserially and fully scanned some inputs even though it displayed only a\npreview. This change runs independent work concurrently, reuses shared\nmetadata, and stops preview-oriented reads once enough output is\navailable.\n\nBenchmark results:\n\n- **Overall detection:** approximately 16–17% faster, reducing the\nmedian initial load or context refresh from 73 ms to 61 ms.\n- **Large inputs:** approximately 50% faster for large Makefile previews\nand 35% faster for 10,000-entry directory listings.\n- **Prompt composition:** approximately 8–12% faster per model call.\n\nThe benchmarks cover a realistic monorepo, large directories and\nMakefiles, initial middleware bookkeeping, and per-model-request prompt\ncomposition.","tree":{"sha":"870c59125495529cbf2a776cb0d5e69eec07310f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/870c59125495529cbf2a776cb0d5e69eec07310f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0b512d4b79b1a03c7e452f1e76350cf726b1ec38","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYAXmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQmQQADz1FQ4wUVsTIyQbHaw5UVZ1\nWR+tOxHnXPgJKaZF9rPq2tIyR7XnmAxThyPrwGXOWTdO54JMn6XbtrpXmsx0AmNp\naLnG6GbnparpxZGW5px+MDASioy+0ikduMNJlRGogz9po94wJVM6mSXS10q5LI6x\nnq7rXdwxzder2mbt4BWzaYlHsNw4g5dVmamx2+wHsDgCTtOzyE35G0/l5fzE/pRP\nOU46czK0TV4cNJfEYO4kWuSDdHhVkh/hgpmowYpiYlTYVw8l98psFvG8h+/9wnFM\nrnleGqUoFN/YtiaOceejzdEESukiuQgttuegfvqvtiJHxvRWclsH7Juf4wsvsxIF\nJPxn0lK/Sl7utKFHiElBv0ijqxpbTSbNBnXxLRwU6hFvFnLvK536cj3vofMm8Qw5\nCHnWl1Hz8CbXcHw9mz1vAYRjg7scXEFMG74+p7pTLxOGKCVXOn0ORFtRGtB/MZky\nspYy5jltKmPAPFCNflsNf/UGGBXFqLAZ+qsKymA0sqT3qn5GakmOJIiTEEcUkkCw\nhHMQMe7RAJEDpRD0JBX2HRuxjJoL8dDndAN2z8wLk3+fNg9CKnsh0H43M2o2Jr7N\nskiePDunDzQo38l/uY3NWsBFbi5EYnfmBEXuFhqjOmv5IdDinD+lbPLAXlazWe8x\nvwVlC20bdMneSp2NRDVG\n=EjnZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 870c59125495529cbf2a776cb0d5e69eec07310f\nparent a8e476807cf1da54acecffd3614a0d64e4705e29\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784677862 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784677862 -0400\n\nperf(code): speed up local context detection (#4922)\n\nSpeeds up Deep Agents Code's local-context collection, reducing the\ndelay before the first interaction and after conversation summarization\nwithout changing the context shown to the agent.\n\n---\n\nLocal-context collection previously ran several independent shell probes\nserially and fully scanned some inputs even though it displayed only a\npreview. This change runs independent work concurrently, reuses shared\nmetadata, and stops preview-oriented reads once enough output is\navailable.\n\nBenchmark results:\n\n- **Overall detection:** approximately 16–17% faster, reducing the\nmedian initial load or context refresh from 73 ms to 61 ms.\n- **Large inputs:** approximately 50% faster for large Makefile previews\nand 35% faster for 10,000-entry directory listings.\n- **Prompt composition:** approximately 8–12% faster per model call.\n\nThe benchmarks cover a realistic monorepo, large directories and\nMakefiles, initial middleware bookkeeping, and per-model-request prompt\ncomposition.","verified_at":"2026-07-21T23:51:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0b512d4b79b1a03c7e452f1e76350cf726b1ec38","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0b512d4b79b1a03c7e452f1e76350cf726b1ec38","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0b512d4b79b1a03c7e452f1e76350cf726b1ec38/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0ND