54acecffd3614a0d64e4705e29","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYAB7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvcwQABnFcLjuumdi3wijl/VNVg9X\nJDNb24foFfH4xVDiv3mjPLc93NkR49zylopFQcF+MV7eOlTi6h2lNh7/oMNSSX3/\ngJmgp0q9FRTfctZFkVZQz+1mJTQVVP4gEb2hx3lOSQxgmy/VvBEaz9F1SJ2oxLjg\nqND2SiHfZzandJFNh5m4dpGhOf/AJCYZXvjB5tGQhIEEvdgdm91PckM7BOjDPTkv\ngq0huMhvtnFSfW4VlAzhROQRLR7LtTGIQL59LstDy+P/p0nhlPVDBUU3lS44DG/Z\nkXHdkMxPT2E5mFSSfA8UeTPLOtcms5V1w8kp/b/2ciVFlsk/YocL0ZWpRoQPWTMc\n854QqWrDV9MBmUIq6NDQDm9o0J5rpobKnt3LmZigOAXBhUi3PEYqG4hhPWCgZqGG\nbu/HAX/3F4LoGrIIYTSh7D2ljt5P3lHeLN3rUnbLso7btvr8dKTkRjUsha8OVfNl\nKxVNCa6q+m38AbTz2jlFYscBLecZlda+OtV1LzoxNwlIXx3kPY+my2tsAGPfUC30\nBLrPvFvXVFYTSeE8VLMyBkSVKDHjZqUi/JXhshTo7D2R6bNawhFfRTFYrzBkX3+c\n3fEQYLIat974BI7X/P9Vnux7xmDd5tl22mQOe/hD5ZCvRPQXF7TwCCgP/9yU3ftw\noWefeLFUFlYM50hu7fxo\n=rYTz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a6471f1ff0f2bf3aea4c90ff908541b9b3f1552e\nparent f0b198faa220ad90f24713f08acc09d41e4a81de\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784676475 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784676475 -0400\n\ndocs(sdk): explain backend file operation semantics (#4919)\n\nClarifies why file operations are defined on `BackendProtocol` instead\nof only on `SandboxBackendProtocol`, including the behavior these\nspecialized tools provide beyond raw shell execution.","verified_at":"2026-07-21T23:27:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a8e476807cf1da54acecffd3614a0d64e4705e29","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a8e476807cf1da54acecffd3614a0d64e4705e29","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a8e476807cf1da54acecffd3614a0d64e4705e29/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f0b198faa220ad90f24713f08acc09d41e4a81de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f0b198faa220ad90f24713f08acc09d41e4a81de","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f0b198faa220ad90f24713f08acc09d41e4a81de"}]},{"sha":"f0b198faa220ad90f24713f08acc09d41e4a81de","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGYwYjE5OGZhYTIyMGFkOTBmMjQ3MTNmMDhhY2MwOWQ0MWU0YTgxZGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-21T22:32:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T22:32:47Z"},"message":"feat(code): add Hooks v2 execution engine (#4880)\n\nDepends on #4870\n\nHooks v2 can now match configured lifecycle handlers, execute command\nhooks safely, and return typed event-specific decisions.\n\n---\n\nThe engine captures immutable configuration snapshots, projects all nine\nevents onto the compatible wire protocol, bounds subprocess time and\noutput, and reduces ordered results without changing the legacy\ndispatcher. Lifecycle call-site integration remains in a later stack\nlayer.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- 99 focused hook/model compatibility tests\n- `make lint`\n- `make check_imports`\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/019f81f5-89a5-703a-a090-0160871a1091)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/019f81f5-89a5-703a-a090-0160871a1091/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f1ca71171a5074f879385058dcbd7b49dfe3082e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f1ca71171a5074f879385058dcbd7b49dfe3082e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f0b198faa220ad90f24713f08acc09d41e4a81de","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX/OPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVAQQAG6cXuIaR/1WLhutfhFqADad\n3huSTzsjqFVjimt7cEFMi+WmmbxAevDjHzBmTJOw5zA6uyzjs6Wo2eX/dfEBAeyI\nKqSmtDJ0wxUJgvHWr4eI+Fa/D0nkbfdzMkdmRb0NKvIAO8t631fjag8eWYntl4jq\nOIhgcIYZXdOihoMxoNTPqPcUuGgGHOu6IOxZsO0AWk6Okh2k3phQ4yvYM/0JlcV9\nMmEpu1deXQw4/25vvO7Ec289S2wl/93UnRGpfR5BoO/zqhZNLBS16Cml2T5NcTQU\nEpFGSKvoGPkl/gmIFY0W3WFLqZLo2LSJWArZyeUIW/TGQDz0U2jKdULxDVUYU8uU\nWR0hTAxJMqHvMsxPeALGLkThu/DpOj4BA+y/8ZiGhr1dSF0IuuaTeFd1c0+dUY5p\nRdaum1lDEig4vSSps3Jnd+GOlCDTBl9wcHOluTMgVKozJps1iUgYk37zFvfgvp8a\nVjBwhrKTg4NfV1SgDn7u/PsiGkb9BolgN6pF3I2LQdgkIzTvJNu2Qlz6DJvmeYqf\ndh7cbNiHi5wTNw+I2/ERlCmEBWmp803+Kd1OYULBS60FRL9oY5FSdbHkX4j9moEB\nHPTb2JhX5ixQgxu00bG6ceNSv3WikTp1/JiIaBNXUtI/BDlM1iypiqm8GMdNrljl\n4bGIsCNgeeYkgJRWQPZ3\n=N/HC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f1ca71171a5074f879385058dcbd7b49dfe3082e\nparent be1d8ca00f10ed91e68040f8d251990db0626e81\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1784673167 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784673167 -0700\n\nfeat(code): add Hooks v2 execution engine (#4880)\n\nDepends on #4870\n\nHooks v2 can now match configured lifecycle handlers, execute command\nhooks safely, and return typed event-specific decisions.\n\n---\n\nThe engine captures immutable configuration snapshots, projects all nine\nevents onto the compatible wire protocol, bounds subprocess time and\noutput, and reduces ordered results without changing the legacy\ndispatcher. Lifecycle call-site integration remains in a later stack\nlayer.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- 99 focused hook/model compatibility tests\n- `make lint`\n- `make check_imports`\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/019f81f5-89a5-703a-a090-0160871a1091)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/019f81f5-89a5-703a-a090-0160871a1091/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T22:32:48Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f0b198faa220ad90f24713f08acc09d41e4a81de","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f0b198faa220ad90f24713f08acc09d41e4a81de","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f0b198faa220ad90f24713f08acc09d41e4a81de/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"be1d8ca00f10ed91e68040f8d251990db0626e81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/be1d8ca00f10ed91e68040f8d251990db0626e81","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/be1d8ca00f10ed91e68040f8d251990db0626e81"}]},{"sha":"be1d8ca00f10ed91e68040f8d251990db0626e81","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGJlMWQ4Y2EwMGYxMGVkOTFlNjgwNDBmOGQyNTE5OTBkYjA2MjZlODE","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-21T22:26:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T22:26:09Z"},"message":"chore(deps-dev): update setuptools requirement from >=82.0.1 to >=83.0.0 in /examples/async-subagent-server (#4911)\n\nUpdates the requirements on\n[setuptools](https://github.com/pypa/setuptools) to permit the latest\nversion.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/blob/main/NEWS.rst\">setuptools's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>v83.0.0</h1>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Require Python 3.10 or later.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Bugfixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>MANIFEST.in</code> matching (via <code>FileList</code>) is now\ninsensitive to Unicode\nnormalization form. A pattern authored in one form (e.g. NFC, as\ntypically\nsaved by editors) now matches a file whose name is stored on disk in\nanother\n(e.g. NFD, as produced by macOS APFS/HFS+). Previously an\n<code>exclude</code>,\n<code>global-exclude</code>, <code>recursive-exclude</code>, or\n<code>prune</code> rule could silently\nfail to drop a non-ASCII-named file from the source distribution,\npublishing\nit despite the exclusion -- see GHSA-h35f-9h28-mq5c.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Deprecations and Removals</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>pypa/distutils#334</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h1>v82.0.1</h1>\n<h2>Bugfixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix the loading of <code>launcher manifest.xml</code> file. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5047\">#5047</a>)</li>\n<li>Replaced deprecated <code>json.__version__</code> with fixture in\ntests. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5186\">#5186</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Improved Documentation</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add advice about how to improve predictability when installing\nsdists. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5168\">#5168</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Misc</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/4941\">#4941</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5157\">#5157</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5169\">#5169</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5175\">#5175</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>v82.0.0</p>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/6519f728c6f23c992df81a5691ef7655184a20eb\"><code>6519f72</code></a>\nBump version: 82.0.1 → 83.0.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/d1151b125b29a6ee1c7db860f7ee6c365d525b5f\"><code>d1151b1</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5250\">#5250</a>\nfrom pypa/feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2df31e6a741b0fe775969618fe6a3a3d032e900\"><code>a2df31e</code></a>\nCapture removal of dry_run parameter in changelog.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/00144dc3fb6d023fd81cdc26c380a012b084df9b\"><code>00144dc</code></a>\nMoved newsfragment to the release where it occurred.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a4a5a2b160357be77626aa077ddd1d8ee53be50f\"><code>a4a5a2b</code></a>\nAdd news fragment.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/77470c23c35031c9e37d7512694ac5ca52bfcaac\"><code>77470c2</code></a>\nMerge <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/distutils\">https://github.com/pypa/distutils</a>\ninto feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/3c43897420f25a1be1afe6eaa905d056009cc736\"><code>3c43897</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5247\">#5247</a>\nfrom pypa/copilot/fix-pypy-version-issue</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/bb6ea66b4bd01cb35d7c68a1bc61b96d59190269\"><code>bb6ea66</code></a>\nBump PyPy from 3.10 to 3.11 in CI workflow</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2bc3aca2f55eb9b93ea633e58ba68170ce14451\"><code>a2bc3ac</code></a>\nFix broken intersphinx reference to build's installation docs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/2d6a739c64cfedc65e1f635af7b52340aac8d99b\"><code>2d6a739</code></a>\nUse stacked parametrize decorators instead of itertools.product</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/compare/v82.0.1...v83.0.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"8da8bb9cc5a01b0205902ccf433370c0a20294cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/8da8bb9cc5a01b0205902ccf433370c0a20294cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/be1d8ca00f10ed91e68040f8d251990db0626e81","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX/IBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvScQAF2Z12EXQDOWlA+SwgXZU/Gj\nZS+TEl5m00sMgFh//HsVv+3FLjQVXUg/zS9mEAnkAlhji/G6VVe/m7+MTjb4iEue\n1o0pTx3lsIMTmF0ZpXSz0i7WbYaANOK7wqFW332EyRENJf9kI8w+MZFRvPFrMjPq\nDW2CeJ1Vl3Pp5Q5yGsaoJEMXVRlL7/FtO+3L2e7OX4ma6RNv7JGrO+vML+IS5eaO\n/pRag3psE3Aw1Ttw3pqUNVaLcQJ/Am2EJ5la5psaACEXaxYqUjb7CzcI3g1qDYSC\n+K98dfTG+qYRKRnPhAL3zD4CsInpxxzTswQpydH3WhHxrHWefyAVUb0rHE515/fL\nQh8H2wZWLBLw28rBX+ElmtL1iLt1odW8TMX6tCIYIsKc+ps6x/beQHfvxJBSVBCp\nFZwMRlUgiRQ3e5UfGTvIVqHQ5XgGOEqi4LBNvxeV3Ux47TLjeLiYZ+79UVtb/N7T\no8IM5uzYQvcze4nutWxavf/8rKo3YqF8++I0JKP6NTNPEycDx80RcFJS84cYksc2\nf2zAJ3moo1GTG3UgH7TTWjzLKVDysK9D07nhAL/2tkM5Xc9twhZMWV1KwYKlNoan\nL5nzMBrWkZeya0wkokXU/6beeM436/LoXtoWuZ+y+GCZR5HJuw84tmAbA294pfJi\n55FlBff7cfSolXxtdwz2\n=I39F\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8da8bb9cc5a01b0205902ccf433370c0a20294cb\nparent 704f1a53b4a5828c994a07b5976dc2564c27022f\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784672769 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784672769 -0400\n\nchore(deps-dev): update setuptools requirement from >=82.0.1 to >=83.0.0 in /examples/async-subagent-server (#4911)\n\nUpdates the requirements on\n[setuptools](https://github.com/pypa/setuptools) to permit the latest\nversion.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/blob/main/NEWS.rst\">setuptools's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>v83.0.0</h1>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Require Python 3.10 or later.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Bugfixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>MANIFEST.in</code> matching (via <code>FileList</code>) is now\ninsensitive to Unicode\nnormalization form. A pattern authored in one form (e.g. NFC, as\ntypically\nsaved by editors) now matches a file whose name is stored on disk in\nanother\n(e.g. NFD, as produced by macOS APFS/HFS+). Previously an\n<code>exclude</code>,\n<code>global-exclude</code>, <code>recursive-exclude</code>, or\n<code>prune</code> rule could silently\nfail to drop a non-ASCII-named file from the source distribution,\npublishing\nit despite the exclusion -- see GHSA-h35f-9h28-mq5c.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Deprecations and Removals</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>pypa/distutils#334</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h1>v82.0.1</h1>\n<h2>Bugfixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix the loading of <code>launcher manifest.xml</code> file. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5047\">#5047</a>)</li>\n<li>Replaced deprecated <code>json.__version__</code> with fixture in\ntests. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5186\">#5186</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Improved Documentation</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add advice about how to improve predictability when installing\nsdists. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5168\">#5168</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Misc</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/4941\">#4941</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5157\">#5157</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5169\">#5169</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5175\">#5175</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>v82.0.0</p>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/6519f728c6f23c992df81a5691ef7655184a20eb\"><code>6519f72</code></a>\nBump version: 82.0.1 → 83.0.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/d1151b125b29a6ee1c7db860f7ee6c365d525b5f\"><code>d1151b1</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5250\">#5250</a>\nfrom pypa/feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2df31e6a741b0fe775969618fe6a3a3d032e900\"><code>a2df31e</code></a>\nCapture removal of dry_run parameter in changelog.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/00144dc3fb6d023fd81cdc26c380a012b084df9b\"><code>00144dc</code></a>\nMoved newsfragment to the release where it occurred.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a4a5a2b160357be77626aa077ddd1d8ee53be50f\"><code>a4a5a2b</code></a>\nAdd news fragment.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/77470c23c35031c9e37d7512694ac5ca52bfcaac\"><code>77470c2</code></a>\nMerge <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/distutils\">https://github.com/pypa/distutils</a>\ninto feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/3c43897420f25a1be1afe6eaa905d056009cc736\"><code>3c43897</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5247\">#5247</a>\nfrom pypa/copilot/fix-pypy-version-issue</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/bb6ea66b4bd01cb35d7c68a1bc61b96d59190269\"><code>bb6ea66</code></a>\nBump PyPy from 3.10 to 3.11 in CI workflow</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2bc3aca2f55eb9b93ea633e58ba68170ce14451\"><code>a2bc3ac</code></a>\nFix broken intersphinx reference to build's installation docs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/2d6a739c64cfedc65e1f635af7b52340aac8d99b\"><code>2d6a739</code></a>\nUse stacked parametrize decorators instead of itertools.product</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/compare/v82.0.1...v83.0.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T22:26:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/be1d8ca00f10ed91e68040f8d251990db0626e81","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/be1d8ca00f10ed91e68040f8d251990db0626e81","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/be1d8ca00f10ed91e68040f8d251990db0626e81/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"704f1a53b4a5828c994a07b5976dc2564c27022f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/704f1a53b4a5828c994a07b5976dc2564c27022f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/704f1a53b4a5828c994a07b5976dc2564c27022f"}]},{"sha":"704f1a53b4a5828c994a07b5976dc2564c27022f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDcwNGYxYTUzYjRhNTgyOGM5OTRhMDdiNTk3NmRjMjU2NGMyNzAyMmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-21T22:26:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T22:26:04Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump pyasn1 from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4 in /examples/async-subagent-server (#4910)\n\nBumps [pyasn1](https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1) from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/releases\">pyasn1's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Release 0.6.4</h2>\n<p>This is a security release.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders. A small\ncrafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume excessive CPU.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag IDs\nto 20 octets (140 bits). Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate\nto consume excessive CPU and memory.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and CPU\nconsumption in <code>Real.__float__()</code> for values with large\nbase-10 exponents.</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All changes are noted in the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">pyasn1's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Revision 0.6.4, released 08-07-2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders.\nA small crafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume\nexcessive CPU. Arcs are now accumulated in linear time; decoded\nvalues are unchanged (thanks for reporting, tynus2)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag\nIDs to 20 octets (140 bits), matching the OID arc limit introduced\nin 0.6.2. Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate to consume\nexcessive CPU and memory; longer tag IDs are now rejected with\nPyAsn1Error. Also fixed Tag and TagSet repr() failing on huge tag\n(thanks for reporting, mikeappsec)\nIDs due to the integer-to-string conversion limit (Python 3.11+)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and\nCPU consumption in Real.<strong>float</strong>() for values with large\nbase-10\nexponents. Conversion no longer materializes huge intermediate\nintegers; values too large to represent as a Python float raise\nOverflowError promptly, and prettyPrint() renders them as\n'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->' as before. Also fixed base-10 mantissa\nnormalization\nto use exact integer arithmetic; mantissas larger than 2**53\ncould previously lose precision through float division\n(thanks for reporting, gvozdila)</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit\n[pr <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/pull/113\">pyasn1/pyasn1#113</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/72e4803405816c371ed3b2cb4be181c47f038406\"><code>72e4803</code></a>\nPrepare release 0.6.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/0c19eeb853731db1c717ff125ea001a1e558332d\"><code>0c19eeb</code></a>\nPin PyPI publish action to immutable commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/45bdb19eb7df4b3780fe9c912c63e99bffc39dd9\"><code>45bdb19</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/628e36ecbb5277a3f01572ce418ef54271b165a5\"><code>628e36e</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/e60c691cb91addb8fcefa2f537e85ede6fb1e886\"><code>e60c691</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/compare/v0.6.3...v0.6.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"8da8bb9cc5a01b0205902ccf433370c0a20294cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/8da8bb9cc5a01b0205902ccf433370c0a20294cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/704f1a53b4a5828c994a07b5976dc2564c27022f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX/H8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASD4QAAyMeux+rNQ7UriDuvMyTKiL\nC6/vGTVWr4kFYwbRwjfyb/XiLeKpkUjar5gb2b0j6G58jf7EzBQDNGl/1G+0pbGw\nz4kld8a8h7TWUWhpiTRuC6cMHBR0cv0sKRF7OisWiOrUq79issIf2+ao70GKmUse\nplU42eamLtwk8hE753CNTERY+tQ5X+iMcJ/z/MsCEwbu4XG1n7vC3N89ASaJh1AT\n+22PvjnkdvlXab/FySIPDFJl8szu5ipNzPPB0980MkwtwUGI8vgaXNunz5oryt1S\n8nEHhH7+vyZQXuR9Y74sezaJ7ge3zRhV5BXWjtoekT9YguhIwonYZ/SimUGq9Vx0\nVIkT7tjGvN5vEJCB4Qe5KCE7X7Oj0A4FEqy1H6uIsP8EorU4oGSkotM0YZPbnEWG\nTYs1xr/Wr0BMiwYMWwxAKSnOGdJbaK3pSJrZtelt3diuuXd0aaXgKpOm/JUsrRPr\nnkY70d5wevH1GxAOOqwCACU+WuVzlImjjfswEKcbstNWL7JSvD4VC0tCVlBHsVkT\n7ViijWC8AKZ+Wo+TuL7tkOthK2nSiDtFQkkMIzo1W0Wp+vlBeycUfPwRawEGYHOb\nnf3L1lg8WJ4JW3+HfEKLx4RKgvfReGeK/V0wr2SOIfDMD7MDt0DBQVwj5bqN9MWG\n9AKLghNHfpFzWkXTXYO7\n=b7l9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8da8bb9cc5a01b0205902ccf433370c0a20294cb\nparent beededad044612da6e77f8bcdcaf0be5800056e4\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784672764 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784672764 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump pyasn1 from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4 in /examples/async-subagent-server (#4910)\n\nBumps [pyasn1](https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1) from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/releases\">pyasn1's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Release 0.6.4</h2>\n<p>This is a security release.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders. A small\ncrafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume excessive CPU.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag IDs\nto 20 octets (140 bits). Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate\nto consume excessive CPU and memory.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and CPU\nconsumption in <code>Real.__float__()</code> for values with large\nbase-10 exponents.</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All changes are noted in the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">pyasn1's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Revision 0.6.4, released 08-07-2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders.\nA small crafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume\nexcessive CPU. Arcs are now accumulated in linear time; decoded\nvalues are unchanged (thanks for reporting, tynus2)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag\nIDs to 20 octets (140 bits), matching the OID arc limit introduced\nin 0.6.2. Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate to consume\nexcessive CPU and memory; longer tag IDs are now rejected with\nPyAsn1Error. Also fixed Tag and TagSet repr() failing on huge tag\n(thanks for reporting, mikeappsec)\nIDs due to the integer-to-string conversion limit (Python 3.11+)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and\nCPU consumption in Real.<strong>float</strong>() for values with large\nbase-10\nexponents. Conversion no longer materializes huge intermediate\nintegers; values too large to represent as a Python float raise\nOverflowError promptly, and prettyPrint() renders them as\n'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->' as before. Also fixed base-10 mantissa\nnormalization\nto use exact integer arithmetic; mantissas larger than 2**53\ncould previously lose precision through float division\n(thanks for reporting, gvozdila)</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit\n[pr <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/pull/113\">pyasn1/pyasn1#113</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/72e4803405816c371ed3b2cb4be181c47f038406\"><code>72e4803</code></a>\nPrepare release 0.6.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/0c19eeb853731db1c717ff125ea001a1e558332d\"><code>0c19eeb</code></a>\nPin PyPI publish action to immutable commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/45bdb19eb7df4b3780fe9c912c63e99bffc39dd9\"><code>45bdb19</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/628e36ecbb5277a3f01572ce418ef54271b165a5\"><code>628e36e</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/e60c691cb91addb8fcefa2f537e85ede6fb1e886\"><code>e60c691</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/compare/v0.6.3...v0.6.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T22:26:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/704f1a53b4a5828c994a07b5976dc2564c27022f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/704f1a53b4a5828c994a07b5976dc2564c27022f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/704f1a53b4a5828c994a07b5976dc2564c27022f/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","