://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1) from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/releases\">pyasn1's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Release 0.6.4</h2>\n<p>This is a security release.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders. A small\ncrafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume excessive CPU.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag IDs\nto 20 octets (140 bits). Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate\nto consume excessive CPU and memory.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and CPU\nconsumption in <code>Real.__float__()</code> for values with large\nbase-10 exponents.</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All changes are noted in the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">pyasn1's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Revision 0.6.4, released 08-07-2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders.\nA small crafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume\nexcessive CPU. Arcs are now accumulated in linear time; decoded\nvalues are unchanged (thanks for reporting, tynus2)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag\nIDs to 20 octets (140 bits), matching the OID arc limit introduced\nin 0.6.2. Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate to consume\nexcessive CPU and memory; longer tag IDs are now rejected with\nPyAsn1Error. Also fixed Tag and TagSet repr() failing on huge tag\n(thanks for reporting, mikeappsec)\nIDs due to the integer-to-string conversion limit (Python 3.11+)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and\nCPU consumption in Real.<strong>float</strong>() for values with large\nbase-10\nexponents. Conversion no longer materializes huge intermediate\nintegers; values too large to represent as a Python float raise\nOverflowError promptly, and prettyPrint() renders them as\n'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->' as before. Also fixed base-10 mantissa\nnormalization\nto use exact integer arithmetic; mantissas larger than 2**53\ncould previously lose precision through float division\n(thanks for reporting, gvozdila)</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit\n[pr <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/pull/113\">pyasn1/pyasn1#113</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/72e4803405816c371ed3b2cb4be181c47f038406\"><code>72e4803</code></a>\nPrepare release 0.6.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/0c19eeb853731db1c717ff125ea001a1e558332d\"><code>0c19eeb</code></a>\nPin PyPI publish action to immutable commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/45bdb19eb7df4b3780fe9c912c63e99bffc39dd9\"><code>45bdb19</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/628e36ecbb5277a3f01572ce418ef54271b165a5\"><code>628e36e</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/e60c691cb91addb8fcefa2f537e85ede6fb1e886\"><code>e60c691</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/compare/v0.6.3...v0.6.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1c8f05120e13e8bae090b51e657eed25687b7c3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1c8f05120e13e8bae090b51e657eed25687b7c3e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/beededad044612da6e77f8bcdcaf0be5800056e4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX/H2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAosIQAJvDZjF6xEdl7FQ8adMRs7sK\nlB7wI/7HAglsFkwCujcjPG0H6zQ4DoFkyvJRcxN1xIRrPrDyLgGnFIZK4boW0QAL\nqHsjQaQ+FW7aqa8qibDOOshFVCSZC5+tZsdarVfiQNpjUxZLOoOcAiX7JJ8wKiUv\nyh1QhvVH4So/524aTEQy0gsLpIUHfix/n+RcbjdTtTXmYmAhvobrpzZQSDPaYmlz\naBAyocyF8kBb3nptlrdYDjfxGBk1+R/cF3Ti+Sr1KulODojUntaFOVCNeronwLVf\nNGs4duh/nn/3fbecmoeiDrXBSklYFXvf08Vuoh4VM6gLwsWKGb1Rify4qtmGkEI3\nkGNxsjLKAQuDoV1xTBtkzu/M3RXGlKWJ24WaMlIgqxrye+MQPVBuDReiTPOC03rk\n23uSd9EtUj81vHWczYBfJ/8T+ghxZyuj6ZCfW2awsM5Eyh5WJSiXmCGWMohjrkZ8\n+WMvuUzmIn1QzvbX2hbYgo2tX14Ft0xeA4GQrTr7CdsgJZxE3OjzpX89eU8jDr76\nbHZ/uaJlGoauGVdLI3Z26BhMDW8Ur30oxiXM0kobbME5Bg/7Puo+Z6CLiUE5xzys\nUIT4dNrcde7m5ILrDFdX/F0u3ljHQ+3hzQldE7OOMlsIraMON+i5Qj75Sj4KdZSI\nDK12Bepuisz2HyvU5zfJ\n=zOqg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1c8f05120e13e8bae090b51e657eed25687b7c3e\nparent 923d1fae2fa2e77d39a900615728dafaff9929ee\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784672758 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784672758 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump pyasn1 from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4 in /examples/content-builder-agent (#4909)\n\nBumps [pyasn1](https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1) from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/releases\">pyasn1's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Release 0.6.4</h2>\n<p>This is a security release.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders. A small\ncrafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume excessive CPU.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag IDs\nto 20 octets (140 bits). Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate\nto consume excessive CPU and memory.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and CPU\nconsumption in <code>Real.__float__()</code> for values with large\nbase-10 exponents.</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All changes are noted in the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">pyasn1's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Revision 0.6.4, released 08-07-2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders.\nA small crafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume\nexcessive CPU. Arcs are now accumulated in linear time; decoded\nvalues are unchanged (thanks for reporting, tynus2)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag\nIDs to 20 octets (140 bits), matching the OID arc limit introduced\nin 0.6.2. Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate to consume\nexcessive CPU and memory; longer tag IDs are now rejected with\nPyAsn1Error. Also fixed Tag and TagSet repr() failing on huge tag\n(thanks for reporting, mikeappsec)\nIDs due to the integer-to-string conversion limit (Python 3.11+)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and\nCPU consumption in Real.<strong>float</strong>() for values with large\nbase-10\nexponents. Conversion no longer materializes huge intermediate\nintegers; values too large to represent as a Python float raise\nOverflowError promptly, and prettyPrint() renders them as\n'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->' as before. Also fixed base-10 mantissa\nnormalization\nto use exact integer arithmetic; mantissas larger than 2**53\ncould previously lose precision through float division\n(thanks for reporting, gvozdila)</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit\n[pr <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/pull/113\">pyasn1/pyasn1#113</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/72e4803405816c371ed3b2cb4be181c47f038406\"><code>72e4803</code></a>\nPrepare release 0.6.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/0c19eeb853731db1c717ff125ea001a1e558332d\"><code>0c19eeb</code></a>\nPin PyPI publish action to immutable commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/45bdb19eb7df4b3780fe9c912c63e99bffc39dd9\"><code>45bdb19</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/628e36ecbb5277a3f01572ce418ef54271b165a5\"><code>628e36e</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/e60c691cb91addb8fcefa2f537e85ede6fb1e886\"><code>e60c691</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/compare/v0.6.3...v0.6.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T22:25:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/beededad044612da6e77f8bcdcaf0be5800056e4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/beededad044612da6e77f8bcdcaf0be5800056e4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/beededad044612da6e77f8bcdcaf0be5800056e4/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"923d1fae2fa2e77d39a900615728dafaff9929ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/923d1fae2fa2e77d39a900615728dafaff9929ee","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/923d1fae2fa2e77d39a900615728dafaff9929ee"}]},{"sha":"923d1fae2fa2e77d39a900615728dafaff9929ee","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDkyM2QxZmFlMmZhMmU3N2QzOWE5MDA2MTU3MjhkYWZhZmY5OTI5ZWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-21T22:25:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T22:25:53Z"},"message":"chore(deps-dev): bump setuptools from 80.9.0 to 83.0.0 in /examples/deep_research (#4908)\n\nBumps [setuptools](https://github.com/pypa/setuptools) from 80.9.0 to\n83.0.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/blob/main/NEWS.rst\">setuptools's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>v83.0.0</h1>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Require Python 3.10 or later.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Bugfixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>MANIFEST.in</code> matching (via <code>FileList</code>) is now\ninsensitive to Unicode\nnormalization form. A pattern authored in one form (e.g. NFC, as\ntypically\nsaved by editors) now matches a file whose name is stored on disk in\nanother\n(e.g. NFD, as produced by macOS APFS/HFS+). Previously an\n<code>exclude</code>,\n<code>global-exclude</code>, <code>recursive-exclude</code>, or\n<code>prune</code> rule could silently\nfail to drop a non-ASCII-named file from the source distribution,\npublishing\nit despite the exclusion -- see GHSA-h35f-9h28-mq5c.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Deprecations and Removals</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>pypa/distutils#334</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h1>v82.0.1</h1>\n<h2>Bugfixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix the loading of <code>launcher manifest.xml</code> file. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5047\">#5047</a>)</li>\n<li>Replaced deprecated <code>json.__version__</code> with fixture in\ntests. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5186\">#5186</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Improved Documentation</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add advice about how to improve predictability when installing\nsdists. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5168\">#5168</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Misc</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/4941\">#4941</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5157\">#5157</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5169\">#5169</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5175\">#5175</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>v82.0.0</p>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/6519f728c6f23c992df81a5691ef7655184a20eb\"><code>6519f72</code></a>\nBump version: 82.0.1 → 83.0.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/d1151b125b29a6ee1c7db860f7ee6c365d525b5f\"><code>d1151b1</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5250\">#5250</a>\nfrom pypa/feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2df31e6a741b0fe775969618fe6a3a3d032e900\"><code>a2df31e</code></a>\nCapture removal of dry_run parameter in changelog.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/00144dc3fb6d023fd81cdc26c380a012b084df9b\"><code>00144dc</code></a>\nMoved newsfragment to the release where it occurred.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a4a5a2b160357be77626aa077ddd1d8ee53be50f\"><code>a4a5a2b</code></a>\nAdd news fragment.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/77470c23c35031c9e37d7512694ac5ca52bfcaac\"><code>77470c2</code></a>\nMerge <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/distutils\">https://github.com/pypa/distutils</a>\ninto feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/3c43897420f25a1be1afe6eaa905d056009cc736\"><code>3c43897</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5247\">#5247</a>\nfrom pypa/copilot/fix-pypy-version-issue</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/bb6ea66b4bd01cb35d7c68a1bc61b96d59190269\"><code>bb6ea66</code></a>\nBump PyPy from 3.10 to 3.11 in CI workflow</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2bc3aca2f55eb9b93ea633e58ba68170ce14451\"><code>a2bc3ac</code></a>\nFix broken intersphinx reference to build's installation docs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/2d6a739c64cfedc65e1f635af7b52340aac8d99b\"><code>2d6a739</code></a>\nUse stacked parametrize decorators instead of itertools.product</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/compare/v80.9.0...v83.0.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=setuptools&package-manager=uv&previous-version=80.9.0&new-version=83.0.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9b6ad222a5e3b678f4788a09ff6ba12e7f0f33e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9b6ad222a5e3b678f4788a09ff6ba12e7f0f33e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/923d1fae2fa2e77d39a900615728dafaff9929ee","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX/HxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0DwQACFQAmlU504TzNhD/HOVFg1U\nPLjzoPxic2x5pKAIdh9ltGI6MsAsUopX4SI3YAOB4KQY0hn/Oh8zQQPZuYfBBOK4\nTA2pbc9XqyxsDRj6IiQSwNhEdzGcMWcEUxbtjT5RTdfbD7PCPuJ2EjmzRaPNJDjw\nNRl9fNoSb1LOdQThz9CgYmWzU9k9DRzLHqs/KZZZL6rIKx917bctbnydNN3sAZBF\nkV3QIBpcz1n+MNnDJL1aeQlBAkt/bHo62+aK9McRX38GXBEnrwpvqXi7E6Fd0vP9\nFyZEqrEFVkwFq9wZq4Davl7U7dg1b7WHys0FgW26qHIIZlAo8wONUBWlSe+Klx3m\ngtvjUzFTM4+32JldHf0tMsyGHaTAi3y841AGKXosLAF9y64JxnWhclJcc1/NfSIB\nNJAzk7tiQrjT8mD6DixVDRlvwjB/YSBNillMT7M0MSSXRxP+rSZNijiyNFqflL5G\nykiqql3/5cQ4JGj8WwWHaKN/cOK3YLDI07Sft8mi215QHS1HZs0gHQlhaAdR+Ox0\nNf2uFoSFeEbrCu8MwypuJ6Dg/3O+re0grSpYF5PkILcTM4vwdU2W8FSaim2htTIU\nA3/Lgh0rB4Szg/eteHhtF0dzc/0SCD0xZgkEigk+lXu3rVl6TW2HycEXBymQ+uC4\nHHA93sbHSpRTkYrfQ3u8\n=pRP8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9b6ad222a5e3b678f4788a09ff6ba12e7f0f33e8\nparent 5c11851d9c11f71b61bacbc1d3945531872501bc\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784672753 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784672753 -0400\n\nchore(deps-dev): bump setuptools from 80.9.0 to 83.0.0 in /examples/deep_research (#4908)\n\nBumps [setuptools](https://github.com/pypa/setuptools) from 80.9.0 to\n83.0.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/blob/main/NEWS.rst\">setuptools's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>v83.0.0</h1>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Require Python 3.10 or later.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Bugfixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>MANIFEST.in</code> matching (via <code>FileList</code>) is now\ninsensitive to Unicode\nnormalization form. A pattern authored in one form (e.g. NFC, as\ntypically\nsaved by editors) now matches a file whose name is stored on disk in\nanother\n(e.g. NFD, as produced by macOS APFS/HFS+). Previously an\n<code>exclude</code>,\n<code>global-exclude</code>, <code>recursive-exclude</code>, or\n<code>prune</code> rule could silently\nfail to drop a non-ASCII-named file from the source distribution,\npublishing\nit despite the exclusion -- see GHSA-h35f-9h28-mq5c.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Deprecations and Removals</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>pypa/distutils#334</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h1>v82.0.1</h1>\n<h2>Bugfixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix the loading of <code>launcher manifest.xml</code> file. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5047\">#5047</a>)</li>\n<li>Replaced deprecated <code>json.__version__</code> with fixture in\ntests. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5186\">#5186</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Improved Documentation</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add advice about how to improve predictability when installing\nsdists. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5168\">#5168</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Misc</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/4941\">#4941</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5157\">#5157</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5169\">#5169</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5175\">#5175</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>v82.0.0</p>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/6519f728c6f23c992df81a5691ef7655184a20eb\"><code>6519f72</code></a>\nBump version: 82.0.1 → 83.0.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/d1151b125b29a6ee1c7db860f7ee6c365d525b5f\"><code>d1151b1</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5250\">#5250</a>\nfrom pypa/feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2df31e6a741b0fe775969618fe6a3a3d032e900\"><code>a2df31e</code></a>\nCapture removal of dry_run parameter in changelog.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/00144dc3fb6d023fd81cdc26c380a012b084df9b\"><code>00144dc</code></a>\nMoved newsfragment to the release where it occurred.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a4a5a2b160357be77626aa077ddd1d8ee53be50f\"><code>a4a5a2b</code></a>\nAdd news fragment.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/77470c23c35031c9e37d7512694ac5ca52bfcaac\"><code>77470c2</code></a>\nMerge <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/distutils\">https://github.com/pypa/distutils</a>\ninto feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/3c43897420f25a1be1afe6eaa905d056009cc736\"><code>3c43897</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5247\">#5247</a>\nfrom pypa/copilot/fix-pypy-version-issue</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/bb6ea66b4bd01cb35d7c68a1bc61b96d59190269\"><code>bb6ea66</code></a>\nBump PyPy from 3.10 to 3.11 in CI workflow</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2bc3aca2f55eb9b93ea633e58ba68170ce14451\"><code>a2bc3ac</code></a>\nFix broken intersphinx reference to build's installation docs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/2d6a739c64cfedc65e1f635af7b52340aac8d99b\"><code>2d6a739</code></a>\nUse stacked parametrize decorators instead of itertools.product</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/compare/v80.9.0...v83.0.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=setuptools&package-manager=uv&previous-version=80.9.0&new-version=83.0.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T22:25:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/923d1fae2fa2e77d39a900615728dafaff9929ee","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/923d1fae2fa2e77d39a900615728dafaff9929ee","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/923d1fae2fa2e77d39a900615728dafaff9929ee/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5c11851d9c11f71b61bacbc1d3945531872501bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5c11851d9c11f71b61bacbc1d3945531872501bc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5c11851d9c11f71b61bacbc1d3945531872501bc"}]},{"sha":"5c11851d9c11f71b61bacbc1d3945531872501bc","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDVjMTE4NTFkOWMxMWY3MWI2MWJhY2JjMWQzOTQ1NTMxODcyNTAxYmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-21T22:25:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T22:25:44Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump pyasn1 from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4 in /examples/deep_research (#4907)\n\nBumps [pyasn1](https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1) from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/releases\">pyasn1's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Release 0.6.4</h2>\n<p>This is a security release.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders. A small\ncrafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume excessive CPU.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag IDs\nto 20 octets (140 bits). Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate\nto consume excessive CPU and memory.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and CPU\nconsumption in <code>Real.__float__()</code> for values with large\nbase-10 exponents.</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All changes are noted in the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">pyasn1's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Revision 0.6.4, released 08-07-2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders.\nA small crafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume\nexcessive CPU. Arcs are now accumulated in linear time; decoded\nvalues are unchanged (thanks for reporting, tynus2)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag\nIDs to 20 octets (140 bits), matching the OID arc limit introduced\nin 0.6.2. Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate to consume\nexcessive CPU and memory; longer tag IDs are now rejected with\nPyAsn1Error. Also fixed Tag and TagSet repr() failing on huge tag\n(thanks for reporting, mikeappsec)\nIDs due to the integer-to-string conversion limit (Python 3.11+)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and\nCPU consumption in Real.<strong>float</strong>() for values with large\nbase-10\nexponents. Conversion no longer materializes huge intermediate\nintegers; values too large to represent as a Python float raise\nOverflowError promptly, and prettyPrint() renders them as\n'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->' as before. Also fixed base-10 mantissa\nnormalization\nto use exact integer arithmetic; mantissas larger than 2**53\ncould previously lose precision through float division\n(thanks for reporting, gvozdila)</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit\n[pr <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/pull/113\">pyasn1/pyasn1#113</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/72e4803405816c371ed3b2cb4be181c47f038406\"><code>72e4803</code></a>\nPrepare release 0.6.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/0c19eeb853731db1c717ff125ea001a1e558332d\"><code>0c19eeb</code></a>\nPin PyPI publish action to immutable commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/45bdb19eb7df4b3780fe9c912c63e99bffc39dd9\"><code>45bdb19</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/628e36ecbb5277a3f01572ce418ef54271b165a5\"><code>628e36e</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/e60c691cb91addb8fcefa2f537e85ede6fb1e886\"><code>e60c691</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/compare/v0.6.3...v0.6.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e8838754ff2ab125597db3f7df2c629a49f3f735","url":"h