d BER long-form tag IDs\nto 20 octets (140 bits). Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate\nto consume excessive CPU and memory.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and CPU\nconsumption in <code>Real.__float__()</code> for values with large\nbase-10 exponents.</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All changes are noted in the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">pyasn1's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Revision 0.6.4, released 08-07-2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders.\nA small crafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume\nexcessive CPU. Arcs are now accumulated in linear time; decoded\nvalues are unchanged (thanks for reporting, tynus2)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag\nIDs to 20 octets (140 bits), matching the OID arc limit introduced\nin 0.6.2. Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate to consume\nexcessive CPU and memory; longer tag IDs are now rejected with\nPyAsn1Error. Also fixed Tag and TagSet repr() failing on huge tag\n(thanks for reporting, mikeappsec)\nIDs due to the integer-to-string conversion limit (Python 3.11+)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and\nCPU consumption in Real.<strong>float</strong>() for values with large\nbase-10\nexponents. Conversion no longer materializes huge intermediate\nintegers; values too large to represent as a Python float raise\nOverflowError promptly, and prettyPrint() renders them as\n'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->' as before. Also fixed base-10 mantissa\nnormalization\nto use exact integer arithmetic; mantissas larger than 2**53\ncould previously lose precision through float division\n(thanks for reporting, gvozdila)</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit\n[pr <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/pull/113\">pyasn1/pyasn1#113</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/72e4803405816c371ed3b2cb4be181c47f038406\"><code>72e4803</code></a>\nPrepare release 0.6.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/0c19eeb853731db1c717ff125ea001a1e558332d\"><code>0c19eeb</code></a>\nPin PyPI publish action to immutable commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/45bdb19eb7df4b3780fe9c912c63e99bffc39dd9\"><code>45bdb19</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/628e36ecbb5277a3f01572ce418ef54271b165a5\"><code>628e36e</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/e60c691cb91addb8fcefa2f537e85ede6fb1e886\"><code>e60c691</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/compare/v0.6.3...v0.6.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T22:25:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5da48d32b71026d28d13f0846dd673aa6f927649","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5da48d32b71026d28d13f0846dd673aa6f927649","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5da48d32b71026d28d13f0846dd673aa6f927649/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"94fd4a8be0e272c9f31f0feac4a86a544d41d665","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/94fd4a8be0e272c9f31f0feac4a86a544d41d665","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/94fd4a8be0e272c9f31f0feac4a86a544d41d665"}]},{"sha":"94fd4a8be0e272c9f31f0feac4a86a544d41d665","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDk0ZmQ0YThiZTBlMjcyYzlmMzFmMGZlYWM0YTg2YTU0NGQ0MWQ2NjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-21T22:25:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T22:25:03Z"},"message":"chore(deps-dev): update setuptools requirement from >=82.0.1 to >=83.0.0 in /examples/text-to-sql-agent (#4901)\n\nUpdates the requirements on\n[setuptools](https://github.com/pypa/setuptools) to permit the latest\nversion.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/blob/main/NEWS.rst\">setuptools's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>v83.0.0</h1>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Require Python 3.10 or later.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Bugfixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>MANIFEST.in</code> matching (via <code>FileList</code>) is now\ninsensitive to Unicode\nnormalization form. A pattern authored in one form (e.g. NFC, as\ntypically\nsaved by editors) now matches a file whose name is stored on disk in\nanother\n(e.g. NFD, as produced by macOS APFS/HFS+). Previously an\n<code>exclude</code>,\n<code>global-exclude</code>, <code>recursive-exclude</code>, or\n<code>prune</code> rule could silently\nfail to drop a non-ASCII-named file from the source distribution,\npublishing\nit despite the exclusion -- see GHSA-h35f-9h28-mq5c.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Deprecations and Removals</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>pypa/distutils#334</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h1>v82.0.1</h1>\n<h2>Bugfixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix the loading of <code>launcher manifest.xml</code> file. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5047\">#5047</a>)</li>\n<li>Replaced deprecated <code>json.__version__</code> with fixture in\ntests. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5186\">#5186</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Improved Documentation</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add advice about how to improve predictability when installing\nsdists. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5168\">#5168</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Misc</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/4941\">#4941</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5157\">#5157</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5169\">#5169</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5175\">#5175</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>v82.0.0</p>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/6519f728c6f23c992df81a5691ef7655184a20eb\"><code>6519f72</code></a>\nBump version: 82.0.1 → 83.0.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/d1151b125b29a6ee1c7db860f7ee6c365d525b5f\"><code>d1151b1</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5250\">#5250</a>\nfrom pypa/feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2df31e6a741b0fe775969618fe6a3a3d032e900\"><code>a2df31e</code></a>\nCapture removal of dry_run parameter in changelog.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/00144dc3fb6d023fd81cdc26c380a012b084df9b\"><code>00144dc</code></a>\nMoved newsfragment to the release where it occurred.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a4a5a2b160357be77626aa077ddd1d8ee53be50f\"><code>a4a5a2b</code></a>\nAdd news fragment.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/77470c23c35031c9e37d7512694ac5ca52bfcaac\"><code>77470c2</code></a>\nMerge <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/distutils\">https://github.com/pypa/distutils</a>\ninto feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/3c43897420f25a1be1afe6eaa905d056009cc736\"><code>3c43897</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5247\">#5247</a>\nfrom pypa/copilot/fix-pypy-version-issue</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/bb6ea66b4bd01cb35d7c68a1bc61b96d59190269\"><code>bb6ea66</code></a>\nBump PyPy from 3.10 to 3.11 in CI workflow</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2bc3aca2f55eb9b93ea633e58ba68170ce14451\"><code>a2bc3ac</code></a>\nFix broken intersphinx reference to build's installation docs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/2d6a739c64cfedc65e1f635af7b52340aac8d99b\"><code>2d6a739</code></a>\nUse stacked parametrize decorators instead of itertools.product</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/compare/v82.0.1...v83.0.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"2d1d4e9f1fe9814c72b4f9fb896ccce8a12e1edc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2d1d4e9f1fe9814c72b4f9fb896ccce8a12e1edc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/94fd4a8be0e272c9f31f0feac4a86a544d41d665","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX/G/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWRsQACPeJex+gYc4hWuI1e0oYVrf\nHipqQIbHoX8oOjs1+bKjDy5toGpvvKXPmzks1bHg+Abahu30xFuqB0b2wCdp5Rs5\n30csudJWqYO2lvULLN/8uNi5T6JAYTPvDTudP7eEe9h9g7ccsA1TCXkE6T/g2IJR\ntEqYrbU6pnLg1m1YUkF29vMbwcylUZpS8HLKgaflNbvv9WlpK1Gvg3uOzrmQWffa\noRSHGkQll7pOLMG/ILKcQa8XpORQxruQFOxsfKZMeRLzTKxLqcU+fNRSFxsJqV9K\nVVjEeZ/KrGdKAWQ/3U3skXZF/1oAuSnifiFw/hCXVers5FBbUoI2up+y3pG1Tk3Z\nPQZHMBTj61Yt31HpkOM+fuC9oS63s0Hux8yRFO4QYNB1wMVzBVU27FFlma7NTYwc\nAlMgNeC7sVPewsVxWbBUM8hBqdwQysI9FBOnE6jDfcXTZrMp5Syf8KIFHuBrwIEU\nEy7b0Z6q7WBjNjRSYqi0jJoC/jByvaYRVlIDdJeNpHs6akRm1E+jszNZCdN/3zii\ngJPcXiq26sRzBIollXPw0xV507WaDYm48sfEbvghh4MDK7ImunP+ru2bO+IlNFbB\nuMRJCI1vJ0WbQL0ylOj2ppObE1/NkZeNvGm6FKeKYDQUjgh9izK/uDhVTKKauY2q\nbOKo/tR1Lmk4/jN6ebYX\n=/yjW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2d1d4e9f1fe9814c72b4f9fb896ccce8a12e1edc\nparent 4571bbd23417380cfbdc23ecf7f1c1e38c805225\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784672703 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784672703 -0400\n\nchore(deps-dev): update setuptools requirement from >=82.0.1 to >=83.0.0 in /examples/text-to-sql-agent (#4901)\n\nUpdates the requirements on\n[setuptools](https://github.com/pypa/setuptools) to permit the latest\nversion.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/blob/main/NEWS.rst\">setuptools's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>v83.0.0</h1>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Require Python 3.10 or later.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Bugfixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>MANIFEST.in</code> matching (via <code>FileList</code>) is now\ninsensitive to Unicode\nnormalization form. A pattern authored in one form (e.g. NFC, as\ntypically\nsaved by editors) now matches a file whose name is stored on disk in\nanother\n(e.g. NFD, as produced by macOS APFS/HFS+). Previously an\n<code>exclude</code>,\n<code>global-exclude</code>, <code>recursive-exclude</code>, or\n<code>prune</code> rule could silently\nfail to drop a non-ASCII-named file from the source distribution,\npublishing\nit despite the exclusion -- see GHSA-h35f-9h28-mq5c.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Deprecations and Removals</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>pypa/distutils#334</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h1>v82.0.1</h1>\n<h2>Bugfixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix the loading of <code>launcher manifest.xml</code> file. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5047\">#5047</a>)</li>\n<li>Replaced deprecated <code>json.__version__</code> with fixture in\ntests. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5186\">#5186</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Improved Documentation</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add advice about how to improve predictability when installing\nsdists. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5168\">#5168</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Misc</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/4941\">#4941</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5157\">#5157</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5169\">#5169</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5175\">#5175</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>v82.0.0</p>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/6519f728c6f23c992df81a5691ef7655184a20eb\"><code>6519f72</code></a>\nBump version: 82.0.1 → 83.0.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/d1151b125b29a6ee1c7db860f7ee6c365d525b5f\"><code>d1151b1</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5250\">#5250</a>\nfrom pypa/feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2df31e6a741b0fe775969618fe6a3a3d032e900\"><code>a2df31e</code></a>\nCapture removal of dry_run parameter in changelog.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/00144dc3fb6d023fd81cdc26c380a012b084df9b\"><code>00144dc</code></a>\nMoved newsfragment to the release where it occurred.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a4a5a2b160357be77626aa077ddd1d8ee53be50f\"><code>a4a5a2b</code></a>\nAdd news fragment.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/77470c23c35031c9e37d7512694ac5ca52bfcaac\"><code>77470c2</code></a>\nMerge <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/distutils\">https://github.com/pypa/distutils</a>\ninto feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/3c43897420f25a1be1afe6eaa905d056009cc736\"><code>3c43897</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5247\">#5247</a>\nfrom pypa/copilot/fix-pypy-version-issue</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/bb6ea66b4bd01cb35d7c68a1bc61b96d59190269\"><code>bb6ea66</code></a>\nBump PyPy from 3.10 to 3.11 in CI workflow</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2bc3aca2f55eb9b93ea633e58ba68170ce14451\"><code>a2bc3ac</code></a>\nFix broken intersphinx reference to build's installation docs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/2d6a739c64cfedc65e1f635af7b52340aac8d99b\"><code>2d6a739</code></a>\nUse stacked parametrize decorators instead of itertools.product</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/compare/v82.0.1...v83.0.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T22:25:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/94fd4a8be0e272c9f31f0feac4a86a544d41d665","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/94fd4a8be0e272c9f31f0feac4a86a544d41d665","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/94fd4a8be0e272c9f31f0feac4a86a544d41d665/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4571bbd23417380cfbdc23ecf7f1c1e38c805225","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4571bbd23417380cfbdc23ecf7f1c1e38c805225","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4571bbd23417380cfbdc23ecf7f1c1e38c805225"}]},{"sha":"4571bbd23417380cfbdc23ecf7f1c1e38c805225","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQ1NzFiYmQyMzQxNzM4MGNmYmRjMjNlY2Y3ZjFjMWUzOGM4MDUyMjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-21T22:24:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T22:24:44Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump pyasn1 from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4 in /libs/acp (#4900)\n\nBumps [pyasn1](https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1) from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/releases\">pyasn1's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Release 0.6.4</h2>\n<p>This is a security release.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders. A small\ncrafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume excessive CPU.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag IDs\nto 20 octets (140 bits). Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate\nto consume excessive CPU and memory.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and CPU\nconsumption in <code>Real.__float__()</code> for values with large\nbase-10 exponents.</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All changes are noted in the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">pyasn1's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Revision 0.6.4, released 08-07-2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders.\nA small crafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume\nexcessive CPU. Arcs are now accumulated in linear time; decoded\nvalues are unchanged (thanks for reporting, tynus2)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag\nIDs to 20 octets (140 bits), matching the OID arc limit introduced\nin 0.6.2. Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate to consume\nexcessive CPU and memory; longer tag IDs are now rejected with\nPyAsn1Error. Also fixed Tag and TagSet repr() failing on huge tag\n(thanks for reporting, mikeappsec)\nIDs due to the integer-to-string conversion limit (Python 3.11+)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and\nCPU consumption in Real.<strong>float</strong>() for values with large\nbase-10\nexponents. Conversion no longer materializes huge intermediate\nintegers; values too large to represent as a Python float raise\nOverflowError promptly, and prettyPrint() renders them as\n'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->' as before. Also fixed base-10 mantissa\nnormalization\nto use exact integer arithmetic; mantissas larger than 2**53\ncould previously lose precision through float division\n(thanks for reporting, gvozdila)</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit\n[pr <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/pull/113\">pyasn1/pyasn1#113</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/72e4803405816c371ed3b2cb4be181c47f038406\"><code>72e4803</code></a>\nPrepare release 0.6.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/0c19eeb853731db1c717ff125ea001a1e558332d\"><code>0c19eeb</code></a>\nPin PyPI publish action to immutable commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/45bdb19eb7df4b3780fe9c912c63e99bffc39dd9\"><code>45bdb19</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/628e36ecbb5277a3f01572ce418ef54271b165a5\"><code>628e36e</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/e60c691cb91addb8fcefa2f537e85ede6fb1e886\"><code>e60c691</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/compare/v0.6.3...v0.6.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"aa03f2f5b70e9dc059a078775b0efa11c35b4bd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/aa03f2f5b70e9dc059a078775b0efa11c35b4bd1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4571bbd23417380cfbdc23ecf7f1c1e38c805225","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX/GsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAj3QQAFSCZKW7yvbok296WTdMe3/c\ndUGTl1AVe6cDVhUJW0FgwoTECDraaQ3tbULVjCEEBSaV/8Zmtg18Dl1Vc8IX/tR/\nWUeeysp8V1vaaYn4+l9lEZLMHpliRoSsSMiNOaVnG1EYBZWSdRFw8TnM4TgMXAAE\nqiwByTJVnLA6ma5WkvoP1uwgr+S6aNzaqfnd7BEVBSotrXk+7sj4X/ObiZXTVBPY\nEjvScU4jRC8rzcoLMEeQctw++eNNm8yk81BVBzTFBulbhzQqtcjulRRIcF9KIpOK\n3D8DvqDnkvdjlLyRxBEPYgds6CFc2L/RcBi4QJhtH5gsTvBm8f9U7jIq1cfWKTzy\nYjElwpKCKaY2CuMzRE/Tludun6Yod4WAV67/GX5MI+jv2bFoN5zGETIGqR+NTt8m\nv7u9FzCjpXrG+cnfJQOM6NeBiG7e3NkZM2qyiW5cyEwyq7JPOxHARcBVfoZZaZqL\ntwGHWKqI/ans9va197kjMPlh7wGsluAg5rr07u2PVWEFggfXi41zg8ivfHqjOsOI\ngD6VkHlEumATcS/isz+rYH1u2dMd0ABnhXlhJ1DXElv+wtrnIg2cf++AQ5M9Iao7\nalZ9TkNnZUzrdNWMnsZ3AVEmiwieELl9vYq6LSUSa5/7BNSSww0TiiEOp/XvwBKx\nbp2faFt3MeYNdtqaBpES\n=MnXL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree aa03f2f5b70e9dc059a078775b0efa11c35b4bd1\nparent 9e8d478e2d1a8c50d77a121a2ccd51b584e0841d\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784672684 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784672684 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump pyasn1 from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4 in /libs/acp (#4900)\n\nBumps [pyasn1](https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1) from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/releases\">pyasn1's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Release 0.6.4</h2>\n<p>This is a security release.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders. A small\ncrafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume excessive CPU.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag IDs\nto 20 octets (140 bits). Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate\nto consume excessive CPU and memory.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and CPU\nconsumption in <code>Real.__float__()</code> for values with large\nbase-10 exponents.</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All changes are noted in the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">pyasn1's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Revision 0.6.4, released 08-07-2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders.\nA small crafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume\nexcessive CPU. Arcs are now accumulated in linear time; decoded\nvalues are unchanged (thanks for reporting, tynus2)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag\nIDs to 20 octets (140 bits), matching the OID arc limit introduced\nin 0.6.2. Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate to consume\nexcessive CPU and memory; longer tag IDs are now rejected with\nPyAsn1Error. Also fixed Tag and TagSet repr() failing on huge tag\n(thanks for reporting, mikeappsec)\nIDs due to the integer-to-string conversion limit (Python 3.11+)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and\nCPU consumption in Real.<strong>float</strong>() for values with large\nbase-10\nexponents. Conversion no longer materializes huge intermediate\nintegers; values too large to represent as a Python float raise\nOverflowError promptly, and prettyPrint() renders them as\n'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->' as before. Also fixed base-10 mantissa\nnormalization\nto use exact integer arithmetic; mantissas larger than 2**53\ncould previously lose precision through float division\n(thanks for reporting, gvozdila)</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit\n[pr <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/pull/113\">pyasn1/pyasn1#113</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/72e4803405816c371ed3b2cb4be181c47f038406\"><code>72e4803</code></a>\nPrepare release 0.6.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/0c19eeb853731db1c717ff125ea001a1e558332d\"><code>0c19eeb</code></a>\nPin PyPI publish action to immutable commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/45bdb19eb7df4b3780fe9c912c63e99bffc39dd9\"><code>45bdb19</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/628e36ecbb5277a3f01572ce418ef54271b165a5\"><code>628e36e</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/e60c691cb91addb8fcefa2f537e85ede6fb1e886\"><code>e60c691</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/compare/v0.6.3...v0.6.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T22:24:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4571bbd23417380cfbdc23ecf7f1c1e38c805225","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4571bbd23417380cfbdc23ecf7f1c1e38c805225","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4571bbd23417380cfbdc23ecf7f1c1e38c805225/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9e8d478e2d1a8c50d77a121a2ccd51b584e0841d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9e8d478e2d1a8c50d77a121a2ccd51b584e0841d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9e8d478e2d1a8c50d77a121a2ccd51b584e0841d"}]},{"sha":"9e8d478e2d1a8c50d77a121a2ccd51b584e0841d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDllOGQ0NzhlMmQxYThjNTBkNzdhMTIxYTJjY2Q1MWI1ODRlMDg0MWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Hunter Lovell","email":"40191806+hntrl@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-21T21:49:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T21:49:29Z"},"message":"refactor(sdk): extract prompt caching helpers (#4892)\n\nCleans up caching middleware logic from `graph.py`, slimming it down\n\n---\n\nExtract provider-specific prompt-caching construction from the Deep\nAgents graph module into a dedicated middleware helper. This gives\nmain-agent and subagent stack assembly a shared prompt-caching\nimplementation without coupling either path to `graph.py`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add `deepagents.middleware._prompt_caching` with the Anthropic,\nBedrock, and Fireworks prompt-caching helpers.\n- Replace graph-local helper definitions with the shared append helper.\n- Update prompt-caching tests to target the extracted helper module\nwhile preserving graph-level wiring coverage.","tree":{"sha":"5adee8dea23901b114bbe545b4a32e383452b753","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5adee8dea23901b114bbe545b4a32e383452b753"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9e8d478e2d1a8c50d77a121a2ccd51b584e0841d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX+lqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA44UQAEKE7rH0/JDdmQ+LFaO7bY8F\n7dCU6ZJv6Zk5VUDyJHikYNWBcPKadmoBHHD0O1FEGtQI/rq7uJ3qYNHJ5XDxKaSh\nwVovyGO1P+2yaRT4aFC/AmVh/OBf95eQJE2dCF2oZP8LESkO7f68q9HivNLfKuA0\noL7MCYYqPZISC0BciS/dGN+csdGTsUhmkM/DqDdQcGzREy3Lfu5CNXIQVjNplvdX\naWI2i1kfpTkJ9ZQoCRJQf0RL07Dg1I8r4rCyFGMgjyvTU3ZZ1nhAV86GEwfKq0Bu\nN9+7k8NwSLAPHxh2BT9W35C7ua/8LU/eO21QNzv/rCnfv8FBbxS5W0bh1oiQ4me/\neIl42/xatKa0BdqmZYgQ4sqlWw3xPd3N7QT1BPQ4tvGfxffbmc1aF4rh4C5aUvjX\nSb5Jb7YEx+VPKn0SRcGzVIPucPvEgGBsXVXJWB5XuNUZKM5Wixeq1lZiXnebswh5\nNhOvAeBqNPKJi24F5BS99VAijhWmz4t1Op2Lvfw393oxKiJ3PePsLLMuLUsHA9zH\nhbtb5AtlD4e8ApqXpLVRrwr9H1zQD5yMvCbOlS2PpXbdJIOy7T9Q0jlqeD39qM6A\n3+GPs3yxj1phP43CjT88Ls3VxL5GtlYuS7PpI5PFKhYQVHfh3U7cLMWpHuujNzn8\nwB4oWCdx09QIDat4au2e\n=dl5o\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5adee8dea23901b114bbe545b4a32e383452b753\nparent 09670121b8d20fa8029804143852f6fcc6135dba\nauthor Hunter Lovell <40191806+hntrl@users.noreply.github.com> 1784670569 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784670569 -0400\n\nrefactor(sdk): extract prompt caching helpers (#4892)\n\nCleans up caching middleware logic from `graph.py`, slimming it down\n\n---\n\nExtract provider-specific prompt-caching construction from the Deep\nAgents graph module into a dedicated middleware helper. This gives\nmain-agent and subagent stack assembly a shared prompt-caching\nimplementation without coupling either path to `graph.py`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add `deepagents.middleware._prompt_caching` with the Anthropic,\nBedrock, and Fireworks prompt-caching helpers.\n- Replace graph-local helper definitions with the shared append helper.\n- Update prompt-caching tests to target the extracted helper module\nwhile preserving graph-level wiring coverage.","verified_at":"2026-07-21T21:49:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9e8d478e2d1a8c50d77a121a2ccd51b584e0841d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9e8d478e2d1a8c50d77a121a2ccd51b584e0841d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9e8d478e2d1a8c50d77a121a2ccd51b584e0841d/comments","author":{"login":"hntrl","id":40191806,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMTkxODA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40191806?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl","html_url":"https://github.com/hntrl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"09670121b8d20fa8029804143852f6fcc6135dba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/09670121b8d20fa8029804143852f6fcc6135dba","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/09670121b8d20fa8029804143852f6fcc6135dba"}]},{"sha":"09670121b8d20fa8029804143852f6fcc6135dba","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDA5NjcwMTIxYjhkMjBmYTgwMjk4MDQxNDM4NTJmNmZjYzYxMzVkYmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-21T21:01:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T21:01:17Z"},"message":"feat(code): add typed hooks data models (#4870)\n\nIntroduces the typed domain and wire contracts that future dcode hook\nexecution will build on. This PR does not integrate lifecycle events or\nexecute the new hook protocol.\n\nDesign: https://app.notion.com/p/3a3808527b17808ea4f9e0074d705dc4\n\n---\n\n- Adds discriminated domain events and event-specific decisions for all\nnine MVP hook events.\n- Adds compatible wire input/output, permission update, command\nconfiguration, and versioned transport models with cached Pydantic\nadapters.\n- Adds shared recursive JSON validation and exact-key contract coverage.\n- Moves the existing fire-and-forget dispatcher to `hooks.legacy`\nwithout changing its public imports, making room for the new package.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `make lint`\n- `make check_imports`\n- Hooks model and legacy compatibility tests: 84 passed\n- Full unit suite: 10,105 passed; 3 unrelated terminal-width assertions\nfail locally because Rich resolves the test consoles to width 80\n\n</details>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d2c210aae1163d9a64e95bee7a31f2a72ee799de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d2c210aae1163d9a64e95bee7a31f2a72ee799de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/09670121b8d20fa8029804143852f6fcc6135dba","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX94dCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnjEQABASLBbufKUINYSQtplba8ug\ndL0Lvgv9QZ02JcI7YabSXo0WDYQAJVBDt0ExR5OOfKAHCITUiqNYjt8W4c8SXGCY\nOwxZtr1yWYfZbUrtVZRh8LR1RmAacUmfrygjSSxku9h95XX2U9ND92fgUPl6drTs\nid86qUtiZRglHlWwpJSrJbBbEAhujHylFssVUM4oyujPaZXpcHpzKsmwsreQddrj\nxYmzd0sDLElYpZ8vH2491wsXCMGw2qUtBvChpERjzodk6OpOv/x8wZRP4HLvvQvw\nMIqXYcMggjP+vGQmrHJX6wd8BfKFUSanklWqHgr1xfq0zqJ3Bb0tiErp3S2u/rAE\noyzeVBMAFIS2GsoOm0qaFzpYErStLzY/UQarC1rAUCqv3Nm2bWNhufWKTRf32aAM\nCYvuaMahz9owhkTim1CH3VgvOGM7im40zL8VBIQxg0NgFh3cdPaES5Br6MYg2GsM\nWxec62pthhlDDcLOTu0y5+pCCO3Dv+YDfGmhjCFNpYKhIZN51T6hHklyeAV7Vtem\nrNMBcjmXaa2h9Ey6KG0VdRvj8HEWXR4In3KNMhBshuPxcRJjpz5MPKZx4eIsdpfJ\nXRMYFiFNgUQB1HsvZtg+wxW55EOP0wOONrIYf2sBJ3TnaHP2In+LKSswVVEW4N9Z\nXEaLW33Z09vYABxbE1g6\n=ksyd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d2c210aae1163d9a64e95bee7a31f2a72ee799de\nparent d0e148a72612137fc7bc1e49a8972643e0ca2c28\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1784667677 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784667677 +0000\n\nfeat(code): add typed hooks data models (#4870)\n\nIntroduces the typed domain and wire contracts that future dcode hook\nexecution will build on. This PR does not integrate lifecycle events or\nexecute the new hook protocol.\n\nDesign: https://app.notion.com/p/3a3808527b17808ea4f9e0074d705dc4\n\n---\n\n- Adds discriminated domain events and event-specific decisions for all\nnine MVP hook events.\n- Adds compatible wire input/output, permission update, command\nconfiguration, and versioned transport models with cached Pydantic\nadapters.\n- Adds shared recursive JSON validation and exact-key contract coverage.\n- Moves the existing fire-and-forget dispatcher to `hooks.legacy`\nwithout changing its public imports, making room for the new package.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `make lint`\n- `make check_imports`\n- Hooks model and legacy compatibility tests: 84 passed\n- Full unit suite: 10,105 passed; 3 unrelated terminal-width assertions\nfail locally because Rich resolves the test consoles to width 80\n\n</details>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T21:01:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/09670121b8d20fa8029804143852f6fcc6135dba","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/09670121b8d20fa8029804143852f6fcc6135dba","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/09670121b8d20fa8029804143852f6fcc6135dba/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d0e148a72612137fc7bc1e49a8972643e0ca2c28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d0e148a72612137fc7bc1e49a8972643e0ca2c28","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d0e148a72612137fc7bc1e49a8972643e0ca2c28"}]},{"sha":"d0e148a72612137fc7bc1e49a8972643e0ca2c28","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQwZTE0OGE3MjYxMjEzN2ZjN2JjMWU0OWE4OTcyNjQzZTBjYTJjMjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-21T20:48:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T20:48:21Z"},"message":"fix(code): show `-m` prompt as queued immediately on startup (#4861)\n\nRunning `dcode -m \"hello\"` now shows the message as queued right away\nwhile the server connects, instead of the transcript staying empty until\nconnection completes. This matches the immediate feedback you get typing\ninto an already-running session mid-reconnect.\n\n---\n\nPreviously a `-m`/`--message` prompt was stashed in `_initial_prompt`\nand only submitted after `ServerReady` fired, so the user saw nothing\nduring the connect window. Now, during a fresh (non-`-r`) connect,\n`on_mount` mounts a `QueuedUserMessage` placeholder for the prompt\n(dismissing the startup tip and revealing the connection status, exactly\nlike the typed-while-connecting path). When the session-start sequence\ndispatches the initial submission, the placeholder is removed and\nreplaced by the real user message.\n\nResume (`-r`) is intentionally excluded because that path bulk-loads\nhistory on connect, which would briefly render the placeholder above the\nrestored transcript. The status-bar queued count includes the\nplaceholder so it reads `1` while pending.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/9d01dcfe-8985-e5ff-fd19-9e25c7d4943c)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6062ec8ccddf1794ecfe3f8dfb0be15265035d44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6062ec8ccddf1794ecfe3f8dfb0be15265035d44"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d0e148a72612137fc7bc1e49a8972643e0ca2c28","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX9sVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4aYQAFOKHnF+UNAMKmG7zWEdpJbJ\nTZOYa9FjXbbKJ4PNePrB/1rAy1bIIPs7Q7KKVZTsdScSkjWfYjee6q6B38MvuPdR\nOvjaFp9NY/pei6zKzKQeaGXM31vTIRX4rx6D3QUcaskG86j9tc39xGYjwMf/C7eM\nvnJ9IZ4KZoIbAYv1I1edYxE4Nk3OjFtZx7/VwW4H4XtWPWEbcxSiClvKLVabbjBX\ndmM2EvM83NZ8ffvjHKZXeuR/hHN2KVFZ/kKoBHYAoztcYZHatAQoC3kYKlTXG86t\n/xmqsainq415iwsbA87QQf6PHrnVaH2rZ4T7JVUzh23gKog36O4+iWA+HdimzcSG\nPyd68ZwLzILx9+AqHyZJBM6iLPJU2bCGiz11PPVNZae6X89iq7HZ9zsX7OqdTwNG\n9VlVcDOEq6BvE+Gbly1oPCtvKZK6ErwxeSxSmrq9pxW07qRjX7AMDTM3mUZIeuHz\nzrlRND7ZgDMrQ3cgq0exldwuQCheQevOYGykF0xiBTu4X+LDwDwxAmFaqnrE5XIb\n39DeeKcybW3ZEK+6x48400g8+GDjINYYP5twWcRxgdAT6nWnjZ6CJ7W+0HWiVGPu\nzZLGkeWQgh8te1KaQtQqjG6HuvfcagqVxpbg0RahBk90vCoc8ILhYTkU3BF+nM0j\nCaLUDlSxabx2z1HbaQug\n=yZVf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6062ec8ccddf1794ecfe3f8dfb0be15265035d44\nparent 89822e105b42840e079e19f905c8f4abe2604750\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784666901 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784666901 -0400\n\nfix(code): show `-m` prompt as queued immediately on startup (#4861)\n\nRunning `dcode -m \"hello\"` now shows the message as queued right away\nwhile the server connects, instead of the transcript staying empty until\nconnection completes. This matches the immediate feedback you get typing\ninto an already-running session mid-reconnect.\n\n---\n\nPreviously a `-m`/`--message` prompt was stashed in `_initial_prompt`\nand only submitted after `ServerReady` fired, so the user saw nothing\nduring the connect window. Now, during a fresh (non-`-r`) connect,\n`on_mount` mounts a `QueuedUserMessage` placeholder for the prompt\n(dismissing the startup tip and revealing the connection status, exactly\nlike the typed-while-connecting path). When the session-start sequence\ndispatches the initial submission, the placeholder is removed and\nreplaced by the real user message.\n\nResume (`-r`) is intentionally excluded because that path bulk-loads\nhistory on connect, which would briefly render the placeholder above the\nrestored transcript. The status-bar queued count includes the\nplaceholder so it reads `1` while pending.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/9d01dcfe-8985-e5ff-fd19-9e25c7d4943c)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T20:48:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d0e148a72612137fc7bc1e49a8972643e0ca2c28","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d0e148a72612137fc7bc1e49a8972643e0ca2c28","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d0e148a72612137fc7bc1e49a8972643e0ca2c28/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"89822e105b42840e079e19f905c8f4abe2604750","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/89822e105b42840e079e19f905c8f4abe2604750","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/89822e105b42840e079e19f905c8f4abe2604750"}]},{"sha":"89822e105b42840e079e19f905c8f4abe2604750","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDg5ODIyZTEwNWI0Mjg0MGUwNzllMTlmOTA1YzhmNGFiZTI2MDQ3NTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-21T20:21:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T20:21:18Z"},"message":"chore(code): update dependency minimums (#4912)\n\nRefreshes Deep Agents Code's dependency lower bounds and lockfile to\nkeep minimum-version installs on current supported releases.\n\nThe NVIDIA extra assertion now matches the updated `aiohttp` minimum,\nand Ruff's newer selector rules are accounted for in the lint\nconfiguration.","tree":{"sha":"bf6ed22fc361878abfc1f339b4fd702e48ef8aff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/bf6ed22fc361878abfc1f339b4fd702e48ef8aff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/89822e105b42840e079e19f905c8f4abe2604750","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX9S+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuX0QAGiPMgNamzYMDZOaDzfnz9Bm\nheiZEG45tMfDU2uCeRDwIDawZRZYIG4fF9y6nP7T2iJZ4w7QdVvxm/1YUTTYcaaa\n7Sl2hUe5zxQNbifLoC15d1utrIUxjej8Dkmyz0oGxM0i4gj3FZ4DaS7xDdlYzQFA\nLA9iamwW0Ik84f3n/lAkYQDBvjdEkjnNAlDAZN5uYuvzFBSdoBu3as1KFbCEXQop\ngMYoNFTXonR24tCZ60UAqc6Z1zl41sglWEE6CFJocYuN3rvQYbxaDwBs2tj+f9Kp\naj9xNipQDNhGtGOOl/qLk4O8FvaDFVWJWODGndYEXq3PQ/DDZdeULQPdr3vBpiEM\nG3Qn2QWaCji4G0RwYFQOLfuuByzWrll3AIMKf/qo7EgTnrVLb7lax5DVGZAeqRIn\n//e5sg7rdHxGz9fKDXmJIm3BiENnm9RXqQydJggp5vNi3q4iMxc4A/ukW+dDMLD3\nedi31/r349YXSxlPJBf9gHtfSDpvxMQx2q3BLrfLSU0aAYNswE+yYR9rT74z+EbK\nsqJ2681QYyPz6u3fnE0WpA2PNKyCjmifr6iCt6B3W02Sn3RgXm6is/XanPFj2oF3\n0l4pNKAKa0CAW5qStYgxbJieX31Ao/Cpqmr8rVfiQ4b9xVQszzVk34sUPa3DS2bA\nCORcRFeGOPq0/mpvnJ+i\n=2tMZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bf6ed22fc361878abfc1f339b4fd702e48ef8aff\nparent e4d69b04a84de226d26d9ca3adea96f1337eef04\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784665278 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784665278 -0400\n\nchore(code): update dependency minimums (#4912)\n\nRefreshes Deep Agents Code's dependency lower bounds and lockfile to\nkeep minimum-version installs on current supported releases.\n\nThe NVIDIA extra assertion now matches the updated `aiohttp` minimum,\nand Ruff's newer selector rules are accounted for in the lint\nconfiguration.","verified_at":"2026-07-21T20:21:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/89822e105b42840e079e19f905c8f4abe2604750","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/89822e105b42840e079e19f905c8f4abe2604750","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/89822e105b42840e079e19f905c8f4abe2604750/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e4d69b04a84de226d26d9ca3adea96f1337eef04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e4d69b04a84de226d26d9ca3adea96f1337eef04","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e4d69b04a84de226d26d9ca3adea96f1337eef04"}]},{"sha":"e4d69b04a84de226d26d9ca3adea96f1337eef04","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGU0ZDY5YjA0YTg0ZGUyMjZkMjZkOWNhM2FkZWE5NmYxMzM3ZWVmMDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-21T20:03:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T20:03:26Z"},"message":"fix(code): prevent failed exit setup from stranding the app (#4913)\n\nDeep Agents Code no longer becomes stuck rejecting input if shutdown\nsetup fails before teardown is scheduled. Restart cleanup timeouts are\nnow covered directly, and restart error documentation matches runtime\nbehavior.\n\n---\n\n`exit()` now marks the app as exiting only after hook loading and iTerm\ncursor-guide restoration complete. The flag is still set before either\nthe deferred teardown task or immediate `super().exit()` path, so a\nsecond exit during the graceful window continues to force quit.\n\nThe new teardown test holds a tracked restart task in cancellation\ncleanup until the graceful-exit deadline expires, then verifies the\nwarning, server stop, and single Textual exit. Related docstrings and\nthe `_respawn_server` cancellation comment now identify where\ncancellation, timeout, and restart errors are handled.\n\nNo timeout values or teardown phase ordering changed.","tree":{"sha":"9f2d1478aa5cd8a502655a68a608109a0e78108c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9f2d1478aa5cd8a502655a68a608109a0e78108c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/e4d69b04a84de226d26d9ca3adea96f1337eef04","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX9COCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZnYQAIex44mX5b4aebJc6EpwwxVj\n2V3v1nCabqFhmrFALS0F5Q/MPJ1UHnlZ9MPzl33HgMbDFjKbHy3zNnneNGTpg7YU\np76Ri6sDiiykCu+O+8LvSx77TUZlMQWB8VuXT3rx1wgmna+sPCsqcP37nZ5iSrZi\np+amLkK7jT5Z/zT0TFAa9FY2QUS4CwlJvihH0k/D9cCOAT4aisyLCfNDqgd70Fld\nJcAKtoR8xi8XTQIVHHoo0skSLDwKV7f28zMz26oPKrdEXYaos4V+v6+sfk4dql8c\n9jV3XdQYaP4Xi5WNkgBEHDpa/Pexm6eLsUIXxG2Yeh4/5ohn8Z9QaHhfiYWtU0++\n+QSvsYBsoL1beUPwPA5ODyu1R8bgK6p+1Fy2ufExiLbFNRRbPaQrun0Spj7Iz9Re\nyaxusCz61cYkzQC0ESS89ujPvq4ZiSrZ2ve782XFs0Khdfb47PBgSaEAW7GL7Ro2\nyNQZHUn2D07E1sI5OoCfab/wxxw3KwCeZNPoDxF1+ncJ1YWJe2kUrsfGVrg7wBTU\neQe/t3/78qRpEMGNkwr50TDgcMIwW851Vx/nQy9vrRlxg/AJ0BHYn/9rifucZQHd\nUE9p91LXvy7aV+7u+nh9zLMsL9in0rdYQskpqwANw3aiAV8mJzkEpRe1XJjegkMB\n4c5vhlexuOM6YKnYDoun\n=Q8Mg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9f2d1478aa5cd8a502655a68a608109a0e78108c\nparent c518ac6cb27307be86e8073adebf27e9db4f4017\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784664206 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784664206 -0400\n\nfix(code): prevent failed exit setup from stranding the app (#4913)\n\nDeep Agents Code no longer becomes stuck rejecting input if shutdown\nsetup fails before teardown is scheduled. Restart cleanup timeouts are\nnow covered directly, and restart error documentation matches runtime\nbehavior.\n\n---\n\n`exit()` now marks the app as exiting only after hook loading and iTerm\ncursor-guide restoration complete. The flag is still set before either\nthe deferred teardown task or immediate `super().exit()` path, so a\nsecond exit during the graceful window continues to force quit.\n\nThe new teardown test holds a tracked restart task in cancellation\ncleanup until the graceful-exit deadline expires, then verifies the\nwarning, server stop, and single Textual exit. Related docstrings and\nthe `_respawn_server` cancellation comment now identify where\ncancellation, timeout, and restart errors are handled.\n\nNo timeout values or teardown phase ordering changed.","verified_at":"2026-07-21T20:03:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e4d69b04a84de226d26d9ca3adea96f1337eef04","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e4d69b04a84de226d26d9ca3adea96f1337eef04","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e4d69b04a84de226d26d9ca3adea96f1337eef04/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c518ac6cb27307be86e8073adebf27e9db4f4017","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c518ac6cb27307be86e8073adebf27e9db4f4017","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c518ac6cb27307be86e8073adebf27e9db4f4017"}]},{"sha":"c518ac6cb27307be86e8073adebf27e9db4f4017","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGM1MThhYzZjYjI3MzA3YmU4NmU4MDczYWRlYmYyN2U5ZGI0ZjQwMTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-21T19:40:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T19:40:33Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump pyasn1 from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4 in /libs/cli (#4899)\n\nBumps [pyasn1](https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1) from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/releases\">pyasn1's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Release 0.6.4</h2>\n<p>This is a security release.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders. A small\ncrafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume excessive CPU.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag IDs\nto 20 octets (140 bits). Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate\nto consume excessive CPU and memory.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and CPU\nconsumption in <code>Real.__float__()</code> for values with large\nbase-10 exponents.</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All changes are noted in the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">pyasn1's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Revision 0.6.4, released 08-07-2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders.\nA small crafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume\nexcessive CPU. Arcs are now accumulated in linear time; decoded\nvalues are unchanged (thanks for reporting, tynus2)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag\nIDs to 20 octets (140 bits), matching the OID arc limit introduced\nin 0.6.2. Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate to consume\nexcessive CPU and memory; longer tag IDs are now rejected with\nPyAsn1Error. Also fixed Tag and TagSet repr() failing on huge tag\n(thanks for reporting, mikeappsec)\nIDs due to the integer-to-string conversion limit (Python 3.11+)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and\nCPU consumption in Real.<strong>float</strong>() for values with large\nbase-10\nexponents. Conversion no longer materializes huge intermediate\nintegers; values too large to represent as a Python float raise\nOverflowError promptly, and prettyPrint() renders them as\n'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->' as before. Also fixed base-10 mantissa\nnormalization\nto use exact integer arithmetic; mantissas larger than 2**53\ncould previously lose precision through float division\n(thanks for reporting, gvozdila)</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit\n[pr <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/pull/113\">pyasn1/pyasn1#113</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/72e4803405816c371ed3b2cb4be181c47f038406\"><code>72e4803</code></a>\nPrepare release 0.6.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/0c19eeb853731db1c717ff125ea001a1e558332d\"><code>0c19eeb</code></a>\nPin PyPI publish action to immutable commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/45bdb19eb7df4b3780fe9c912c63e99bffc39dd9\"><code>45bdb19</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/628e36ecbb5277a3f01572ce418ef54271b165a5\"><code>628e36e</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/e60c691cb91addb8fcefa2f537e85ede6fb1e886\"><code>e60c691</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/compare/v0.6.3...v0.6.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"dd9d8dbbeca6e0b329fe6a5876d5e72439af437f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/dd9d8dbbeca6e0b329fe6a5876d5e72439af437f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c518ac6cb27307be86e8073adebf27e9db4f4017","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX8sxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhk0QAID93tnIszQh2vcXmgLEeSFE\nRtRH0rj8yee5I18wLrXQ1gAHWA8//aE01jU/oKATWaeox4jdTGzuNUV62xR3nfeZ\n5/8QOyDq59boshF4HTiVTZA1n5lpivYVHZlw6vkOeCHt9PsWFABtvZlA50Q/Kpnn\nq3JFLJ6zw6D0sP6NgIqJqjYiQxnOLZg40eVsb0+msBopfaa7AarAj7GYKMyyX6hL\nfuitm6wjCk3gs6/DDbY43MdM3Lls/v7o5Y/aCXXPXJdJ9C4or++EZ4Q3sj6uyBov\nZ5psiAtWTs3iu0Y+sjGfhR1HDSAiuYr7Km9Uvid/kWK/T5viIT3MJ3ALsSGiXgcM\n38FYsHUGPh7OhM6O6ZKwbOZ2to7yBjzr/zANfOi94FH2xP0eXrCuGAQDHs4jS9hf\nsTgSRhKO/JaUnSr6H5zpwD8Ab9z29u5yJzEJtPR5lyQ2oCNWN7mbmKXfOjTtKTeB\n9X4JMbRM31z/PMASjyNCr/Ftrloi9ZCytqUaHB9mh4mafXvNIKiD36Gxf6HMhlne\n+f64WRsWVbr2rDHhkR9UZGTlSBpe7b9JMFT2lqyLwhyjTL422TZt0krr1G7k/XbI\n92wumHaX5wE/l4nGhzW5BmV5Qd80OUhKz6ijcREklWtZD4NbIqGGykrLJbIINgDH\n1lfFZmxvv6b5xSS2ZQrG\n=IJYK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree dd9d8dbbeca6e0b329fe6a5876d5e72439af437f\nparent de2173aa56375d3c8d91e29c55e0c4f52cfd1ca1\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784662833 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784662833 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump pyasn1 from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4 in /libs/cli (#4899)\n\nBumps [pyasn1](htt