HSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders. A small\ncrafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume excessive CPU.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag IDs\nto 20 octets (140 bits). Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate\nto consume excessive CPU and memory.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and CPU\nconsumption in <code>Real.__float__()</code> for values with large\nbase-10 exponents.</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All changes are noted in the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">pyasn1's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Revision 0.6.4, released 08-07-2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders.\nA small crafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume\nexcessive CPU. Arcs are now accumulated in linear time; decoded\nvalues are unchanged (thanks for reporting, tynus2)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag\nIDs to 20 octets (140 bits), matching the OID arc limit introduced\nin 0.6.2. Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate to consume\nexcessive CPU and memory; longer tag IDs are now rejected with\nPyAsn1Error. Also fixed Tag and TagSet repr() failing on huge tag\n(thanks for reporting, mikeappsec)\nIDs due to the integer-to-string conversion limit (Python 3.11+)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and\nCPU consumption in Real.<strong>float</strong>() for values with large\nbase-10\nexponents. Conversion no longer materializes huge intermediate\nintegers; values too large to represent as a Python float raise\nOverflowError promptly, and prettyPrint() renders them as\n'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->' as before. Also fixed base-10 mantissa\nnormalization\nto use exact integer arithmetic; mantissas larger than 2**53\ncould previously lose precision through float division\n(thanks for reporting, gvozdila)</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit\n[pr <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/pull/113\">pyasn1/pyasn1#113</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/72e4803405816c371ed3b2cb4be181c47f038406\"><code>72e4803</code></a>\nPrepare release 0.6.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/0c19eeb853731db1c717ff125ea001a1e558332d\"><code>0c19eeb</code></a>\nPin PyPI publish action to immutable commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/45bdb19eb7df4b3780fe9c912c63e99bffc39dd9\"><code>45bdb19</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/628e36ecbb5277a3f01572ce418ef54271b165a5\"><code>628e36e</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/e60c691cb91addb8fcefa2f537e85ede6fb1e886\"><code>e60c691</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/compare/v0.6.3...v0.6.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T19:38:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8326177f280e4ae0fe10f8dfcd8c646507950bb6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8326177f280e4ae0fe10f8dfcd8c646507950bb6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8326177f280e4ae0fe10f8dfcd8c646507950bb6/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8400b89a0273e6bf21a712f104ef26e0ff0acd1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8400b89a0273e6bf21a712f104ef26e0ff0acd1c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8400b89a0273e6bf21a712f104ef26e0ff0acd1c"}]},{"sha":"8400b89a0273e6bf21a712f104ef26e0ff0acd1c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDg0MDBiODlhMDI3M2U2YmYyMWE3MTJmMTA0ZWYyNmUwZmYwYWNkMWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-21T19:34:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T19:34:45Z"},"message":"chore(deps-dev): bump setuptools from 82.0.1 to 83.0.0 in /libs/evals (#4896)\n\nBumps [setuptools](https://github.com/pypa/setuptools) from 82.0.1 to\n83.0.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/blob/main/NEWS.rst\">setuptools's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>v83.0.0</h1>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Require Python 3.10 or later.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Bugfixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>MANIFEST.in</code> matching (via <code>FileList</code>) is now\ninsensitive to Unicode\nnormalization form. A pattern authored in one form (e.g. NFC, as\ntypically\nsaved by editors) now matches a file whose name is stored on disk in\nanother\n(e.g. NFD, as produced by macOS APFS/HFS+). Previously an\n<code>exclude</code>,\n<code>global-exclude</code>, <code>recursive-exclude</code>, or\n<code>prune</code> rule could silently\nfail to drop a non-ASCII-named file from the source distribution,\npublishing\nit despite the exclusion -- see GHSA-h35f-9h28-mq5c.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Deprecations and Removals</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>pypa/distutils#334</code></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/6519f728c6f23c992df81a5691ef7655184a20eb\"><code>6519f72</code></a>\nBump version: 82.0.1 → 83.0.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/d1151b125b29a6ee1c7db860f7ee6c365d525b5f\"><code>d1151b1</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5250\">#5250</a>\nfrom pypa/feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2df31e6a741b0fe775969618fe6a3a3d032e900\"><code>a2df31e</code></a>\nCapture removal of dry_run parameter in changelog.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/00144dc3fb6d023fd81cdc26c380a012b084df9b\"><code>00144dc</code></a>\nMoved newsfragment to the release where it occurred.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a4a5a2b160357be77626aa077ddd1d8ee53be50f\"><code>a4a5a2b</code></a>\nAdd news fragment.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/77470c23c35031c9e37d7512694ac5ca52bfcaac\"><code>77470c2</code></a>\nMerge <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/distutils\">https://github.com/pypa/distutils</a>\ninto feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/3c43897420f25a1be1afe6eaa905d056009cc736\"><code>3c43897</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5247\">#5247</a>\nfrom pypa/copilot/fix-pypy-version-issue</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/bb6ea66b4bd01cb35d7c68a1bc61b96d59190269\"><code>bb6ea66</code></a>\nBump PyPy from 3.10 to 3.11 in CI workflow</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2bc3aca2f55eb9b93ea633e58ba68170ce14451\"><code>a2bc3ac</code></a>\nFix broken intersphinx reference to build's installation docs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/2d6a739c64cfedc65e1f635af7b52340aac8d99b\"><code>2d6a739</code></a>\nUse stacked parametrize decorators instead of itertools.product</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/compare/v82.0.1...v83.0.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=setuptools&package-manager=uv&previous-version=82.0.1&new-version=83.0.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a587eb173442e3bfd87ac76c830433afa454c79d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a587eb173442e3bfd87ac76c830433afa454c79d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8400b89a0273e6bf21a712f104ef26e0ff0acd1c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX8nVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfmUQAIFNuflqUpFJk+8D3UqDpwlr\n7+AH4vJdg4bDEgUITJGdMh2bydMSGnGNckGnpKv8UVo17/3IuNF3JtXW7nZnn3im\n/OHHtCInhl+1zcz3m+MoO3yhfQ/p/iNAVRngaao0Bz4Ans93JbsdVosBnkUgZrvv\nHiGLNnQTz0jDJT5xGAAFhkEySTWmnHVneLrsbQPQTvuzw8cvVbANGRp8b7/Cze6t\n/W+BFfjpNsVuy4AKqCgbdl8cQ0Np4gcGSuHxBKB5zhCNDdXV4Tlm6O5pB/7sOSTX\ns3uzhwpmj664+PA/M/6zvQdN0TUsiZKbJs6G+taACWKT2XMkaTkeHI8oqFz2OJXp\njvDjnRv0DpbpZxqJ/fv5gRZrtj3HyMORylaGWWVdpqY6Is4iEPeRGAw+SabRvVSu\n9SV5pJTcfTk9/04lU0BC3s+TsNLwSw05Nv41xky1M6h2H/h8QdFc2Ry7wqDp2S40\ngGudNlcdJ0SnMESKpit4luwIRnzjkOfSPWuWuvKXAEqasdrcCYz/dcNLbT40/0xy\ndr6yzp5nxj6ub6VOG+R8KfgZIN3eRribbmTqRoVPkUivr82aFAT/wKLnxOgtVfIb\nIuMEUIY/x4wjQ0comZYujg1v54Deb/q88GYDgnSGlyDNcfIta9mx425aEj3jdc3j\nOGzqXmvLcmx7PBH4Qf4p\n=bazA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a587eb173442e3bfd87ac76c830433afa454c79d\nparent 54e896bbb799271310b25e4ce137254afbee2e10\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784662485 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784662485 -0400\n\nchore(deps-dev): bump setuptools from 82.0.1 to 83.0.0 in /libs/evals (#4896)\n\nBumps [setuptools](https://github.com/pypa/setuptools) from 82.0.1 to\n83.0.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/blob/main/NEWS.rst\">setuptools's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>v83.0.0</h1>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Require Python 3.10 or later.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Bugfixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>MANIFEST.in</code> matching (via <code>FileList</code>) is now\ninsensitive to Unicode\nnormalization form. A pattern authored in one form (e.g. NFC, as\ntypically\nsaved by editors) now matches a file whose name is stored on disk in\nanother\n(e.g. NFD, as produced by macOS APFS/HFS+). Previously an\n<code>exclude</code>,\n<code>global-exclude</code>, <code>recursive-exclude</code>, or\n<code>prune</code> rule could silently\nfail to drop a non-ASCII-named file from the source distribution,\npublishing\nit despite the exclusion -- see GHSA-h35f-9h28-mq5c.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Deprecations and Removals</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>pypa/distutils#334</code></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/6519f728c6f23c992df81a5691ef7655184a20eb\"><code>6519f72</code></a>\nBump version: 82.0.1 → 83.0.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/d1151b125b29a6ee1c7db860f7ee6c365d525b5f\"><code>d1151b1</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5250\">#5250</a>\nfrom pypa/feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2df31e6a741b0fe775969618fe6a3a3d032e900\"><code>a2df31e</code></a>\nCapture removal of dry_run parameter in changelog.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/00144dc3fb6d023fd81cdc26c380a012b084df9b\"><code>00144dc</code></a>\nMoved newsfragment to the release where it occurred.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a4a5a2b160357be77626aa077ddd1d8ee53be50f\"><code>a4a5a2b</code></a>\nAdd news fragment.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/77470c23c35031c9e37d7512694ac5ca52bfcaac\"><code>77470c2</code></a>\nMerge <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/distutils\">https://github.com/pypa/distutils</a>\ninto feature/distutils-d7633fbed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/3c43897420f25a1be1afe6eaa905d056009cc736\"><code>3c43897</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/5247\">#5247</a>\nfrom pypa/copilot/fix-pypy-version-issue</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/bb6ea66b4bd01cb35d7c68a1bc61b96d59190269\"><code>bb6ea66</code></a>\nBump PyPy from 3.10 to 3.11 in CI workflow</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/a2bc3aca2f55eb9b93ea633e58ba68170ce14451\"><code>a2bc3ac</code></a>\nFix broken intersphinx reference to build's installation docs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/commit/2d6a739c64cfedc65e1f635af7b52340aac8d99b\"><code>2d6a739</code></a>\nUse stacked parametrize decorators instead of itertools.product</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/compare/v82.0.1...v83.0.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=setuptools&package-manager=uv&previous-version=82.0.1&new-version=83.0.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T19:34:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8400b89a0273e6bf21a712f104ef26e0ff0acd1c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8400b89a0273e6bf21a712f104ef26e0ff0acd1c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8400b89a0273e6bf21a712f104ef26e0ff0acd1c/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"54e896bbb799271310b25e4ce137254afbee2e10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/54e896bbb799271310b25e4ce137254afbee2e10","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/54e896bbb799271310b25e4ce137254afbee2e10"}]},{"sha":"54e896bbb799271310b25e4ce137254afbee2e10","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDU0ZTg5NmJiYjc5OTI3MTMxMGIyNWU0Y2UxMzcyNTRhZmJlZTJlMTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-21T19:31:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T19:31:55Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump pyasn1 from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4 in /libs/evals (#4895)\n\nBumps [pyasn1](https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1) from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/releases\">pyasn1's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Release 0.6.4</h2>\n<p>This is a security release.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders. A small\ncrafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume excessive CPU.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag IDs\nto 20 octets (140 bits). Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate\nto consume excessive CPU and memory.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and CPU\nconsumption in <code>Real.__float__()</code> for values with large\nbase-10 exponents.</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All changes are noted in the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">pyasn1's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Revision 0.6.4, released 08-07-2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders.\nA small crafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume\nexcessive CPU. Arcs are now accumulated in linear time; decoded\nvalues are unchanged (thanks for reporting, tynus2)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag\nIDs to 20 octets (140 bits), matching the OID arc limit introduced\nin 0.6.2. Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate to consume\nexcessive CPU and memory; longer tag IDs are now rejected with\nPyAsn1Error. Also fixed Tag and TagSet repr() failing on huge tag\n(thanks for reporting, mikeappsec)\nIDs due to the integer-to-string conversion limit (Python 3.11+)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and\nCPU consumption in Real.<strong>float</strong>() for values with large\nbase-10\nexponents. Conversion no longer materializes huge intermediate\nintegers; values too large to represent as a Python float raise\nOverflowError promptly, and prettyPrint() renders them as\n'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->' as before. Also fixed base-10 mantissa\nnormalization\nto use exact integer arithmetic; mantissas larger than 2**53\ncould previously lose precision through float division\n(thanks for reporting, gvozdila)</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit\n[pr <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/pull/113\">pyasn1/pyasn1#113</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/72e4803405816c371ed3b2cb4be181c47f038406\"><code>72e4803</code></a>\nPrepare release 0.6.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/0c19eeb853731db1c717ff125ea001a1e558332d\"><code>0c19eeb</code></a>\nPin PyPI publish action to immutable commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/45bdb19eb7df4b3780fe9c912c63e99bffc39dd9\"><code>45bdb19</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/628e36ecbb5277a3f01572ce418ef54271b165a5\"><code>628e36e</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/e60c691cb91addb8fcefa2f537e85ede6fb1e886\"><code>e60c691</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/compare/v0.6.3...v0.6.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=pyasn1&package-manager=uv&previous-version=0.6.3&new-version=0.6.4)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"763bd00389c80e2d9e56958843fca6642ae19c5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/763bd00389c80e2d9e56958843fca6642ae19c5f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/54e896bbb799271310b25e4ce137254afbee2e10","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX8krCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ9YQAEaitcex1nnU4Zv2ZRrtGGsC\nE00RNawMLYAECFbI1ObRBpKT9qPxYl+dHjVzn641ypg0gMlywRLyeOHJLq9Bbtio\ncyWQEmT9boZ0N5qrl2sZjn0bAtK2cR9U9tEA9/mBF+9wi39Im6WweBdeytaHBaG0\nz4bL7Gh0EQet5yvMg8j7Q19+q2WGsTE4GR0jI5aohRSWLF1JmJLKEYNmwFLD/8t5\n7QSDkmfqEO75Iglts1wiI/ixywouIasKvpuwtFXbFYsNj7Zx3wdWdWpFfNu0P6/f\nNopuncD1svrn6K409Tfixq5EXIQDltsJlgnmnjVWKR69DN6wYIe1ahtWMNCxprJ/\ntNo8xCEjOLtUDV7cLgsPQOMVcjF4ktB5E78aQbHM1ilr55o9kogpZm73zQOAc08m\n3P+HqrXOP+ehWffGYtS2fvg1xvj0QZ78cO8PlVOhTuaGfzoRbMP3yI6iQhYomDzB\nC8JZMB/DL1LmKh/CBNJuFU/DUYrBWqOFnUOy+V0NpSmimV0YHuB1DXNkCDsBA59X\nmGZyugdOWraudIJH7KM8r1BHIU/JSLKXoNGurj67LR2a3mNgbi2BVWO96XMMp7aU\nmiAN9OyTqnJtTEV8C0HHncxboyLDwFPLArUjjJmIh2jMTUu8LCK8eDD922rM245C\n6admwVb4gJZ4n5hjWXcU\n=iU9O\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 763bd00389c80e2d9e56958843fca6642ae19c5f\nparent 0b071ef71a1f0d63cb09de7ac528e030cd75af2e\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784662315 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784662315 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump pyasn1 from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4 in /libs/evals (#4895)\n\nBumps [pyasn1](https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1) from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/releases\">pyasn1's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Release 0.6.4</h2>\n<p>This is a security release.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders. A small\ncrafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume excessive CPU.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag IDs\nto 20 octets (140 bits). Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate\nto consume excessive CPU and memory.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and CPU\nconsumption in <code>Real.__float__()</code> for values with large\nbase-10 exponents.</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All changes are noted in the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">pyasn1's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Revision 0.6.4, released 08-07-2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders.\nA small crafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume\nexcessive CPU. Arcs are now accumulated in linear time; decoded\nvalues are unchanged (thanks for reporting, tynus2)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag\nIDs to 20 octets (140 bits), matching the OID arc limit introduced\nin 0.6.2. Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate to consume\nexcessive CPU and memory; longer tag IDs are now rejected with\nPyAsn1Error. Also fixed Tag and TagSet repr() failing on huge tag\n(thanks for reporting, mikeappsec)\nIDs due to the integer-to-string conversion limit (Python 3.11+)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and\nCPU consumption in Real.<strong>float</strong>() for values with large\nbase-10\nexponents. Conversion no longer materializes huge intermediate\nintegers; values too large to represent as a Python float raise\nOverflowError promptly, and prettyPrint() renders them as\n'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->' as before. Also fixed base-10 mantissa\nnormalization\nto use exact integer arithmetic; mantissas larger than 2**53\ncould previously lose precision through float division\n(thanks for reporting, gvozdila)</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit\n[pr <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/pull/113\">pyasn1/pyasn1#113</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/72e4803405816c371ed3b2cb4be181c47f038406\"><code>72e4803</code></a>\nPrepare release 0.6.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/0c19eeb853731db1c717ff125ea001a1e558332d\"><code>0c19eeb</code></a>\nPin PyPI publish action to immutable commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/45bdb19eb7df4b3780fe9c912c63e99bffc39dd9\"><code>45bdb19</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/628e36ecbb5277a3f01572ce418ef54271b165a5\"><code>628e36e</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/e60c691cb91addb8fcefa2f537e85ede6fb1e886\"><code>e60c691</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/compare/v0.6.3...v0.6.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=pyasn1&package-manager=uv&previous-version=0.6.3&new-version=0.6.4)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T19:31:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/54e896bbb799271310b25e4ce137254afbee2e10","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/54e896bbb799271310b25e4ce137254afbee2e10","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/54e896bbb799271310b25e4ce137254afbee2e10/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0b071ef71a1f0d63cb09de7ac528e030cd75af2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0b071ef71a1f0d63cb09de7ac528e030cd75af2e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0b071ef71a1f0d63cb09de7ac528e030cd75af2e"}]},{"sha":"0b071ef71a1f0d63cb09de7ac528e030cd75af2e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDBiMDcxZWY3MWExZjBkNjNjYjA5ZGU3YWM1MjhlMDMwY2Q3NWFmMmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-21T19:26:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T19:26:57Z"},"message":"fix(code): avoid tracking inline restart callers (#4894)\n\nAfter `/reload` or a pending `/mcp reconnect` restarts the owned server,\nquitting now allows coordinated graceful teardown to finish instead of\ncanceling Textual’s application loop early.\n\n---\n\nRestart tracking now distinguishes Textual workers and explicitly\ndetached tasks from inline callers on the long-lived message loop. The\ndeferred web-search restart prompt is also registered at its scheduling\nsite, preserving cancellation and waiting for genuine background restart\nwork before the server stops.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `python -m pytest -q\ntests/unit_tests/test_app.py::TestExitGracefulWorkerHandoff\ntests/unit_tests/test_app.py::TestRespawnServer` (49 passed)\n- Ruff check and format validation for the edited files\n- `make -C libs/code type`\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"3d34f6ee9817e884406ee00f811b16088de3b00f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3d34f6ee9817e884406ee00f811b16088de3b00f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0b071ef71a1f0d63cb09de7ac528e030cd75af2e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX8gBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAr9kQABrNFar3lzhiUfpZ6yQ4gZYi\nv84yNdYNqPkexGlWo7xZGP0aUhHhNyY4ioTMJaWyVrpXll6r9R/0lF+0N6JURGRs\nmz3ap/cYsJtPbq+CKgC7N5FSwYG72dW8EcbRAcgYsx+KI1/eLIjVY7I3mD/8jziq\np3Eb+26IYm+iCU2uHJTPJAN4wSO+4s2GLaZ6A2TtE4ctJYz0mR1b2/qFNutRYeJD\nowj8qPuOAR1dn2fqHBRpkQgX5XrcSKGXR1jurXnxQodsgU0OZHm4mdhnw7KEwd0z\nHkBmnNqDBa5ZEotyJl05/wYtxHGW9lxYCeeRjWw8cTKuW5o9lzKft2EKzSiQS+3j\nF52Bu9y4MkMI8/Zq2eHvcYBLzdWBLdqR/t52t64OU5YfLoSBT3Ute2YCwYGqq1mP\nb6lO2uFLkz0Y84LzC2gn/ydnxoykBz7UFmH1wFw8fe7PonGWbkVz7bD9KkKH+Tlv\ntJWwtWq8umiV5jJC3yeyOSlGZ9j8rZryCPBLTVsXe8JXarNaU04wp/UACLfHJaPi\nnT5nJ6ahzh6/OVNW/VxxRD1BPjPVcX8iqxUprflr2LAbg6jOy7LVpxXpelzop1KM\n22AsF2/R3slQrX6pOOlMoX3pxjmZ/ljWw+njyPG97lbqy+xSzEmvQ8X9xEH8thni\nE/Ag54J9Iqcc+47/8tyJ\n=C8Za\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3d34f6ee9817e884406ee00f811b16088de3b00f\nparent 4fe8a49c15694202753822489e93aa783f1690b8\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784662017 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784662017 -0400\n\nfix(code): avoid tracking inline restart callers (#4894)\n\nAfter `/reload` or a pending `/mcp reconnect` restarts the owned server,\nquitting now allows coordinated graceful teardown to finish instead of\ncanceling Textual’s application loop early.\n\n---\n\nRestart tracking now distinguishes Textual workers and explicitly\ndetached tasks from inline callers on the long-lived message loop. The\ndeferred web-search restart prompt is also registered at its scheduling\nsite, preserving cancellation and waiting for genuine background restart\nwork before the server stops.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `python -m pytest -q\ntests/unit_tests/test_app.py::TestExitGracefulWorkerHandoff\ntests/unit_tests/test_app.py::TestRespawnServer` (49 passed)\n- Ruff check and format validation for the edited files\n- `make -C libs/code type`\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T19:26:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0b071ef71a1f0d63cb09de7ac528e030cd75af2e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0b071ef71a1f0d63cb09de7ac528e030cd75af2e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0b071ef71a1f0d63cb09de7ac528e030cd75af2e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4fe8a49c15694202753822489e93aa783f1690b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4fe8a49c15694202753822489e93aa783f1690b8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4fe8a49c15694202753822489e93aa783f1690b8"}]},{"sha":"4fe8a49c15694202753822489e93aa783f1690b8","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRmZThhNDljMTU2OTQyMDI3NTM4MjI0ODllOTNhYTc4M2YxNjkwYjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-21T19:26:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T19:26:40Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump js-yaml from 4.2.0 to 4.3.0 in /libs/talon/deepagents_talon/channels/whatsapp_bridge (#4891)\n\nBumps [js-yaml](https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml) from 4.2.0 to 4.3.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md\">js-yaml's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>4.3.0, 3.15.0 - 2026-06-27</h2>\n<h3>Security</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Backported <code>maxTotalMergeKeys</code> option.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[5.2.0] - 2026-06-26</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Added <code>maxTotalMergeKeys</code> (10000) loader option to limit\nthe total number of\nkeys processed by YAML merge (<code>&lt;&lt;</code>) across one\n<code>load()</code> / <code>loadAll()</code> call.</li>\n<li>Added <code>maxAliases</code> (-1) loader option to limit the number\nof YAML aliases per\ndocument.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Removed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>maxMergeSeqLength</code> replaced with\n<code>maxTotalMergeKeys</code> for limiting YAML merge\nprocessing.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Fixed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Round-trip of integers with exponential form (&gt;=\n<code>1e21</code>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[5.1.0] - 2026-06-23</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Collection tags can finalize an incrementally populated carrier into\na\ndifferent result value.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Changed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>[breaking] <code>quoteStyle</code> now selects the preferred quote\nstyle; use the\nrestored <code>forceQuotes</code> option to force quoting non-key\nstrings.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[5.0.0] - 2026-06-20</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Added named exports for schemas, tags, parser events and AST\nutilities.</li>\n<li>Reworked <code>JSON_SCHEMA</code> and <code>CORE_SCHEMA</code> with\nspec-compliant scalar resolution\nrules, and added <code>YAML11_SCHEMA</code>.</li>\n<li>Added <code>realMapTag</code> for lossless mappings with non-string\nand complex keys.\nObject-based mappings now reject complex keys instead of stringifying\nthem.</li>\n<li>Added <code>dump()</code> <code>transform</code> option for changing\nthe generated AST before\nrendering.</li>\n<li>Added <code>dump()</code> options <code>seqInlineFirst</code>,\n<code>flowBracketPadding</code>,\n<code>flowSkipCommaSpace</code>, <code>flowSkipColonSpace</code>,\n<code>quoteFlowKeys</code>, <code>quoteStyle</code> and\n<code>tagBeforeAnchor</code>.</li>\n<li>Added formal data layers (events and AST) for modular data\npipelines.\n<ul>\n<li>Added low-level parser (to events), presenter and visitor APIs.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Added the <a href=\"https://github.com/yaml/yaml-test-suite\">YAML\nTest Suite</a> to the\ntest set.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Changed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>See the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/blob/master/docs/migrate_v4_to_v5.md\">migration\nguide</a> for upgrade notes.</li>\n<li>Rewritten in TypeScript and reorganized the public API around flat\nnamed\nexports.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/33d05b5d29a8c21360f620f7e1c1706e24522eda\"><code>33d05b5</code></a>\n4.3.0 released</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/663bfab6db2b4a146a9366fd685f069345be4ddb\"><code>663bfab</code></a>\nDrop demo publish, to not override new v5 one.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/1cb8c7b94bf75e15116869c1c0482dcb22785986\"><code>1cb8c7b</code></a>\nAdd v4-legacy tag for publish</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/02f27afad532763263cd2b6be35c24ee8e1f6157\"><code>02f27af</code></a>\nRestore umd builds back to es5</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/8be84edaf15e7c394fa3b813179d1bcc280e87fb\"><code>8be84ed</code></a>\nFix es5 compatibility</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/59423c6f8cdc78742ac00e25a4dd39ef16b702e4\"><code>59423c6</code></a>\nReplace <code>maxMergeSeqLength</code> option with\n<code>maxTotalMergeKeys</code> (more robust). Ba...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/6842ef6a02df01ca7282ea01dc3c70787710c05d\"><code>6842ef6</code></a>\ndoc polish</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/compare/4.2.0...4.3.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=js-yaml&package-manager=npm_and_yarn&previous-version=4.2.0&new-version=4.3.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"2764b869ab0290c27e13faa82e35721aac0ec329","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2764b869ab0290c27e13faa82e35721aac0ec329"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4fe8a49c15694202753822489e93aa783f1690b8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX8fwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVroQACvggTGz398GbpJFmOiAKH8m\nLan/ynR+608OkxP6MYPYXLpiVvlRzyR/ENCNGfLO1TxDRmOxh1m1Z/ybPAfnArBD\nX7uiUDs0I+DlDjTP4Q4XXmH1uN6nXSYQOyognxic08EKmfWTdO0F2IRIryRaiZg7\nBEFwHnkxgAKfvLUgBxeyBy5YSCRYQGdnrQ/SyeGbZ1HimSmilHtFn+vSPpJKhlZQ\nNqyx5d3UaV32SDMxaPd+XbBz+xmEixC356vj0Ydz2wO3f8mWOhILS7d6SqT66A/N\nFyASm7SLkSuCVC/Qwe9aWC+EhmMhZ4d/rf70OpU5RA1QVpjud/Aq37S3js5ma4HX\n+JIEgvYf36Z21AYGR1tDfQMfOQqDsdrRNlebM8Iz1ZmxMYlslmEl1uPnSW11chTp\nT0RFgB3Z1KGYQPmqe6HQyY0jtTMnwJK/6QSZFaPMY486rJcB6UpB7L5GJJWX6Tww\njzMwevQ8Wpl5KbO0BGLKCA8DKHgdkJjnYijM9SsG+Z8UpQy5jll9iUPNF0OfsDch\nM/2bYCZyA7H2n+QSKzZz3u1NTefnVjOzUNI7qrZvRbovIFO3WaYsrX2TattEOs/p\n3wm0RK60vfz4dv2B9XZc0rxo9cZhG7KMKRWUPqK5kV69Yf1YMsSGETS087WhE1hu\nX/tSrRiC3XyqjiB1G36T\n=N9BP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2764b869ab0290c27e13faa82e35721aac0ec329\nparent a2e501b71f3d91769f56d5b3e433af8e03f7656e\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784662000 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784662000 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump js-yaml from 4.2.0 to 4.3.0 in /libs/talon/deepagents_talon/channels/whatsapp_bridge (#4891)\n\nBumps [js-yaml](https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml) from 4.2.0 to 4.3.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md\">js-yaml's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>4.3.0, 3.15.0 - 2026-06-27</h2>\n<h3>Security</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Backported <code>maxTotalMergeKeys</code> option.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[5.2.0] - 2026-06-26</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Added <code>maxTotalMergeKeys</code> (10000) loader option to limit\nthe total number of\nkeys processed by YAML merge (<code>&lt;&lt;</code>) across one\n<code>load()</code> / <code>loadAll()</code> call.</li>\n<li>Added <code>maxAliases</code> (-1) loader option to limit the number\nof YAML aliases per\ndocument.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Removed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>maxMergeSeqLength</code> replaced with\n<code>maxTotalMergeKeys</code> for limiting YAML merge\nprocessing.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Fixed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Round-trip of integers with exponential form (&gt;=\n<code>1e21</code>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[5.1.0] - 2026-06-23</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Collection tags can finalize an incrementally populated carrier into\na\ndifferent result value.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Changed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>[breaking] <code>quoteStyle</code> now selects the preferred quote\nstyle; use the\nrestored <code>forceQuotes</code> option to force quoting non-key\nstrings.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[5.0.0] - 2026-06-20</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Added named exports for schemas, tags, parser events and AST\nutilities.</li>\n<li>Reworked <code>JSON_SCHEMA</code> and <code>CORE_SCHEMA</code> with\nspec-compliant scalar resolution\nrules, and added <code>YAML11_SCHEMA</code>.</li>\n<li>Added <code>realMapTag</code> for lossless mappings with non-string\nand complex keys.\nObject-based mappings now reject complex keys instead of stringifying\nthem.</li>\n<li>Added <code>dump()</code> <code>transform</code> option for changing\nthe generated AST before\nrendering.</li>\n<li>Added <code>dump()</code> options <code>seqInlineFirst</code>,\n<code>flowBracketPadding</code>,\n<code>flowSkipCommaSpace</code>, <code>flowSkipColonSpace</code>,\n<code>quoteFlowKeys</code>, <code>quoteStyle</code> and\n<code>tagBeforeAnchor</code>.</li>\n<li>Added formal data layers (events and AST) for modular data\npipelines.\n<ul>\n<li>Added low-level parser (to events), presenter and visitor APIs.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Added the <a href=\"https://github.com/yaml/yaml-test-suite\">YAML\nTest Suite</a> to the\ntest set.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Changed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>See the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/blob/master/docs/migrate_v4_to_v5.md\">migration\nguide</a> for upgrade notes.</li>\n<li>Rewritten in TypeScript and reorganized the public API around flat\nnamed\nexports.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/33d05b5d29a8c21360f620f7e1c1706e24522eda\"><code>33d05b5</code></a>\n4.3.0 released</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/663bfab6db2b4a146a9366fd685f069345be4ddb\"><code>663bfab</code></a>\nDrop demo publish, to not override new v5 one.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/1cb8c7b94bf75e15116869c1c0482dcb22785986\"><code>1cb8c7b</code></a>\nAdd v4-legacy tag for publish</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/02f27afad532763263cd2b6be35c24ee8e1f6157\"><code>02f27af</code></a>\nRestore umd builds back to es5</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/8be84edaf15e7c394fa3b813179d1bcc280e87fb\"><code>8be84ed</code></a>\nFix es5 compatibility</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/59423c6f8cdc78742ac00e25a4dd39ef16b702e4\"><code>59423c6</code></a>\nReplace <code>maxMergeSeqLength</code> option with\n<code>maxTotalMergeKeys</code> (more robust). Ba...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/6842ef6a02df01ca7282ea01dc3c70787710c05d\"><code>6842ef6</code></a>\ndoc polish</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/compare/4.2.0...4.3.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=js-yaml&package-manager=npm_and_yarn&previous-version=4.2.0&new-version=4.3.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T19:26:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4fe8a49c15694202753822489e93aa783f1690b8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4fe8a49c15694202753822489e93aa783f1690b8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4fe8a49c15694202753822489e93aa783f1690b8/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a2e501b71f3d91769f56d5b3e433af8e03f7656e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a2e501b71f3d91769f56d5b3e433af8e03f7656e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a2e501b71f3d91769f56d5b3e433af8e03f7656e"}]},{"sha":"a2e501b71f3d91769f56d5b3e433af8e03f7656e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGEyZTUwMWI3MWYzZDkxNzY5ZjU2ZDViM2U0MzNhZjhlMDNmNzY1NmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-21T18:46:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T18:46:52Z"},"message":"perf(code): coordinate async shutdown teardown to cut exit latency (#4831)\n\nInteractive shutdown is faster because independent cleanup now overlaps\ninstead of running sequentially, without skipping any cleanup.\n\n---\n\n`session.end` hooks run off the Textual event loop. Interrupted-agent\ncleanup still finishes before server shutdown; afterward, pending hooks\ndrain while the server stops.\n\nServer stop and restart paths are synchronized to prevent duplicate or\nracing teardown. Existing timeouts and cleanup guarantees are unchanged,\nand debug logs record phase timings.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/ce9a3224-140d-08bc-25d2-202982da0203)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"8aab8eb74774e2403166b9ecb22fe4bfa8b266f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/8aab8eb74774e2403166b9ecb22fe4bfa8b266f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a2e501b71f3d91769f56d5b3e433af8e03f7656e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX76cCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApnwQAIkfrsS63vvynKvMqdmhKcbn\nkgbxDcxibvoBQpYb1FA5xOzh5VQuAkCW0yxBQeYdPkuFANr+N9SBU/crNiDOQxSR\nn7V9DqzppZGKcQwVoO0P+5UKjZH9+K7/Xi9MPQAssyqhk7VReg3PZy5SRJ+EoPkV\nMq7JNJ35OLB2sUCkSG8mXdp2JJyqJvG+SKpSYHmCrU8r65ecQCkcdd+uUiADO6Jv\nzNlaBDeq2TpeLtXqpy6DefC9PK81sskyJ7KJZovSFM5QcuPwRuiWUU7TmwU6rBmU\nkIHYP/TdVAKrc2dUU6TrlCo1nJkhw5iHxvUtcHqzPvnZ1m5nCbr3tNlcj4DhDf9o\nmxC1AazEaNEY6hjh16IWGVnWgEHm+XxgyfbEXAC1pyWguJ/KGaTVk5vSTWFinjuC\nto9zcxCFhfzcXo2ZakN8KUS515e3FQhfLqG/MFi38Va7Tp638ae3bXeoQoPncx2y\n0FLxqzMGX9fiLckPkl2FufOzYoXyGwK3rL7JSR+vomZif/7UCXk40fFAcv/BBM/2\nPHTMQKzQ7v4ZyfTuQ2fBSILawy+NXnwejC7oZb5MTzIDeAOn+qIf5867bfRPb7c/\nbtzK1paX7qNCnjhqKr/8QCCxtxtGpyn/yfPLIRcXswKqtLeZt8ylDgJ7uNWPQr1d\n0E3d6ZOkTvl5FFTVgyki\n=/0kX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8aab8eb74774e2403166b9ecb22fe4bfa8b266f5\nparent 5c99687bdecfd9e33051373581cacddbf7d0202a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784659612 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784659612 -0400\n\nperf(code): coordinate async shutdown teardown to cut exit latency (#4831)\n\nInteractive shutdown is faster because independent cleanup now overlaps\ninstead of running sequentially, without skipping any cleanup.\n\n---\n\n`session.end` hooks run off the Textual event loop. Interrupted-agent\ncleanup still finishes before server shutdown; afterward, pending hooks\ndrain while the server stops.\n\nServer stop and restart paths are synchronized to prevent duplicate or\nracing teardown. Existing timeouts and cleanup guarantees are unchanged,\nand debug logs record phase timings.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/ce9a3224-140d-08bc-25d2-202982da0203)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T18:46:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a2e501b71f3d91769f56d5b3e433af8e03f7656e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a2e501b71f3d91769f56d5b3e433af8e03f7656e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a2e501b71f3d91769f56d5b3e433af8e03f7656e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5c99687bdecfd9e33051373581cacddbf7d0202a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5c99687bdecfd9e33051373581cacddbf7d0202a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5c99687bdecfd9e33051373581cacddbf7d0202a"}]},{"sha":"5c99687bdecfd9e33051373581cacddbf7d0202a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDVjOTk2ODdiZGVjZmQ5ZTMzMDUxMzczNTgxY2FjZGRiZjdkMDIwMmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-21T18:32:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T18:32:23Z"},"message":"feat(code): replace Gemini 3.5 Flash with 3.6 Flash in model switcher (#4890)\n\nGemini 3.6 Flash supersedes 3.5 Flash, so surface the newer model in the\n`/model` selector instead of the older one.\n\nSwaps both the `google_genai` and `openrouter` Gemini `3.5 Flash`\nentries in the `deepagents-code` recommended-model list for `3.6 Flash`,\nand moves the model-specific default thinking-level keying in\n`reasoning_effort` over to the new id so the recommended model keeps its\n`medium` default. Representative unit-test references are updated to\nmatch.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/0441ce8a-bfb9-b73a-31c9-9754af24aaad)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"06a117b3359c2c0c09355c7d51a9a9e270967a4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/06a117b3359c2c0c09355c7d51a9a9e270967a4f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5c99687bdecfd9e33051373581cacddbf7d0202a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX7s3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4ekQACIQ85OFK5tm23JcUWdeXDXM\nd+Jk//8bxXBIhNRHG5njqdoQ0GgXejNTTQwMt2rekWsdeSS8Fg12Zt/ntFyJmjN5\nSAQUv8WedKJam6LF10pXNHA27xnl+Aoo49y9vG8EuCTyWJ7XbW6yo8DCGtEHDWrl\nGx0iurjLhPBhfrra59SdQSbYPR29RK5HKvMJg+FUVJ+VRM3OJ7/LFkFYcxz2N1BN\n9llH5gC7hYfw454fER20VulJXUbuz0Ko1zG5+B+JqywDm0y6HDzUoiLYybOGIiLl\nURei1HB0ekq3447wkzBNHZqghz19CUJIRFBvsxt5FBL+mfFLUGJm/xuu7Eq8vQjV\nx5eKLYCyNyGZanyl+5mnc0+VwwTeYD/ZYEmNc0VWilgA1fvuCTBwrUkAm3F0IkqD\nes9PCdAidEr8RzGsUU95T8jzIrNDx3cjV0d6K/mWMU7nR4GAf1YbUiisUJsOl7QA\nczT2C7Pm/zWnxN6dvts8C4lv2s8u3Xg2FwQYwf/3N6rFX6aQyMIWFK9gH3ZN8yTf\nZHAQOE8+MpNH5e1VsOxaAGYU2IaZOtqrw7GZUJdwq5/Kxjhi202TMZqgy1fbaH0o\njgHFsigmP/C7cH6rgQfe07dDWvQ5DYAzWyyzK7a6hGfh22kmTOcZ0nM9lTQsTirT\nXsla9oGRPITEbiEBfp5O\n=/7uM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 06a117b3359c2c0c09355c7d51a9a9e270967a4f\nparent 1444ee2de09c01a6ffebc08a066a006e7d835126\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784658743 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784658743 -0400\n\nfeat(code): replace Gemini 3.5 Flash with 3.6 Flash in model switcher (#4890)\n\nGemini 3.6 Flash supersedes 3.5 Flash, so surface the newer model in the\n`/model` selector instead of the older one.\n\nSwaps both the `google_genai` and `openrouter` Gemini `3.5 Flash`\nentries in the `deepagents-code` recommended-model list for `3.6 Flash`,\nand moves the model-specific default thinking-level keying in\n`reasoning_effort` over to the new id so the recommended model keeps its\n`medium` default. Representative unit-test references are updated to\nmatch.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/0441ce8a-bfb9-b73a-31c9-9754af24aaad)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T18:32:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5c99687bdecfd9e33051373581cacddbf7d0202a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5c99687bdecfd9e33051373581cacddbf7d0202a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5c99687bdecfd9e33051373581cacddbf7d0202a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1444ee2de09c01a6ffebc08a066a006e7d835126","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1444ee2de09c01a6ffebc08a066a006e7d835126","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1444ee2de09c01a6ffebc08a066a006e7d835126"}]},{"sha":"1444ee2de09c01a6ffebc08a066a006e7d835126","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDE0NDRlZTJkZTA5YzAxYTZmZmViYzA4YTA2NmEwMDZlN2Q4MzUxMjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-21T18:26:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T18:26:21Z"},"message":"chore(deps-dev): bump pillow from 12.2.0 to 12.3.0 in /libs/talon (#4875)\n\nBumps [pillow](https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow) from 12.2.0 to\n12.3.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/releases\">pillow's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>12.3.0</h2>\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/releasenotes/12.3.0.html\">https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/releasenotes/12.3.0.html</a></p>\n<h2>Removals</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Remove non-image ImageCms modes <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9697\">#9697</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Documentation</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add release notes for SBOM and performance improvements <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9747\">#9747</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Add security release notes <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9741\">#9741</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Add release notes for Python 3.15 beta wheels <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9696\">#9696</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n<li>ImageFont can also be used with ImageText <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9597\">#9597</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Additional guidelines for security reports <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9659\">#9659</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/wiredfool\"><code>@​wiredfool</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Fixed typo <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9636\">#9636</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Added CVEs to 12.2.0 release notes <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9591\">#9591</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Revise development support information in README <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9583\">#9583</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aclark4life\"><code>@​aclark4life</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Add INCIDENT_RESPONSE.md <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9555\">#9555</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aclark4life\"><code>@​aclark4life</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Add STRIDE threat model to security docs <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9562\">#9562</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aclark4life\"><code>@​aclark4life</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Add CVEs to 12.2.0 release notes <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9556\">#9556</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Update README with revised security policy <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9553\">#9553</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Update security policy <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9552\">#9552</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aclark4life\"><code>@​aclark4life</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Update macOS tested Python versions <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9534\">#9534</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Dependencies</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update dep