https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9654\">#9654</a>\n[<a href=\"https://github.com/akx\"><code>@​akx</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Use reshape() instead of setting NumPy array shape directly <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9728\">#9728</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/bb1d8e8ab8d29048624d96e3ee53cecf7c13d13d\"><code>bb1d8e8</code></a>\n12.3.0 version bump</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/e63fc481dc2e07e21d5403deafb8f1ed98a513af\"><code>e63fc48</code></a>\nAdd release notes for SBOM and performance improvements (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9747\">#9747</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/13b701bbab291eec4bc87ea17ba06c94e5fe3054\"><code>13b701b</code></a>\nAdd release notes for <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9679\">#9679</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/5564ca72fcd59d040e270af5dcf17a0d7161c364\"><code>5564ca7</code></a>\nList methods</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/a0920fd384f800b5d0ba3dd29ecdeae4f1d4043b\"><code>a0920fd</code></a>\nSpeed up ImageChops operations (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9738\">#9738</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/07e9a6cd5336dc6cf8cae9165cd70cdd2b3e42fc\"><code>07e9a6c</code></a>\nSpeed up <code>Image.filter()</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9736\">#9736</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/a94578cf9649ea13e426cf7fb2b71b39ffc0dd50\"><code>a94578c</code></a>\nSpeed up <code>Image.getchannel()</code>, <code>Image.merge()</code>,\n<code>Image.putalpha()</code> and `Image...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/53e02c43c919d149b2a154a5180079f9df18fbbb\"><code>53e02c4</code></a>\nSpeed up <code>Image.fill()</code>, <code>Image.linear_gradient()</code>\nand `Image.radial_gradient...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/af037475be8634ba739744243164ba9e2c8346a6\"><code>af03747</code></a>\nSpeed up <code>Image.resample()</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9739\">#9739</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/5c9ca56c3e5fba52b647809fbb0986c87e73a571\"><code>5c9ca56</code></a>\nSpeed up <code>alpha_composite</code>, <code>matrix</code>,\n<code>negative</code>, <code>quantize</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9740\">#9740</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/compare/12.2.0...12.3.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T18:26:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7a11fb8a175bdabd812596fd5166f8cb56cfc2a7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7a11fb8a175bdabd812596fd5166f8cb56cfc2a7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7a11fb8a175bdabd812596fd5166f8cb56cfc2a7/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"eea0a84d9621565a707c161c2f22878771d9b38b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/eea0a84d9621565a707c161c2f22878771d9b38b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/eea0a84d9621565a707c161c2f22878771d9b38b"}]},{"sha":"eea0a84d9621565a707c161c2f22878771d9b38b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGVlYTBhODRkOTYyMTU2NWE3MDdjMTYxYzJmMjI4Nzg3NzFkOWIzOGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"corridor-security[bot]","email":"203152403+corridor-security[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-21T16:16:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T16:16:43Z"},"message":"fix(code): honor MCP server disables for plugins (#4848)\n\nDeep Agents Code now respects explicit MCP server disables for servers\nbundled with installed plugins.\n\n---\n\nInstalling or enabling a plugin is the user's trust decision for all of\nits bundled components, including MCP servers. First-time plugin servers\ntherefore continue to load without requiring a separate project\napproval.\n\nPlugin-provided MCP servers now pass through the user-level deny policy\nbefore loading. An explicitly disabled server remains disabled even when\nit is supplied by an installed plugin. If the MCP trust policy cannot be\nread, plugin servers fail closed rather than risking bypassing a saved\ndisable. Invalid plugin MCP configuration shapes are surfaced as\nconfiguration errors.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: corridor-security[bot] <203152403+corridor-security[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langsmith-fleet[bot] <langsmith-fleet[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"6380fd914a1178d3ec010bceb3de46e35e4e6956","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6380fd914a1178d3ec010bceb3de46e35e4e6956"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/eea0a84d9621565a707c161c2f22878771d9b38b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX5trCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAC0kQACorw/yN5tQRixc0Qof1DQpn\n5AuAo/d3L5RaVyWK8wK77RAgbwIYfS9KmU5wlPySRuzlOTuLLZPWOuoVckG6SbtP\nlOZ1Ex/dbmLMFsqnEpM0u1W3UD4x97Mg/E+Os+ZhHAsV33/0wrxrBtnStmaAaO0i\n941l0v2PWVqI+9f57eyFUhGrJEOsllYWnInSOT9IYpl1P1cT6nc4lZtOFxWEauGZ\nZx/PXVXjhy3AcnVYkA7kfITJreGeR1X78On+/jyFVhZtiNFq92hpoi+ryEMsNzV7\na+69Ha3NbwmlgI0S09I2LM3rV0ir8wgh9Nl3Ne+gMbjAJVCwXAj2QemGG8LcoLAi\n6Iu/th3Uc83xdObUcuShGkVb0BwTNW3VQHmbrFA0KLQ+aWZYd46++PjEczNwC17x\nXfC4pq6wbBycLddzoNQg2X6QJ/YVGOgf8fzw0Z+NLZ4zw1KQtXaF/TMxBBgyuF9i\nvXgQ/+7nkSy36aYsOEP6VLMV7QhJBCUKCT5+O0XGbLwU89zfVj3f3aVK0EpT1JYh\nM8VP2C7hqb08FniuwuuDcWOns5I9LKBe0E9xzjV9BbedrNP3KLexNS8jrRgmauRG\nxAcWbiGvD65fjZDhIFRsdPJTbQVIQTCoBXvjN9bUBBf+OC2g2cvyFcT1F1IceMdG\nrFWqktuUPD/ej/BK0+Rr\n=l18Z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6380fd914a1178d3ec010bceb3de46e35e4e6956\nparent b513bf3b2aaa30738da9b9b0ced1c001efb1bd5a\nauthor corridor-security[bot] <203152403+corridor-security[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784650603 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784650603 -0400\n\nfix(code): honor MCP server disables for plugins (#4848)\n\nDeep Agents Code now respects explicit MCP server disables for servers\nbundled with installed plugins.\n\n---\n\nInstalling or enabling a plugin is the user's trust decision for all of\nits bundled components, including MCP servers. First-time plugin servers\ntherefore continue to load without requiring a separate project\napproval.\n\nPlugin-provided MCP servers now pass through the user-level deny policy\nbefore loading. An explicitly disabled server remains disabled even when\nit is supplied by an installed plugin. If the MCP trust policy cannot be\nread, plugin servers fail closed rather than risking bypassing a saved\ndisable. Invalid plugin MCP configuration shapes are surfaced as\nconfiguration errors.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: corridor-security[bot] <203152403+corridor-security[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langsmith-fleet[bot] <langsmith-fleet[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T16:16:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/eea0a84d9621565a707c161c2f22878771d9b38b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/eea0a84d9621565a707c161c2f22878771d9b38b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/eea0a84d9621565a707c161c2f22878771d9b38b/comments","author":{"login":"corridor-security[bot]","id":203152403,"node_id":"BOT_kgDODBvcEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1177339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/corridor-security%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/corridor-security","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/corridor-security%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/corridor-security%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/corridor-security%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/corridor-security%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/corridor-security%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/corridor-security%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/corridor-security%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/corridor-security%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/corridor-security%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b513bf3b2aaa30738da9b9b0ced1c001efb1bd5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b513bf3b2aaa30738da9b9b0ced1c001efb1bd5a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b513bf3b2aaa30738da9b9b0ced1c001efb1bd5a"}]},{"sha":"b513bf3b2aaa30738da9b9b0ced1c001efb1bd5a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGI1MTNiZjNiMmFhYTMwNzM4ZGE5YjliMGNlZDFjMDAxZWZiMWJkNWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-21T16:13:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T16:13:04Z"},"message":"fix(code): preserve remembered MCP approvals with env allowlist (#4889)\n\nUsers who configure a process-wide MCP allowlist and also choose “Allow\nfor this project — until changed” are now prompted only once (fixes an\nissue where this was previously discarded).\n\n---\n\nA user can intentionally have two kinds of MCP approval at the same\ntime:\n\n- Process-wide server names in\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DANGEROUSLY_ENABLE_PROJECT_MCP_SERVERS`, which bypass\nproject and server-definition binding.\n- Project-scoped approvals saved by the startup prompt, which match only\nthe same project root, server name, and server-definition fingerprint.\n\n### Before\n\n1. The user starts `dcode` in a project whose MCP servers are not in the\nprocess-wide allowlist.\n2. They choose “Allow for this project — until changed.”\n3. `dcode` writes valid scoped approvals and reports:\n\nAllowing 2 project MCP servers for this session; remembering 2 for this\nproject.\n\n4. On the next launch, the presence of the process-wide env var causes\nthe loader to ignore every saved scoped approval, even when the env var\ncontains unrelated names.\n5. The same “Approve project MCP servers” prompt appears again.\n\n### After\n\n- Process-wide names and scoped remembered approvals are independent\ngrants, so both remain active.\n- The next launch recognizes the saved project/server fingerprints and\ndoes not prompt again.\n- An explicitly empty process-wide allowlist contributes no global names\nbut does not clear remembered project approvals.\n- A changed server command or URL still requires re-approval, and\ndisabled server names still take precedence over every approval source.\n\nRegression coverage reproduces the repeated-launch case and verifies\nboth populated and empty process-wide allowlists.","tree":{"sha":"95c9c287f13a16d02b362e5023d107994048215a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/95c9c287f13a16d02b362e5023d107994048215a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b513bf3b2aaa30738da9b9b0ced1c001efb1bd5a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX5qQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3OMQAKXFkIeqz+HhKvcNqU7Ttrsq\nJ9jIDTRxbcHIXYu2UCDXoq0kA2nyINxSa3YmyaXuNd0e29A8PY6t0Q8tkFxFlA30\ntOfZHLYRjL1DmWEWxjr5lkq92toDUK1BvaLtXrv4enANQvGbsUVbsUE+9G0WrEJJ\n81VANsvqOamefck49RojTZ7iesf9ptGyPYF8+Bg0Qc7uy/NCQ4x2DlaEkHiMmk5q\nWhtRt+Yy6NnPleoZdzyZEtVNtuHexhCTZtARrWQsMLPAbg3cZa9UI+RlyQyOYp2K\njx0iHSWlxoUHfLaGxBbVsvBusJ2xZ5y030I0X1smzMwofzfh//9lalXvLwClzJAl\nDdRCrB9V0JQY6VD2Fk3JkUqz8chBtWYA7zAhjo/2ZaxVGgzeKD3StNtdM343czf2\naioO80QYXCAlEB4Vje0tfoJZbbpzwbpOlucCLVRkH6MwgNi2rwA5b5MbvNTBXst8\nCnBW7Icb57eDQZgqtO2i/4RjynBHjAQlXuQEBRIaXE4GZxzdAD+9yXzP6lLoGz15\n8tZo70QZsbqtm1paXAfWqxCK7ZqEJjDMSIPhCC2zISgj3kSt6qo/XaM+nn2w7sf+\nFtxLuWwLO/YQjPzC89jfWy7rFmrjMG3EHVUhmjZFa1kSljxiPi5tBm3bcFmWY84a\naHhX6oEFMojUVVoiZ6bN\n=g/af\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 95c9c287f13a16d02b362e5023d107994048215a\nparent 46bb1a86c8041d5c161d7cd07de66d068fb100c0\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784650384 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784650384 -0400\n\nfix(code): preserve remembered MCP approvals with env allowlist (#4889)\n\nUsers who configure a process-wide MCP allowlist and also choose “Allow\nfor this project — until changed” are now prompted only once (fixes an\nissue where this was previously discarded).\n\n---\n\nA user can intentionally have two kinds of MCP approval at the same\ntime:\n\n- Process-wide server names in\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DANGEROUSLY_ENABLE_PROJECT_MCP_SERVERS`, which bypass\nproject and server-definition binding.\n- Project-scoped approvals saved by the startup prompt, which match only\nthe same project root, server name, and server-definition fingerprint.\n\n### Before\n\n1. The user starts `dcode` in a project whose MCP servers are not in the\nprocess-wide allowlist.\n2. They choose “Allow for this project — until changed.”\n3. `dcode` writes valid scoped approvals and reports:\n\nAllowing 2 project MCP servers for this session; remembering 2 for this\nproject.\n\n4. On the next launch, the presence of the process-wide env var causes\nthe loader to ignore every saved scoped approval, even when the env var\ncontains unrelated names.\n5. The same “Approve project MCP servers” prompt appears again.\n\n### After\n\n- Process-wide names and scoped remembered approvals are independent\ngrants, so both remain active.\n- The next launch recognizes the saved project/server fingerprints and\ndoes not prompt again.\n- An explicitly empty process-wide allowlist contributes no global names\nbut does not clear remembered project approvals.\n- A changed server command or URL still requires re-approval, and\ndisabled server names still take precedence over every approval source.\n\nRegression coverage reproduces the repeated-launch case and verifies\nboth populated and empty process-wide allowlists.","verified_at":"2026-07-21T16:13:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b513bf3b2aaa30738da9b9b0ced1c001efb1bd5a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b513bf3b2aaa30738da9b9b0ced1c001efb1bd5a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b513bf3b2aaa30738da9b9b0ced1c001efb1bd5a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"46bb1a86c8041d5c161d7cd07de66d068fb100c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/46bb1a86c8041d5c161d7cd07de66d068fb100c0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/46bb1a86c8041d5c161d7cd07de66d068fb100c0"}]},{"sha":"46bb1a86c8041d5c161d7cd07de66d068fb100c0","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQ2YmIxYTg2YzgwNDFkNWMxNjFkN2NkMDdkZTY2ZDA2OGZiMTAwYzA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-21T16:10:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T16:10:12Z"},"message":"fix(code): abort project MCP approval on Esc (#4888)\n\nPressing Esc in the project MCP approval prompt now aborts startup and\nreturns to the terminal instead of treating Esc as **Deny** and\ncontinuing into the TUI.\n\n---\n\nEsc now produces the same launch-cancellation outcome in both project\nMCP selectors. The explicit **Deny** option remains available and\nselected by default, so declining trust still requires choosing it and\npressing Enter.","tree":{"sha":"99f343912be19ec981dc5c09f7d6776038388bb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/99f343912be19ec981dc5c09f7d6776038388bb8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/46bb1a86c8041d5c161d7cd07de66d068fb100c0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX5nkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgssQAEOH7r0CaM1VGho70aF8Z3vp\nLwPf8A8yRavXlB5aFa8oz8PvNU8toinR1k+GvGWRQXimSXtvwAWKeEWL7OirSOhS\nvvLLNREwPKXkjJCnpSiDku7SKAN5ktFK8mJO6uwnOu0GVKSa1sykTHrsUv2Yhfbw\nBEAMEP6xSGEwLfWC+kHvFn/wc+VgLE5B2U3ha4gAASUxe5HeTwUTJS2zNJ6ImKP7\nkes61K15xwQWAyuzHjqrJwTZ+ncPVdpqPFbr7O98F9oHyxPdROYR1lbT21Ouz99K\nAl3cb97jDk1iGsSC41ceJWBEO4aYe7Wk361NqPH8yGgGi07RSlPj1Gt1hUnTzkgm\nyhfLbaFDXl1fsK4dBgLuDCTyHNf/ibSI5pHxVzF6CjH4BakSVu289Qy7MRgwRNy0\nb/qtKcn6lVSz4CGdU4ChfTWwm3qijcbtV79voFMLYIIrfQgiQb7c6yG9x+7MOhid\nV3Ke6k3YETi8T3rJnmggxw3TETIVP10thS6RXBXCE5i0mELsGwtMbtxBx4VGclSY\nX+CTq9ZIuB8A8z+G7xfgt1J1jfANSWBvqMF0zb3fN1Z/91O4WyEAJG18bJzt9u1B\n0Ryu0XoUKh0b2k/mYCjxv+7EWKOB3LAjxvwxQjEeGF+5UzJbx63mzhHjGbmXCbr5\nL3lq6/iM6O4Gp9878Sbi\n=oMx2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 99f343912be19ec981dc5c09f7d6776038388bb8\nparent 2d729b30c5df7265e8062bccd38026b745c6cf02\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784650212 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784650212 -0400\n\nfix(code): abort project MCP approval on Esc (#4888)\n\nPressing Esc in the project MCP approval prompt now aborts startup and\nreturns to the terminal instead of treating Esc as **Deny** and\ncontinuing into the TUI.\n\n---\n\nEsc now produces the same launch-cancellation outcome in both project\nMCP selectors. The explicit **Deny** option remains available and\nselected by default, so declining trust still requires choosing it and\npressing Enter.","verified_at":"2026-07-21T16:10:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/46bb1a86c8041d5c161d7cd07de66d068fb100c0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/46bb1a86c8041d5c161d7cd07de66d068fb100c0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/46bb1a86c8041d5c161d7cd07de66d068fb100c0/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","sta