5:58:58Z"},"message":"feat(code): add built-in thread inspector skill (#4769)\n\nDeep Agents Code now includes a built-in `deepagents-thread-inspector`\nskill for inspecting and summarizing local conversation threads.","tree":{"sha":"ce9caeabc38061daf29ecbe713c49fd72ecf5fa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ce9caeabc38061daf29ecbe713c49fd72ecf5fa4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2d729b30c5df7265e8062bccd38026b745c6cf02","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX5dCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYV8QAKc5papK+18fRKfNVS+uSQLG\n4nj/TsaaKk+2hgiXEHfOUfW6xcNloToYq2Li1F42Yj1zB0iulMCSWNM/U/vsjoOq\ni0SH9av+XnfADTzrtVNrMeWp/WTIsBDPJRCwStp6GzJK71xoybB3UrgFy7Oa70dm\narjNWmKgMHUbfJWTSgz4FELYKALZww+K1QXI2r+L7ZPkUWYpUtV0j2viBLmd03in\ntykMkAGaXRfb9eoeKjjZBxTQ8K1EEUUl+WF38w8yC1nm/ReT7Dep8FczKTjz2xk5\n4zjWBgKsxOI/L/yrzh3cS6rCr7Ys8WU1aGD3YwdxaBVPwkpLXbbHUqDSEE74wa90\n/uAFLKfAhlb4Ubf18WXNjs/DcJWGkTHDOyb8vToFqy02JAWVrrHqlQg9sZJqut3D\nipbaSHKeCiO635MoD25GqI8Yi+QQ7LR3moEB9WEc07EG7x134yCgd1anj3SC/mXx\nKqDL1alTuYKHcF8DfT0yMBXSGIfz1Mr8Q104TGQzd4q2QPW/7P1WRQUUZJeT3r3o\nTslRdvCPSI30HdDc6dv9YPjrLFhyHE6988D/A5S+9ATHZAPm+MqOyWc9RSaS1G1E\ncOaULMd43Ou4no4MWPKj9EpJSOG62nDFPPpcWRWByIvcoDsZvJ4aHq92A9WwLwU4\nDEhJ725sy0J9rk84OzCf\n=63Qj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ce9caeabc38061daf29ecbe713c49fd72ecf5fa4\nparent 4330534d18cbf79260842dde0e0c450312ef55ca\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784649538 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784649538 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add built-in thread inspector skill (#4769)\n\nDeep Agents Code now includes a built-in `deepagents-thread-inspector`\nskill for inspecting and summarizing local conversation threads.","verified_at":"2026-07-21T15:58:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2d729b30c5df7265e8062bccd38026b745c6cf02","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2d729b30c5df7265e8062bccd38026b745c6cf02","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2d729b30c5df7265e8062bccd38026b745c6cf02/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4330534d18cbf79260842dde0e0c450312ef55ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4330534d18cbf79260842dde0e0c450312ef55ca","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4330534d18cbf79260842dde0e0c450312ef55ca"}]},{"sha":"4330534d18cbf79260842dde0e0c450312ef55ca","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQzMzA1MzRkMThjYmY3OTI2MDg0MmRkZTBlMGM0NTAzMTJlZjU1Y2E","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-21T15:35:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T15:35:29Z"},"message":"fix(code): allow safe OS-temp scratch artifacts (#4869)\n\nRelated #4860\n\nAuto mode can now use a uniquely allocated OS temporary text file when a\ncommand requires file-based input, then remove that exact artifact\nwithout asking separately. Predictable or pre-existing temp paths and\nall other outside-worktree writes remain denied.\n\n---\n\ndcode owns the scratch lifecycle: the model supplies content and an\noptional suffix, while dcode chooses and exclusively creates the path. A\nsuccessful allocation records private provenance scoped to the current\nthread and user turn. Only the exact same file identity can be removed;\nfailed calls, prior proposals, other turns, parent directories, and\ngeneric file tools receive no authority.\n\nThe classifier may use this provenance only to establish what the\nartifact is. Literal user text remains the sole source of consent for\nthe action that consumes it or any destination it affects.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `python -m pytest -q tests/unit_tests/test_auto_mode.py`\n- `make -C libs/code lint`\n- `make -C libs/code type`\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"eb2b37b4f737c9616e4c36f87221df0633d10892","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/eb2b37b4f737c9616e4c36f87221df0633d10892"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4330534d18cbf79260842dde0e0c450312ef55ca","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX5HBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANyUQAE123QlNLQXfJ9cFPQk/sCQB\ngvG8iOHDRVHqEhgnns9sWOC+6uHz8rzZgxpObjM2TRMD5JhZUM1TJC8ugbadkQBX\nYU5fKQafe2rFiv9gXH3C0WsVA0zXbH83GYFN8KlqN1BgeStCCp6bpl9W1Sl/f2nu\n3GrS6EfREOzrUmfk/o8vMr5AuCvYEKYQ2F/FP49erWdBf3JIuoQyp/pegu6/l1xd\n6DbB7quxvutoHcdawNeYCwFgvLxaBxX7jx5i4fooaDQzMbFNcldVTlnEDG06gQya\niad/wHWBtT5RX/X6+0o4oby1o+pVIL4zZiUZs8q7Pfn3bfQH+jues5iI3Gp//ZXK\n3eMIdF2c9iws4OGf4cMO1HMnNvPFd6qc9HyyhtIHVZFixSSGKuI8RFeOBmMqyhmF\nyPRcnJqNYHss3CAm4Vnm8Ogflvez9w78j+FJkKtTFepIT/fdMq2tPhly5JbUxWHu\n8wV9XKPV92SBnp1vUwmHKoZ3aUkWmZMZXoT2gNhuyLlz2qxwKEQ+GNb65tFeiYdI\nGgfP1sLbtsv3m1mGffH759RyM0PK+LW64raCN25b0/3TUVjebmlXHBdS86JBZw2O\nx4XDfGrGyUPupuUbWs44zoM3KWXg7B+XMCeG1gjGA0QEZL+ZYjogdKYtsCLDfFyC\nm+zsO3TLq3myGPFGYn48\n=rAAP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree eb2b37b4f737c9616e4c36f87221df0633d10892\nparent 67bcb564ffda6bdaf1165c888d17207b0372f840\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784648129 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784648129 -0400\n\nfix(code): allow safe OS-temp scratch artifacts (#4869)\n\nRelated #4860\n\nAuto mode can now use a uniquely allocated OS temporary text file when a\ncommand requires file-based input, then remove that exact artifact\nwithout asking separately. Predictable or pre-existing temp paths and\nall other outside-worktree writes remain denied.\n\n---\n\ndcode owns the scratch lifecycle: the model supplies content and an\noptional suffix, while dcode chooses and exclusively creates the path. A\nsuccessful allocation records private provenance scoped to the current\nthread and user turn. Only the exact same file identity can be removed;\nfailed calls, prior proposals, other turns, parent directories, and\ngeneric file tools receive no authority.\n\nThe classifier may use this provenance only to establish what the\nartifact is. Literal user text remains the sole source of consent for\nthe action that consumes it or any destination it affects.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `python -m pytest -q tests/unit_tests/test_auto_mode.py`\n- `make -C libs/code lint`\n- `make -C libs/code type`\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T15:35:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4330534d18cbf79260842dde0e0c450312ef55ca","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4330534d18cbf79260842dde0e0c450312ef55ca","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4330534d18cbf79260842dde0e0c450312ef55ca/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"67bcb564ffda6bdaf1165c888d17207b0372f840","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/67bcb564ffda6bdaf1165c888d17207b0372f840","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/67bcb564ffda6bdaf1165c888d17207b0372f840"}]},{"sha":"67bcb564ffda6bdaf1165c888d17207b0372f840","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY3YmNiNTY0ZmZkYTZiZGFmMTE2NWM4ODhkMTcyMDdiMDM3MmY4NDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-21T15:25:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T15:25:29Z"},"message":"refactor(code): share newline affordances across input surfaces (#4852)\n\nFixes the newline-entry inconsistencies across dcode's text-entry\nsurfaces, and refactors so any future surface inherits the affordances.\n\nThree gaps came out of a comparison with Codex and opencode:\n\n- The goal-criteria editor advertised a hardcoded \"Shift+Enter newline\"\nin its footer. On terminals that cannot report Shift+Enter (e.g. macOS\nTerminal.app) that chord submits, so the hint pointed at the wrong key.\n- The VSCode `backslash+enter`→newline fallback (for terminals that\nemulate Shift+Enter that way) lived only in the chat input, so\nShift+Enter submitted with a stray backslash in the goal editor and the\n`ask_user` free-text prompt.\n- The `ask_user` free-text prompt never told users how to insert a\nnewline at all.\n\nRather than patch each surface, the shared newline affordances now live\nin the common `PasteBurstTextArea` base: the modifier-Enter / Ctrl+J\nbindings, the derived newline-key set, and the backslash+enter fallback\n(via small `_consume_backslash_enter_newline` /\n`_track_backslash_pending` / `_consume_modifier_newline` helpers). Both\nthe chat input and the inline prompts inherit them, and any future\n`TextArea`-based input surface that extends the base gets them for free.\nA shared `newline_hint()` helper renders the terminal-aware shortcut\n(`Ctrl+J` / `Option+Enter` / `Shift+Enter`) consistently, now used by\nboth the goal editor and the `ask_user` footer.\n\nThe chat input's existing behavior — including the completion-active\ngating on the backslash path and key ordering — is preserved.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/a7bdfa65-aba1-0246-373d-5a12d84a9860)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1f2331cd344f321544d340818c6fac60c15982c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1f2331cd344f321544d340818c6fac60c15982c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/67bcb564ffda6bdaf1165c888d17207b0372f840","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX49pCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdTQQAB16C4VkUMaKbz06ZDbDrOY4\nMfq6o1cRBGPo9itAcY+sXje6HKnSqt+vZQIU41HIgfKKktHTkT6tRlM6jQ/5GRk+\n3ZqcCJfw7lLRdpbz1G8Ht61g6iOH0ycqdTRgEaft9IPWdKZuPAwAHBF4Bti/HPix\nM0IeQK8BNd2cgz3/HtS1RD38NaQA6aA7K15P/il8+CveRZtBCrbz8wJp954YnnW5\njpTXWhxmOCfOhceXygDlAFounoHGSLbfE1xBkqVN49Z2h0IhLPxkVPkOrDcAtpBP\nQ5Kg3wjEOT+ooUdziSX8GnA8zg69qoIS/eGlvTvCga2RBYEGKYdxcXsgx3MSlWU1\nopgxvWZAcx9y+TX82wIhN+nOVACzMcX6a+O4+mhS7pn/MDV2MMdiiD7Oy3bNGys9\nhLdpEHCDsYPac9oIhzovIhrEORaCk0VDWvYo/9DXkO3X2DHgVFvrK/BZrjNtz21k\nSqJEJ9Qp8RRLQ6puSUDjaBcdnQAkTKjADxLy7vM7VT8hoK1K1WH1vCXb5o1qVzf5\nPH8uxoTqacGeST3SjeTtcXHhAuYbHwtplVZOrs1du9kSIfvJezHwLwQgwzGdJo0I\nCa26+X4jmgrzmvrmaefzwAi6+XLgINDIcfj7S5uh8LfsnST0/MR0UHdbA0dcwsjJ\nJNqNxgzr3/h1J91yjpub\n=wmt4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1f2331cd344f321544d340818c6fac60c15982c4\nparent 9a5bbeb7558405054e970decfc1aef5b96a026f3\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784647529 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784647529 -0400\n\nrefactor(code): share newline affordances across input surfaces (#4852)\n\nFixes the newline-entry inconsistencies across dcode's text-entry\nsurfaces, and refactors so any future surface inherits the affordances.\n\nThree gaps came out of a comparison with Codex and opencode:\n\n- The goal-criteria editor advertised a hardcoded \"Shift+Enter newline\"\nin its footer. On terminals that cannot report Shift+Enter (e.g. macOS\nTerminal.app) that chord submits, so the hint pointed at the wrong key.\n- The VSCode `backslash+enter`→newline fallback (for terminals that\nemulate Shift+Enter that way) lived only in the chat input, so\nShift+Enter submitted with a stray backslash in the goal editor and the\n`ask_user` free-text prompt.\n- The `ask_user` free-text prompt never told users how to insert a\nnewline at all.\n\nRather than patch each surface, the shared newline affordances now live\nin the common `PasteBurstTextArea` base: the modifier-Enter / Ctrl+J\nbindings, the derived newline-key set, and the backslash+enter fallback\n(via small `_consume_backslash_enter_newline` /\n`_track_backslash_pending` / `_consume_modifier_newline` helpers). Both\nthe chat input and the inline prompts inherit them, and any future\n`TextArea`-based input surface that extends the base gets them for free.\nA shared `newline_hint()` helper renders the terminal-aware shortcut\n(`Ctrl+J` / `Option+Enter` / `Shift+Enter`) consistently, now used by\nboth the goal editor and the `ask_user` footer.\n\nThe chat input's existing behavior — including the completion-active\ngating on the backslash path and key ordering — is preserved.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/a7bdfa65-aba1-0246-373d-5a12d84a9860)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T15:25:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/67bcb564ffda6bdaf1165c888d17207b0372f840","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/67bcb564ffda6bdaf1165c888d17207b0372f840","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/67bcb564ffda6bdaf1165c888d17207b0372f840/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9a5bbeb7558405054e970decfc1aef5b96a026f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9a5bbeb7558405054e970decfc1aef5b96a026f3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9a5bbeb7558405054e970decfc1aef5b96a026f3"}]},{"sha":"9a5bbeb7558405054e970decfc1aef5b96a026f3","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDlhNWJiZWI3NTU4NDA1MDU0ZTk3MGRlY2ZjMWFlZjViOTZhMDI2ZjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-21T15:22:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T15:22:59Z"},"message":"fix(code): harden installer downloads and paths (#4871)\n\nThe install script now respects the configured uv tool binary directory,\nretries transient downloads, and avoids unsafe fallback files and broad\nownership changes. Existing installations that are current but shadowed\non `PATH` are reinstalled into the uv tool directory instead of being\nincorrectly treated as up to date.\n\n---\n\nThe installer previously assumed uv placed executables in\n`~/.local/bin`, so custom uv configuration could make version detection,\nverification, `PATH` setup, and ownership repair target the wrong files.\nA single transient PyPI or uv bootstrap failure also immediately fell\nback or failed, and predictable `/tmp` fallbacks were used when `mktemp`\nwas unavailable.\n\nThis resolves the tool bin through `uv tool dir --bin` with legacy\nfallbacks, compares executable paths by inode, preserves existing\nregular files when adding links, retries downloads three times, and\nfails closed for required temporary files. Root and MDM installs avoid\nrunning pre-existing user executables and narrow ownership changes to\npaths created by the installer.\n\nRegression tests cover custom and legacy uv bin locations, shadowed\ninstalls, root execution, retries, and secure temporary-file failures.","tree":{"sha":"7b89c6eb95790c527ea7268285722db26320d74c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7b89c6eb95790c527ea7268285722db26320d74c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9a5bbeb7558405054e970decfc1aef5b96a026f3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX47TCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANGIQAKxmK8kt+Je02EWmShKDS1CN\nOZjIveHyNW9ZNMg52fU5kvP5GDQxNMp4fchcGwpN3kczDAQEpskvLsZEUmRxLCKY\npbztjDqf7VvSr9mmooYdOI+beH6PphY1EiOLc5D939+t/rQd1Ui8eC1zndtQYZo3\nkMLuD3byDGRZG3iyf6KIexBPjNjw/fGYLBGwuls3ZSyiYqGUQPHZBpxwi3/JVhq2\ntLMZUTQXvQJ7Oe+UyHgml0JtcqPnN+vjVJs3pOJLLQujE4ScCY6NSha3Zv6KbhBP\nlRb2nTsY/doLslyxpoJyZJEXeQt8ese6QUbTG+Hr4MWBW2so7ilXWaJGXA+zjFm9\nwB2iYViDEjnB3j2YdIKH9Pvf6UQRfRzSVmFXknv/n9sYXp1YdzanoWzeiPMUzNXG\nXP47A3w+Qc3mBNNfPMKi2iZl9fHIqeVqqrhGyjMaH3iLAz2F2LckgeURidN3ny3U\nPc6WHHd0drdcn6XqwF6CsX6nXVYMjnh3t4fllS1o3O3gxx8Ldd8nkc3MeQ/6sfIX\nSgPytKURXIoum5In4gOrtcAmyGt4SgKM5zGlC5QyJdWsOsYNt+OYwPAZvKeD+/GF\n0SPy1mmBgMI+duNRGOIfzfwC1gM2crVEavYW1VPPtPNfzWqrfQJ6mA3sw4FlTIDl\nIRhsN1IGqaXR5ra/s9E3\n=pyjM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7b89c6eb95790c527ea7268285722db26320d74c\nparent a4854042e5fe9f3acf629b0646a6bf8e348ccc9a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784647379 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784647379 -0400\n\nfix(code): harden installer downloads and paths (#4871)\n\nThe install script now respects the configured uv tool binary directory,\nretries transient downloads, and avoids unsafe fallback files and broad\nownership changes. Existing installations that are current but shadowed\non `PATH` are reinstalled into the uv tool directory instead of being\nincorrectly treated as up to date.\n\n---\n\nThe installer previously assumed uv placed executables in\n`~/.local/bin`, so custom uv configuration could make version detection,\nverification, `PATH` setup, and ownership repair target the wrong files.\nA single transient PyPI or uv bootstrap failure also immediately fell\nback or failed, and predictable `/tmp` fallbacks were used when `mktemp`\nwas unavailable.\n\nThis resolves the tool bin through `uv tool dir --bin` with legacy\nfallbacks, compares executable paths by inode, preserves existing\nregular files when adding links, retries downloads three times, and\nfails closed for required temporary files. Root and MDM installs avoid\nrunning pre-existing user executables and narrow ownership changes to\npaths created by the installer.\n\nRegression tests cover custom and legacy uv bin locations, shadowed\ninstalls, root execution, retries, and secure temporary-file failures.","verified_at":"2026-07-21T15:22:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9a5bbeb7558405054e970decfc1aef5b96a026f3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9a5bbeb7558405054e970decfc1aef5b96a026f3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9a5bbeb7558405054e970decfc1aef5b96a026f3/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a4854042e5fe9f3acf629b0646a6bf8e348ccc9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a4854042e5fe9f3acf629b0646a6bf8e348ccc9a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a4854042e5fe9f3acf629b0646a6bf8e348ccc9a"}]},{"sha":"a4854042e5fe9f3acf629b0646a6bf8e348ccc9a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGE0ODU0MDQyZTVmZTlmM2FjZjYyOWIwNjQ2YTZiZjhlMzQ4Y2NjOWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-21T15:02:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T15:02:55Z"},"message":"feat(code): gate debug console click-to-copy behind a checkbox (#4810)\n\nThe `Ctrl+\\` debug console now only copies a log line or snapshot value\non click when a new \"Click to copy\" checkbox is checked, and that choice\nis remembered across restarts. The checkbox defaults to off, so clicks\nno longer clobber the clipboard while scrolling or selecting text.\nKeyboard Enter-to-copy for the selected log line stays always on.\n\n---\n\nPreviously every click in the console (a log line, or a copyable\nsnapshot value such as the thread ID) copied to the clipboard, which was\neasy to trigger accidentally. This puts that behavior behind an opt-in\ntoolbar checkbox while preserving the primary keyboard copy path.\nSnapshot `(langsmith)` links still open on click regardless of the\ntoggle, and the checkbox is reachable via the existing Tab focus cycle.\n\nThe preference is persisted to `[ui].debug_console_click_to_copy` in\n`~/.deepagents/config.toml` (mirroring the `[ui].show_scrollbar`\npattern), with a `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG_CONSOLE_CLICK_TO_COPY` env\noverride and a matching config-manifest entry so `dcode config` can\nintrospect it. The config write runs off the UI thread and degrades to a\ntoast on failure.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/349c457d-f7ec-252c-cdc3-54fa375ad517)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d1dd02e7dd4a4b1e8af7ec5bad42645ac5f331a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d1dd02e7dd4a4b1e8af7ec5bad42645ac5f331a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a4854042e5fe9f3acf629b0646a6bf8e348ccc9a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX4ofCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXkUQAGEINclUHwNQ8EkFTFsS3Rnr\nGdmoPn8uuRUyY+4uDE78Dwi8g0rxhEocdIQ4nmeaNLCUsQ3dkwFvuAttVGPHUFxB\n648J5tOj1dCJ6+4a92M6bwcp/0B92Pwxea4HVxL3XKx8xAFqZYCStwYCgpGwgO/E\neXIEp7FSvnkbf4oVBGaLuE9pOW1fj4OPjg+Tg9fz+sLRsIGVkVaP4k0a+Jqi7tHr\nsT9LTu44E+CnWcJP2ez2V2UtKoFeDaeAtw0Zeu8/bUEoDzIc7Yq4etBHSwt7tqUk\nenFMcJsGVg03orGmzQR9i9UAUp+wuJPWclvzpIpGaQfzIZjcTd16sA6ROhg+XK+0\nJ/uWdLQnPlaB3K1LJxqybUd8nKnWIP6ZSSGG2vp8GkibX749egU5aiKmhZ/aJR7X\ndwrxTOSgnqsd8/Nboc35tyjCVpldnbixjcd/EddmDBBvipaMWXYI1u+04BBEBImW\np35zalxVPzBFR2s6LPltFm5C06exgwNvt8eqizHGAkXhG2Xzdyn9b0b9bnr+UyWk\nzfuO8fxGSRhsoNQU/W3U6mmlUogOnAz0FgqBs5g0S68XksevZD5WvQuVF8N0CCjE\nJmUFntNAUXFJuSjR4qKsrdZf5yzlOLHNexJoh5+ZqRYNk5MMbddY+7g9SNZh5NHx\nW8UaX3YniqJnobUb+ZP7\n=KxE+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d1dd02e7dd4a4b1e8af7ec5bad42645ac5f331a8\nparent 7a9b27242c4a16f210a0ef85a7f7b23a918c0462\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784646175 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784646175 -0400\n\nfeat(code): gate debug console click-to-copy behind a checkbox (#4810)\n\nThe `Ctrl+\\` debug console now only copies a log line or snapshot value\non click when a new \"Click to copy\" checkbox is checked, and that choice\nis remembered across restarts. The checkbox defaults to off, so clicks\nno longer clobber the clipboard while scrolling or selecting text.\nKeyboard Enter-to-copy for the selected log line stays always on.\n\n---\n\nPreviously every click in the console (a log line, or a copyable\nsnapshot value such as the thread ID) copied to the clipboard, which was\neasy to trigger accidentally. This puts that behavior behind an opt-in\ntoolbar checkbox while preserving the primary keyboard copy path.\nSnapshot `(langsmith)` links still open on click regardless of the\ntoggle, and the checkbox is reachable via the existing Tab focus cycle.\n\nThe preference is persisted to `[ui].debug_console_click_to_copy` in\n`~/.deepagents/config.toml` (mirroring the `[ui].show_scrollbar`\npattern), with a `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG_CONSOLE_CLICK_TO_COPY` env\noverride and a matching config-manifest entry so `dcode config` can\nintrospect it. The config write runs off the UI thread and degrades to a\ntoast on failure.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/349c457d-f7ec-252c-cdc3-54fa375ad517)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T15:02:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a4854042e5fe9f3acf629b0646a6bf8e348ccc9a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a4854042e5fe9f3acf629b0646a6bf8e348ccc9a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a4854042e5fe9f3acf629b0646a6bf8e348ccc9a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7a9b27242c4a16f210a0ef85a7f7b23a918c0462","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7a9b27242c4a16f210a0ef85a7f7b23a918c0462","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7a9b27242c4a16f210a0ef85a7f7b23a918c0462"}]},{"sha":"7a9b27242c4a16f210a0ef85a7f7b23a918c0462","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDdhOWIyNzI0MmM0YTE2ZjIxMGEwZWY4NWE3ZjdiMjNhOTE4YzA0NjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-21T14:59:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T14:59:43Z"},"message":"style(code): dim the `/plugins` modal backdrop (#4851)\n\nThe `/plugins` modal now dims the background behind it, consistent with\nother modals.\n\n---\n\nThe `/plugins` (`PluginManagerScreen`) modal overrode Textual's default\n`ModalScreen` backdrop with `background: transparent`, making it fully\nsee-through instead of dimming the content behind it like every other\nmodal. Removing the override lets it inherit the standard `background:\n$background 60%` dim backdrop (which still degrades to transparent under\nansi themes).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/8d011f9e-b11e-7cc1-e8a6-6138c7381983)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"31aaeb185be194a1d7a4ecebad3b06c5c498f325","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/31aaeb185be194a1d7a4ecebad3b06c5c498f325"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7a9b27242c4a16f210a0ef85a7f7b23a918c0462","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX4lfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqlkQAACtDV96PKJoNhHsk77MOhop\nno2VTijPpzty7i/DAxba6J1ciCZFGcBHZ2eEoqoiiIZVnz4BeXr37u4sa+xCc2Ll\nSc+80tcMuPLBSI0P7XcO2TG+AGGFtsiah3+Ud1wCGPj/C2Kpl5KG5PIPuLFwFH6A\n6a0LTA0vQ84rzFH6l6VxWYzkuuERxCQS3xZD+BLfTWMJa6b6ZaBeAgLDPPytHrVD\ntrD/Xouai7RTD/CSTjiSFBEb7cIqY8Iu8vU7rRgE7hmZ3Veago1TPqEuZIdcqt9G\nJv0rIznU4zitZNNzkpC8SCOb4KFBcPZvqQMVapSVJKtb/e08cx7GePD3qwlfs7Gx\nKLUwWaJxAcU8N/jhkRBE4/eRPQrT/iIIwb75DVRNkZ3DB7LIHRqZvNehFXpefpun\nOoTogh0buO0afu5RxnG0PmAEvc9dRc37GnnvhAaw39JiyORxsdCMn/xSovxc6Zgz\nGha21NjUO0S5L212w5Y+9gb98a8S4RK5J4Rsyi50spNTkpTdDzqtN9ZnSV8z/7z7\nuBNSpfzt9aiUVf/wukJ3va3STNDIKpVQMDWWGF2ZHe9L4cJiXvHk0eKoHQv9MgId\n0Xb+5/4eCZX4uSfB60sqDBEIdcMe+ByrJVbXlcgwQHP9Guj+K8G8KZYppX3Sw7Ea\n7Yf7MmHWhPulEhTj02/k\n=i6d/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 31aaeb185be194a1d7a4ecebad3b06c5c498f325\nparent b70820724301065b7e5fcb2486faf17fa4fde53a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784645983 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784645983 -0400\n\nstyle(code): dim the `/plugins` modal backdrop (#4851)\n\nThe `/plugins` modal now dims the background behind it, consistent with\nother modals.\n\n---\n\nThe `/plugins` (`PluginManagerScreen`) modal overrode Textual's default\n`ModalScreen` backdrop with `background: transparent`, making it fully\nsee-through instead of dimming the content behind it like every other\nmodal. Removing the override lets it inherit the standard `background:\n$background 60%` dim backdrop (which still degrades to transparent under\nansi themes).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/8d011f9e-b11e-7cc1-e8a6-6138c7381983)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T14:59:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7a9b27242c4a16f210a0ef85a7f7b23a918c0462","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7a9b27242c4a16f210a0ef85a7f7b23a918c0462","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7a9b27242c4a16f210a0ef85a7f7b23a918c0462/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b70820724301065b7e5fcb2486faf17fa4fde53a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b70820724301065b7e5fcb2486faf17fa4fde53a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b70820724301065b7e5fcb2486faf17fa4fde53a"}]},{"sha":"b70820724301065b7e5fcb2486faf17fa4fde53a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGI3MDgyMDcyNDMwMTA2NWI3ZTVmY2IyNDg2ZmFmMTdmYTRmZGU1M2E","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-21T14:39:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T14:39:12Z"},"message":"chore(deps-dev): bump pillow from 12.2.0 to 12.3.0 in /libs/evals (#4876)\n\nBumps [pillow](https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow) from 12.2.0 to\n12.3.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/releases\">pillow's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>12.3.0</h2>\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/releasenotes/12.3.0.html\">https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/releasenotes/12.3.0.html</a></p>\n<h2>Removals</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Remove non-image ImageCms modes <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9697\">#9697</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Documentation</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add release notes for SBOM and performance improvements <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9747\">#9747</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Add security release notes <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9741\">#9741</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Add release notes for Python 3.15 beta wheels <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9696\">#9696</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n<li>ImageFont can also be used with ImageText <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9597\">#9597</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Additional guidelines for security reports <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9659\">#9659</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/wiredfool\"><code>@​wiredfool</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Fixed typo <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9636\">#9636</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Added CVEs to 12.2.0 release notes <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9591\">#9591</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Revise development support information in README <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9583\">#9583</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aclark4life\"><code>@​aclark4life</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Add INCIDENT_RESPONSE.md <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9555\">#9555</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aclark4life\"><code>@​aclark4life</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Add STRIDE threat model to security docs <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9562\">#9562</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aclark4life\"><code>@​aclark4life</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Add CVEs to 12.2.0 release notes <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9556\">#9556</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Update README with revised security policy <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9553\">#9553</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Update security policy <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9552\">#9552</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aclark4life\"><code>@​aclark4life</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Update macOS tested Python versions <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9534\">#9534</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Dependencies</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update dependency harfbuzz to v14.2.1 <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9720\">#9720</a>\n[@<a href=\"https://github.com/apps/renovate\">renovate[bot]</a>]</li>\n<li>Update dependency mypy to v2 <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9653\">#9653</a>\n[@<a href=\"https://github.com/apps/renovate\">renovate[bot]</a>]</li>\n<li>Update dependency cibuildwheel to v4 <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9665\">#9665</a>\n[@<a href=\"https://github.com/apps/renovate\">renovate[bot]</a>]</li>\n<li>Update github-actions <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9655\">#9655</a>\n[@<a href=\"https://github.com/apps/renovate\">renovate[bot]</a>]</li>\n<li>Update dependency libavif to v1.4.2 <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9652\">#9652</a>\n[@<a href=\"https://github.com/apps/renovate\">renovate[bot]</a>]</li>\n<li>Update dependency lcms2 to v2.19.1 <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9651\">#9651</a>\n[@<a href=\"https://github.com/apps/renovate\">renovate[bot]</a>]</li>\n<li>Update dependency check-jsonschema to v0.37.2 <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9650\">#9650</a>\n[@<a href=\"https://github.com/apps/renovate\">renovate[bot]</a>]</li>\n<li>Update google/oss-fuzz digest to d872252 <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9614\">#9614</a>\n[@<a href=\"https://github.com/apps/renovate\">renovate[bot]</a>]</li>\n<li>Update dependency lcms2 to v2.19 <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9609\">#9609</a>\n[@<a href=\"https://github.com/apps/renovate\">renovate[bot]</a>]</li>\n<li>Update dependency libpng to v1.6.58 - autoclosed <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9608\">#9608</a>\n[@<a href=\"https://github.com/apps/renovate\">renovate[bot]</a>]</li>\n<li>Update dependency harfbuzz to v14 <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9610\">#9610</a>\n[@<a href=\"https://github.com/apps/renovate\">renovate[bot]</a>]</li>\n<li>Update dependency mypy to v1.20.2 <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9599\">#9599</a>\n[@<a href=\"https://github.com/apps/renovate\">renovate[bot]</a>]</li>\n<li>Update github-actions <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9611\">#9611</a>\n[@<a href=\"https://github.com/apps/renovate\">renovate[bot]</a>]</li>\n<li>Update dependency cibuildwheel to v3.4.1 <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9607\">#9607</a>\n[@<a href=\"https://github.com/apps/renovate\">renovate[bot]</a>]</li>\n<li>Move dependency versions to single JSON and enable Renovate <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9559\">#9559</a>\n[<a href=\"https://github.com/hugovk\"><code>@​hugovk</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Updated raqm to 0.10.5 <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9557\">#9557</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Update dependency cibuildwheel to v3.4.0 <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9532\">#9532</a>\n[@<a href=\"https://github.com/apps/renovate\">renovate[bot]</a>]</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Testing</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Remove matrix.os from benchmark <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9735\">#9735</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Remove references to libavif patch <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9734\">#9734</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Add benchmark tests <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9654\">#9654</a>\n[<a href=\"https://github.com/akx\"><code>@​akx</code></a>]</li>\n<li>Use reshape() instead of setting NumPy array shape directly <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9728\">#9728</a>\n[<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/radarhere\"><code>@​radarhere</code></a>]</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/bb1d8e8ab8d29048624d96e3ee53cecf7c13d13d\"><code>bb1d8e8</code></a>\n12.3.0 version bump</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/e63fc481dc2e07e21d5403deafb8f1ed98a513af\"><code>e63fc48</code></a>\nAdd release notes for SBOM and performance improvements (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9747\">#9747</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/13b701bbab291eec4bc87ea17ba06c94e5fe3054\"><code>13b701b</code></a>\nAdd release notes for <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9679\">#9679</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/5564ca72fcd59d040e270af5dcf17a0d7161c364\"><code>5564ca7</code></a>\nList methods</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/a0920fd384f800b5d0ba3dd29ecdeae4f1d4043b\"><code>a0920fd</code></a>\nSpeed up ImageChops operations (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9738\">#9738</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/07e9a6cd5336dc6cf8cae9165cd70cdd2b3e42fc\"><code>07e9a6c</code></a>\nSpeed up <code>Image.filter()</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9736\">#9736</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/a94578cf9649ea13e426cf7fb2b71b39ffc0dd50\"><code>a94578c</code></a>\nSpeed up <code>Image.getchannel()</code>, <code>Image.merge()</code>,\n<code>Image.putalpha()</code> and `Image...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/53e02c43c919d149b2a154a5180079f9df18fbbb\"><code>53e02c4</code></a>\nSpeed up <code>Image.fill()</code>, <code>Image.linear_gradient()</code>\nand `Image.radial_gradient...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/af037475be8634ba739744243164ba9e2c8346a6\"><code>af03747</code></a>\nSpeed up <code>Image.resample()</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9739\">#9739</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/5c9ca56c3e5fba52b647809fbb0986c87e73a571\"><code>5c9ca56</code></a>\nSpeed up <code>alpha_composite</code>, <code>matrix</code>,\n<code>negative</code>, <code>quantize</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/9740\">#9740</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/compare/12.2.0...12.3.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=pillow&package-manager=uv&previous-version=12.2.0&new-version=12.3.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"fa9d8f53821c1b70cfa0079a32856827ddd8b539","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/fa9d8f53821c1b70cfa0079a32856827ddd8b539"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b70820724301065b7e5fcb2486faf17fa4fde53a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX4SQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxMYQAKAPWm0KICoAuiZuvRVvz+1z\nBrrKgtlNSMigsrRdT/8G2pPSH84F+FrvKJ+NI2lVT02YJIBvdjJG3+AkifCOq1N1\nFanD7Lsvag2pp1ZYwaLSL0tPTjhZ836mJFOqovRM35ZqQ+D2bwVgeLeFQY0WEuRG\n/yWhK+WdvBu9KoZeOwavcOKQxvFh9kfEuu6yN06ksll25Of5LQaPEJ5Cr86+jg8N\nL+AKCB5jUHPFuNnpus08NSXHJsnyC+HKJE