":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhlODgzNTY5M2ZjOTY4YjAyNzk4OWQyZDk0NTFiODQ4YzJhNzhjNDY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Brace Sproul","email":"braceasproul@gmail.com","date":"2026-07-20T23:58:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-20T23:58:55Z"},"message":"feat(repo): openwiki (#4853)\n\nAdds OpenWiki to the repo: an auto-generated, in-tree code wiki that\ncoding agents — and humans — can read for grounded context before\nworking in the monorepo.\n\n<img width=\"885\" height=\"666\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-20 at 9 34 34 AM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c51f488b-58e8-4377-93f8-11a4e9c955c7\"\n/>\n\n---\n\n**What it is:** OpenWiki reads the codebase and git history to generate\nconcise, navigable reference pages — a quickstart, architecture\noverview, key workflows, and operations/testing notes — that live in the\nrepo under `openwiki/`.\n\n**Why:** Gives coding agents reliable, repo-grounded documentation to\nconsult on each task instead of re-discovering structure and conventions\nfrom scratch, which improves their accuracy when working here.\n\n**What it adds:**\n\n- `openwiki/` — the generated wiki (quickstart, architecture, workflows,\nengineering ops/testing), with `openwiki/quickstart.md` as the entry\npoint.\n- A scheduled `OpenWiki Update` GitHub Actions workflow that regenerates\nthe wiki daily and opens a PR with the refresh, so the docs stay current\nautomatically.\n- An `AGENTS.md` pointer directing agents to start from\n`openwiki/quickstart.md` and to avoid hand-editing generated pages\n(update source code/docs and let OpenWiki regenerate).","tree":{"sha":"323474e0c910c2590668c7e9b135159bd94f55fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/323474e0c910c2590668c7e9b135159bd94f55fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8e8835693fc968b027989d2d9451b848c2a78c46","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXrY/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsGcQADL20hpnTEtY4WQtJVnXzlf1\nUT3wz4FuaJQFBF1nHbzgXvU3MjCz6a/wdgPwU1aY/MTiK4kM5O6tUKRtapl+NKCI\nv5GP4PwMD5MJTAWy6rzx5LJ81vpasUfCVZ46NKSQKxNavuaqRbXGLXbQNSlvXcqJ\nMmf2h+s+Tcpn8qIQe6ZTVyFRMruK676c0mYOnx4Crd5x65ijj4t9Uwq6CDvZXuGz\nX3/2cDIGaVloYh8L0pQ+JWmd73K3arf2RYy7VCSjKQKB/kdMS8xqMbc/zRJQ9YUj\nyT7+RdVQ0aIfR6R98JiWfq7eS8/83+ZGaABrHu7+R03k2h2lCXne8TFikHlk7urB\ndR4Yyh2btuLcAP4rQNKzFxkGUUllbnk5DiwfOq3Ym3VqfXMxoKCAXlG3xng1J033\nYQ9rc0tjLP2ZpPYIO49QBjfUgagh4/8kTDK97QmPIbT1bigoZ2TxK2gggFkALkrs\nLe+LiF0kLW0J6vzSX8w81NQ6HokrFDaxLiMEfjTwZ3n5MKpx0nza93vsSBn0qHr2\nwrU54r4S4VLep3VmUKMCgt41j7nCpps5FYvOJzXQ/Zx58MtfXmPbQ+ShyyiYkiYz\nN4210Pqsmi+pWWBhUzygYKBeeu6zjXkYY0Y1VawTYhmJDIacGoBVB/934MSWvmbR\nQ1nKc0GpnjgrqnbQE8/L\n=g7wx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 323474e0c910c2590668c7e9b135159bd94f55fa\nparent c224a238e69de7b7c6e43713170987e46e1776e7\nauthor Brace Sproul <braceasproul@gmail.com> 1784591935 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784591935 -0700\n\nfeat(repo): openwiki (#4853)\n\nAdds OpenWiki to the repo: an auto-generated, in-tree code wiki that\ncoding agents — and humans — can read for grounded context before\nworking in the monorepo.\n\n<img width=\"885\" height=\"666\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-20 at 9 34 34 AM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c51f488b-58e8-4377-93f8-11a4e9c955c7\"\n/>\n\n---\n\n**What it is:** OpenWiki reads the codebase and git history to generate\nconcise, navigable reference pages — a quickstart, architecture\noverview, key workflows, and operations/testing notes — that live in the\nrepo under `openwiki/`.\n\n**Why:** Gives coding agents reliable, repo-grounded documentation to\nconsult on each task instead of re-discovering structure and conventions\nfrom scratch, which improves their accuracy when working here.\n\n**What it adds:**\n\n- `openwiki/` — the generated wiki (quickstart, architecture, workflows,\nengineering ops/testing), with `openwiki/quickstart.md` as the entry\npoint.\n- A scheduled `OpenWiki Update` GitHub Actions workflow that regenerates\nthe wiki daily and opens a PR with the refresh, so the docs stay current\nautomatically.\n- An `AGENTS.md` pointer directing agents to start from\n`openwiki/quickstart.md` and to avoid hand-editing generated pages\n(update source code/docs and let OpenWiki regenerate).","verified_at":"2026-07-20T23:58:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8e8835693fc968b027989d2d9451b848c2a78c46","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8e8835693fc968b027989d2d9451b848c2a78c46","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8e8835693fc968b027989d2d9451b848c2a78c46/comments","author":{"login":"bracesproul","id":46789226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2Nzg5MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46789226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracesproul","html_url":"https://github.com/bracesproul","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracesproul/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracesproul/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracesproul/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracesproul/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracesproul/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracesproul/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracesproul/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracesproul/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bracesproul/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c224a238e69de7b7c6e43713170987e46e1776e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c224a238e69de7b7c6e43713170987e46e1776e7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c224a238e69de7b7c6e43713170987e46e1776e7"}]},{"sha":"c224a238e69de7b7c6e43713170987e46e1776e7","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGMyMjRhMjM4ZTY5ZGU3YjdjNmU0MzcxMzE3MDk4N2U0NmUxNzc2ZTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-20T20:12:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-20T20:12:15Z"},"message":"ci(infra): link release summaries to PRs (#4866)\n\nPackage release run summaries now include a direct link to the pull\nrequest associated with the exact release SHA. Runs without an\nassociated PR continue normally, and a failed GitHub lookup does not\nblock a release.\n\n---\n\nThe package release workflow is dispatched separately from the release\nPR, so GitHub does not provide pull-request event context in the publish\nrun. Resolve the merged PR from the validated release commit instead and\nadd it to the existing release-target table.\n\nThe lookup uses read-only pull-request permission and remains\nbest-effort so manual and prerelease workflows retain their existing\nbehavior.","tree":{"sha":"cc8c29cc9dae772a54cdddbb8133d175588ecdef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/cc8c29cc9dae772a54cdddbb8133d175588ecdef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c224a238e69de7b7c6e43713170987e46e1776e7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXoEfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIgYQAKC11i9fo6RF6yT3hyq9x9kR\n4nWaK0jp8qANI4qDIQPWpiKf3Mmlb5r+4GWe2yqBL8mrtfSr2uCv1bly9EqYs96n\nLKK97rmxwSMXGeb5HzHMz0MZMolMqk7Ts71I+Pjnc1bAQJfxlMPccHEumegMKt4l\nJZuKvjNrk5gzklo1HFCIQ8qi8LhZPAnOhaIskEjZs/7o3WhAmQ7MijzdJh2NB2G9\n90opeznT1VArJvxo7HRZC7LjdXJeJBQgQGFoC3V0jhMjCZ/e4Pqe5qtCxlDYfuso\nST7iRXzFsZSLTEFD5+ojDYWyvfwqTG+1jW74ifeCV0YYQ1sTwRHzGkr/CJ/HNj77\napfSOhbinGutbev2mlLI2wzr6lT0EEjAvkILmwKtznp1X9PwzS6W8D/MJ4im6TXH\neoq+vcymWXLx+NXW0QUpaU5XOdT4HQQYuTjF13X54RHZr5CAteKsbioqF1U7OGkG\njdlivXgV/PANUxrNa28jfhCkLngc7G25loRzr8opozrJjxFHgJFqphLKgCq7vNhi\nJiPgGPLK+1RQqr5HToVmkAaIDWVFIxuBzK3z1E3F3FLglttgZC4xaV6odXnblbet\nME851+t1vldoNguwJgbP/qf+FNq9Fui+RHcSOuqbsA8daV2R13hNqebcpPBqyQDH\n26DqusM51mapEXyR8Dke\n=Ugaq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cc8c29cc9dae772a54cdddbb8133d175588ecdef\nparent f49337595aabd72246249f9bcf50798e0ad15d14\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784578335 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784578335 -0400\n\nci(infra): link release summaries to PRs (#4866)\n\nPackage release run summaries now include a direct link to the pull\nrequest associated with the exact release SHA. Runs without an\nassociated PR continue normally, and a failed GitHub lookup does not\nblock a release.\n\n---\n\nThe package release workflow is dispatched separately from the release\nPR, so GitHub does not provide pull-request event context in the publish\nrun. Resolve the merged PR from the validated release commit instead and\nadd it to the existing release-target table.\n\nThe lookup uses read-only pull-request permission and remains\nbest-effort so manual and prerelease workflows retain their existing\nbehavior.","verified_at":"2026-07-20T20:12:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c224a238e69de7b7c6e43713170987e46e1776e7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c224a238e69de7b7c6e43713170987e46e1776e7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c224a238e69de7b7c6e43713170987e46e1776e7/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f49337595aabd72246249f9bcf50798e0ad15d14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f49337595aabd72246249f9bcf50798e0ad15d14","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f49337595aabd72246249f9bcf50798e0ad15d14"}]},{"sha":"f49337595aabd72246249f9bcf50798e0ad15d14","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGY0OTMzNzU5NWFhYmQ3MjI0NjI0OWY5YmNmNTA3OThlMGFkMTVkMTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-20T20:09:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-20T20:09:46Z"},"message":"refactor(code): centralize JSON type aliases (#4868)\n\nCentralize recursive JSON aliases in a neutral module so config and\nplugin code share one definition while preserving plugin import\ncompatibility.\n\nThe aliases remain static types only; existing runtime ingress\nvalidation is unchanged.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `make -C libs/code format`\n- `make -C libs/code lint`\n- Focused JSON, hooks, model config, and MCP login tests (546 passed;\none unrelated root-permission assertion failed)\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/019f8107-bf8c-7545-9a37-299374653ddc)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f68342ee7be12cd1d523f161881c15b235c6e755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f68342ee7be12cd1d523f161881c15b235c6e755"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f49337595aabd72246249f9bcf50798e0ad15d14","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXoCKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtJsQAFGahYbS66t5gqBYam9EBtrd\nRWbJ7UXgudf8aBh2+7uVwBQ60+V2ABS7VAllZTe9bHzzk+d55r7GcPI/hm8ipfTh\nkf5gUUaA6cDsSFL1Pws/foqR9IAFxOVkTmFxY7Xsdo2FJEzClKZLI8qKkA7tehLI\nhTr+KNmH5SfdPAvw+0lx9gOE5haxQ74e3FuwLYFYEyeZ8N13Qual8jwwkvf3SdNu\nAM5Sy9sk174QJ2qWUmx3O/pCZ6DfKN8y/I7u9bq7ZQzonH/Zw2/a68ZIESbOi04X\nYGSynpVlOWlMasYxZ6FrqDFHo1DSoRreMrwfwYnpQejFx0BJAUYdQx8x/aIIjWe0\nTdAuduE2xKY7uI6bvoZ3PTBWwVkhJtiL7h9w8lvByP08lawqzqXcM8Lxf9o6i5zQ\nOcpdu7gNB5sqKEi5ayRsb5Q1kEqsWAnzmtOp2awNiuRjHtkEBBXFVV9Ns0M2Gg+s\n3LA2G5EHeTp2R4FPfd6S/JaoyYLNqw9YQ8D9QVBUjmFhtT6+aYEweTPKXILpqH5K\nQCv24oaU2KsFaOBTOd8SbYfznrZjJ2WPoK1q2vix77Q8q9O7RB73FbpXESnwHD2K\n1mW6yCkA0y1yXLM0ZOLpIosJYPCwXuPnZuqdXiuXGlcYRQ5UEEpYoiMcWn4XNUFA\njr7UW92NsLAGh9zry+eq\n=nlWf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f68342ee7be12cd1d523f161881c15b235c6e755\nparent 911fc28198e5c0c5d9bb6688998b2f2847807c3b\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1784578186 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784578186 +0000\n\nrefactor(code): centralize JSON type aliases (#4868)\n\nCentralize recursive JSON aliases in a neutral module so config and\nplugin code share one definition while preserving plugin import\ncompatibility.\n\nThe aliases remain static types only; existing runtime ingress\nvalidation is unchanged.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `make -C libs/code format`\n- `make -C libs/code lint`\n- Focused JSON, hooks, model config, and MCP login tests (546 passed;\none unrelated root-permission assertion failed)\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/019f8107-bf8c-7545-9a37-299374653ddc)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-20T20:09:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f49337595aabd72246249f9bcf50798e0ad15d14","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f49337595aabd72246249f9bcf50798e0ad15d14","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f49337595aabd72246249f9bcf50798e0ad15d14/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"911fc28198e5c0c5d9bb6688998b2f2847807c3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/911fc28198e5c0c5d9bb6688998b2f2847807c3b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/911fc28198e5c0c5d9bb6688998b2f2847807c3b"}]},{"sha":"911fc28198e5c0c5d9bb6688998b2f2847807c3b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDkxMWZjMjgxOThlNWMwYzVkOWJiNjY4ODk5OGIyZjI4NDc4MDdjM2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-20T20:09:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-20T20:09:26Z"},"message":"fix(infra): allow release-run comments (#4865)\n\nRelated #4817\n\nMerged release PRs once again receive a direct link to the package\nrelease workflow run.\n\n---\n\nRelease PR #4857 demonstrated that the dispatch and run lookup paths\nworked, but GitHub rejected the PR comment with `403 Resource not\naccessible by integration`. The `trigger-releases` token had `Issues:\nwrite` and only `PullRequests: read`; commenting on a pull request\nrequires `pull-requests: write`.\n\nThis grants that permission only to `trigger-releases`. Its existing\n`actions` and `issues` permissions, release dispatch behavior, and\nbest-effort handling for comment failures are unchanged. A workflow\nregression test locks the exact permission map.","tree":{"sha":"177a4eb9630b83a1146c389963eb0a0de448dd7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/177a4eb9630b83a1146c389963eb0a0de448dd7a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/911fc28198e5c0c5d9bb6688998b2f2847807c3b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXoB2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8RMQADM635+mXkTlXMgDZeuVH8qV\nKovAiwf+4waXN00XQKMPfX+3Iz7BF0kB1F5XMJz5M0nqKUrDMCaZxM6zsBOeyYCr\nJ2uwpho2s5nLMgzO5B/ZF6Tk9Olf6pW+hrOSae/dFsGcNnyydMoMyxCrWzUtq9gB\n0S0eKfYvv28OJY2l8CiTJUoKKBC4J+8iGKUK2IRrum6oWL6uz5T2F7BlYoiv5tDL\nAmvjpHAneFS+4Dwsnvq0kgVPOYKQP9/X8AoWOelxpX8RJfHRGJdipUkbGW0VCjEZ\nSbqbaGpZwws7KZc73CKH2EKdlUrWCKUWayvi3bDDwpbhV+YITBo5bX3h28HqsvgP\n0hhSLuUungJ0clSbRDj7r2grd5KuR4W7WULgwkUb3q3CyjL3dPrQkdLHuVZ9i4tE\nxlfZUR7exZAIDqIwNRNk7xYYP3DrpYnAbe9yVu1ZDLBsN/olP1z+0vnb3pU3gM8t\neqh/UlV8k53GThsCRryKR2DFs9O0EiQIRXi/vNQo4U8Iv3iv7U2EAfJmMNnKZNfH\nUVh0TIv2eEUILByKOje6lyBIc+04gERaan7QZ+SdFjuQ31DR33HQk/3VTCVyTuNm\nrw/O/u+aCKq/yxQE/clazQsCy6Flu3ZQzsEXtLr49UjFTVlPfg8qVdGxlHPEUWps\nuZhBMTmtoBLT58+MThFc\n=LAER\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 177a4eb9630b83a1146c389963eb0a0de448dd7a\nparent 44d9dec39b2570d16c285a8b0a99cbe1afab4f1b\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784578166 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784578166 -0400\n\nfix(infra): allow release-run comments (#4865)\n\nRelated #4817\n\nMerged release PRs once again receive a direct link to the package\nrelease workflow run.\n\n---\n\nRelease PR #4857 demonstrated that the dispatch and run lookup paths\nworked, but GitHub rejected the PR comment with `403 Resource not\naccessible by integration`. The `trigger-releases` token had `Issues:\nwrite` and only `PullRequests: read`; commenting on a pull request\nrequires `pull-requests: write`.\n\nThis grants that permission only to `trigger-releases`. Its existing\n`actions` and `issues` permissions, release dispatch behavior, and\nbest-effort handling for comment failures are unchanged. A workflow\nregression test locks the exact permission map.","verified_at":"2026-07-20T20:09:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/911fc28198e5c0c5d9bb6688998b2f2847807c3b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/911fc28198e5c0c5d9bb6688998b2f2847807c3b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/911fc28198e5c0c5d9bb6688998b2f2847807c3b/comments","author":{"lo