url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2b9cd08f0492e3e4ad4763f17deea2d80a145f42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2b9cd08f0492e3e4ad4763f17deea2d80a145f42","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2b9cd08f0492e3e4ad4763f17deea2d80a145f42"}]},{"sha":"2b9cd08f0492e3e4ad4763f17deea2d80a145f42","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDJiOWNkMDhmMDQ5MmUzZTRhZDQ3NjNmMTdkZWVhMmQ4MGExNDVmNDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-20T18:53:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-20T18:53:14Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.44 (#4857)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. The published GitHub release body is extracted from the\nmerged `CHANGELOG.md` by `release.yml`, not from this PR description._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.44](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.43...deepagents-code==0.1.44)\n(2026-07-20)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Improved approval handling by hiding the `Auto` option when it isn't\neligible and moving Auto mode path checks off the event loop.\n([#4839](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4839),\n[#4856](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4856))\n- Warmed MCP auth imports off the event loop to avoid blocking runtime\nwork. ([#4855](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4855))\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"2122ebd7bb317446ec88bcf3e7b438f9e56d580b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2122ebd7bb317446ec88bcf3e7b438f9e56d580b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2b9cd08f0492e3e4ad4763f17deea2d80a145f42","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXm6aCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALL8QADuZjcSR4uddc1HmetYo16LM\n+G6EoHfcpQ4MbcwvoJHzBGSZTNulZhmjp3fcV4oNZJTQdDmejbl/32McJOStudh+\nq6K8ApzYoA8eefnGEGmeQHz6C8Sw2aicwL/NVa8zNYAAko3imBb1FZIyAzXfEvoB\nIvSZjGTPDqCkmCEL4yD+X6+kRnjLWzYlcdvgR2qnDdcdBq3GRcL3jw92ObP2eFBR\nmSlSXoMJK+G8NUdH2HmQwkxUYMTV5RDZNQgr0OQ5ea1x0sz7jjKKM26d+RMRMBx3\n4Y0bpvzGTagngkqDo4eu0fq8JMP3KQ4Af6VUiv1Xx2snAP2weCGYVe9ojEsSBWif\ndCqMDKLei9uvq+X58XpvWCAc3Dq4y4VtaEc/8VI0EwXjcp9Y+uMsud8yEP4Hf27l\nmsmDVCfBQrfi4djTnL0yQCwZHFUQUG2U/lp/En7x1RXJZI9vw/j9JJK/wF9DfJYf\nh8JS0BHAzj28UGarq/6ErS72M7jNw2XfvaH75Y3IOEX4gJbgR1kPkjSr/+4Tr0gP\ngmyK7nkb8KroeQZxJRt/TLF0z0BZJpWfhOgJmD00FkwAqGKIgRNpqgQ1gLprc6fC\nJztC9ZRb8JPfl8tOTSx1DrkQ5b3AvWnt9u5NP0PECy72PmB6rfvbew1y+RpsPez7\nHpfQJuwx58wa64w+tATN\n=HKTk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2122ebd7bb317446ec88bcf3e7b438f9e56d580b\nparent 75d37c347556d962ff14850bdde489657c86feb4\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784573594 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784573594 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.44 (#4857)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. The published GitHub release body is extracted from the\nmerged `CHANGELOG.md` by `release.yml`, not from this PR description._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.44](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.43...deepagents-code==0.1.44)\n(2026-07-20)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Improved approval handling by hiding the `Auto` option when it isn't\neligible and moving Auto mode path checks off the event loop.\n([#4839](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4839),\n[#4856](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4856))\n- Warmed MCP auth imports off the event loop to avoid blocking runtime\nwork. ([#4855](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4855))\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-20T18:53:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2b9cd08f0492e3e4ad4763f17deea2d80a145f42","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2b9cd08f0492e3e4ad4763f17deea2d80a145f42","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2b9cd08f0492e3e4ad4763f17deea2d80a145f42/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"75d37c347556d962ff14850bdde489657c86feb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/75d37c347556d962ff14850bdde489657c86feb4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/75d37c347556d962ff14850bdde489657c86feb4"}]},{"sha":"75d37c347556d962ff14850bdde489657c86feb4","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDc1ZDM3YzM0NzU1NmQ5NjJmZjE0ODUwYmRkZTQ4OTY1N2M4NmZlYjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-20T18:39:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-20T18:39:28Z"},"message":"fix(code): warm MCP auth imports off event loop (#4855)\n\nRelated #4786\n\nWhen `dcode` starts with MCP servers enabled, it loads the code used to\nconnect to those servers. Loading the optional authentication support\nfor the first time can perform filesystem work. Previously, that work\nhappened on the async server's event loop, where blocking calls are\nrejected, so startup could fail with:\n\n    BlockingError: Blocking call to os.getcwd\n\n`dcode` now loads MCP authentication support in a worker thread before\nthe server needs it. This keeps the potentially blocking work away from\nthe event loop so the runtime no longer rejects it during startup.\n\n---\n\n#4786 addressed the immediate failure by limiting `filelock` to versions\nbefore 3.30. This follow-up hardens `dcode` against the broader problem\ninstead of relying only on one dependency version. The version limit\nremains in place for now.\n\nIf the optional authentication support cannot be loaded, the failure is\nstill reported only for an MCP server that needs it; it does not prevent\nunrelated or stdio MCP servers from loading.\n\nA startup smoke test uses the same blocking-call detector as the runtime\nto verify that first-time authentication loading happens in a worker\nthread, so CI catches regressions.","tree":{"sha":"f1f9bb54f47966fe05985d44e8537e54c5a2635f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f1f9bb54f47966fe05985d44e8537e54c5a2635f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/75d37c347556d962ff14850bdde489657c86feb4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXmtgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlJkQAAIfZcGlCsr7biZRQXBlEv6R\nOjP90TcHmE27rux40UaahjeCadGOtqgFOIwjTL3dmHzWeByhYupaLT6wG2iFf0au\nhNpbspgm6S8gxXJ8SlPO4Rozi9hrwxLH6EkxVGy74JlGVWir+aaNyFsnZ1HY8gVK\nTf3ljKCSKx06r0fK9Y2ED496YYeYCkoOVbgaUWZEtREvyc7ULYcu2ALju5VhjDB1\nPbW5+E5n72dTX9N4lEi4eyJU7ekJy6gkw1YCs2hxTlFsTMf8HW81a1DnQ9w+wzVN\nifh6wDXF20JDNOcQhcYUttqQ+NT/q1jsNk05ON8Y82t6COfJrD8Un9ONLUwapRNX\nbfybNmA7OJPLmJPzxGGfPYUnNFIVH+5GF1uTTXVwnhSB7kqs82ajOl7OLsQdWz5I\nc1rWc0Q/PO0ZKK4NQWOt/f9e6lF6B+GVWm6nMcI5aXZT9AqsK8S3AB77lA2h25Bw\noJJaR7PFb7neIKtWm8BQuq8qmaoEleuhLuDDKP+3ap1w7NWnc5hr2Gl8Im9i6oeX\n1FA0T1A5gqGd6xsaYOS/P3lCO17WiWlqOeek95MhZ3W32ojXpVd34a0lFiiuh6uO\nDp+d4BA6DHhoCk+jV2HzEVIh6EABz7N+RxrQvVnPiLaAHhsxDeSka7lQzC7C81JA\nH3qsHugFTVcrgEP19htz\n=lw9B\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f1f9bb54f47966fe05985d44e8537e54c5a2635f\nparent 752af303d50829f6e0c99026bb33e2ed27c725d9\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784572768 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784572768 -0400\n\nfix(code): warm MCP auth imports off event loop (#4855)\n\nRelated #4786\n\nWhen `dcode` starts with MCP servers enabled, it loads the code used to\nconnect to those servers. Loading the optional authentication support\nfor the first time can perform filesystem work. Previously, that work\nhappened on the async server's event loop, where blocking calls are\nrejected, so startup could fail with:\n\n    BlockingError: Blocking call to os.getcwd\n\n`dcode` now loads MCP authentication support in a worker thread before\nthe server needs it. This keeps the potentially blocking work away from\nthe event loop so the runtime no longer rejects it during startup.\n\n---\n\n#4786 addressed the immediate failure by limiting `filelock` to versions\nbefore 3.30. This follow-up hardens `dcode` against the broader problem\ninstead of relying only on one dependency version. The version limit\nremains in place for now.\n\nIf the optional authentication support cannot be loaded, the failure is\nstill reported only for an MCP server that needs it; it does not prevent\nunrelated or stdio MCP servers from loading.\n\nA startup smoke test uses the same blocking-call detector as the runtime\nto verify that first-time authentication loading happens in a worker\nthread, so CI catches regressions.","verified_at":"2026-07-20T18:39:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/75d37c347556d962ff14850bdde489657c86feb4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/75d37c347556d962ff14850bdde489657c86feb4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/75d37c347556d962ff14850bdde489657c86feb4/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"752af303d50829f6e0c99026bb33e2ed27c725d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/752af303d50829f6e0c99026bb33e2ed27c725d9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/752af303d50829f6e0c99026bb33e2ed27c725d9"}]},{"sha":"752af303d50829f6e0c99026bb33e2ed27c725d9","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDc1MmFmMzAzZDUwODI5ZjZlMGM5OTAyNmJiMzNlMmVkMjdjNzI1ZDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-20T18:39:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-20T18:39:18Z"},"message":"style(code): pad between marketplace entries in plugin manager (#4850)\n\nMarketplace entries in the plugin manager now have spacing between them,\nmatching the plugins list.\n\n---\n\nThe marketplaces tab rendered entries back-to-back, while the plugins\nlist (`_plugin_options`) inserts a disabled spacer `Option` between\nrows. This applies the same disabled-spacer pattern between marketplace\nrows so both surfaces are visually consistent. The spacers are disabled,\nso keyboard navigation still skips over them.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/045a43e2-f199-47e8-a7f0-ffb5dbff5762)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"792fa00ff6967614c135d3cd2b9b3a0f50674f54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/792fa00ff6967614c135d3cd2b9b3a0f50674f54"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/752af303d50829f6e0c99026bb33e2ed27c725d9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXmtWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgc8QAIw1oT5+Cz+hsVjHc0CCOXSP\nRwqD3JV5QYve18JW/qBIc1HkoVqDCCi0ljp8h5uvO8RoubNNWfWnXsFvQD+BOT7t\n7hbNMu32NWl8+qR69HO0qThzoD3jUfpELm2AC0qp54Z6yaRsMPEYspATQgDdXAiG\nweVyL5i0Dzcip0tlVzaIYTAarG/a5tHCV5GMR+vSujHNrP4TYahfxuTIzbn5EY9n\nercZIAA88pJlnXnVuhzgOUupmGfHc4xHsfXveYYeElpGiGWrY/9ZXMG6D+Jjc0v/\npskneYamCgXsCbPHiMpT+Z0Im6I2q2ZSPrm+uUSc0N+k+0wNpjjhglULtXwjg5nZ\n0EQQWrytOdXjAdkv57+YaHGrL/hQzoWIZig5mmpoHZaap+9MqHSPaaAdd2VnU4b9\n8yxFeo2Wqu6KH1OIOL1PqYGKBBcFUFO0XJ29FtUOqqJplufOX9w2X0J9RBV8dX6A\nSwHy0bsK279w6dWmAtnEVo2fGXsJbcvimOpilBdhVscoYUI+ANXrTsCOrMbi7IoJ\nuTwwgfvmldGsBT5AMkim/ZiC0x8t7k+enyDepznZyeko5PNxXqAmJBxX1L1MWmDn\n2sMaSQGRLvbGthaVl1ylrAYMw+YQ6IkaYiMRPAXv1cqzNoyTlOKcVwQQmJ0IE9US\nYyUh4m+M+nASmR2uDvvx\n=8YDh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 792fa00ff6967614c135d3cd2b9b3a0f50674f54\nparent acb1a0eeec60deca267282a085970445a582a5e1\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784572758 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784572758 -0400\n\nstyle(code): pad between marketplace entries in plugin manager (#4850)\n\nMarketplace entries in the plugin manager now have spacing between them,\nmatching the plugins list.\n\n---\n\nThe marketplaces tab rendered entries back-to-back, while the plugins\nlist (`_plugin_options`) inserts a disabled spacer `Option` between\nrows. This applies the same disabled-spacer pattern between marketplace\nrows so both surfaces are visually consistent. The spacers are disabled,\nso keyboard navigation still skips over them.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/045a43e2-f199-47e8-a7f0-ffb5dbff5762)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-20T18:39:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/752af303d50829f6e0c99026bb33e2ed27c725d9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/752af303d50829f6e0c99026bb33e2ed27c725d9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/752af303d50829f6e0c99026bb33e2ed27c725d9/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"acb1a0eeec60deca267282a085970445a582a5e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/acb1a0eeec60deca267282a085970445a582a5e1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/acb1a0eeec60deca267282a085970445a582a5e1"}]},{"sha":"acb1a0eeec60deca267282a085970445a582a5e1","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFjYjFhMGVlZWM2MGRlY2EyNjcyODJhMDg1OTcwNDQ1YTU4MmE1ZTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-20T18:13:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-20T18:13:40Z"},"message":"style(code): align `Auto` activation warnings (#4858)\n\nAuto mode now shows the same warning whether it is enabled at startup or\ntoggled during a session.\n\n---\n\nThe startup path used implementation-specific copy that differed from\nthe toggle path. Reuse one warning constant so both paths stay aligned\nand future edits cannot drift.","tree":{"sha"